ments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguesj-hub/reserva-canchas/commits/09148f813352acc69c49736ade627ec66ed2fea1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T06:38:43Z","email":"miguel.larasj@gmail.com","name":"Miguel Lara"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T06:38:43Z","email":"miguel.larasj@gmail.com","name":"Miguel Lara"},"message":"Revert \"docs: especifica las dos brechas\" y \"docs: planifica las dos brechas\"\n\nRevierte 195d7e7 y acac0f2. El trabajo no se descarta: se mueve a una feature\npropia, 002, en lugar de enmendar 001.\n\nEl motivo es tasks.md. Los 134 tasks de 001 están cerrados y son el registro de\nlo entregado; añadirles T135 en adelante deja los IDs fuera de orden y el archivo\nen un estado mixto que /speckit-tasks y /speckit-implement querrían regenerar.\nCada paso siguiente habría sido cirugía a mano. En 002 los dos comandos funcionan\nnativos.\n\nLa enmienda 1.3.0 de la constitución (1f7ea6a) NO se revierte: es global y vale\npara cualquiera de las dos rutas.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2a2905f4c7f9da0328ab3a954a32ff0d193da648","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguesj-hub/reserva-canchas/git/trees/2a2905f4c7f9da0328ab3a954a32ff0d193da648"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguesj-hub/reserva-canchas/git/commits/09148f813352acc69c49736ade627ec66ed2fea1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297528077?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguesj-hub/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguesj-hub/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguesj-hub/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguesj-hub/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/miguesj-hub","id":297528077,"login":"miguesj-hub","node_id":"U_kgDOEbvrDQ","organizations_url":"h