jIwMjlhM2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/miguesj-hub/reserva-canchas/commit/8b5df11e0266f571e24db65a1ec973c651bee608","sha":"8b5df11e0266f571e24db65a1ec973c651bee608","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguesj-hub/reserva-canchas/commits/8b5df11e0266f571e24db65a1ec973c651bee608"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/miguesj-hub/reserva-canchas/commit/02ec100772fe033d3b47c0d486a05984c5ea2c84","sha":"02ec100772fe033d3b47c0d486a05984c5ea2c84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguesj-hub/reserva-canchas/commits/02ec100772fe033d3b47c0d486a05984c5ea2c84"}],"sha":"14cb460b71e12893457fbb2ae8c96cff62029a3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguesj-hub/reserva-canchas/commits/14cb460b71e12893457fbb2ae8c96cff62029a3b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57201017?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AdrianEspinoza92","id":57201017,"login":"AdrianEspinoza92","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjAxMDE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguesj-hub/reserva-canchas/commits/02ec100772fe033d3b47c0d486a05984c5ea2c84/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T21:08:26Z","email":"adrian.espinoza1252@gmail.com","name":"Carlos Adrian Espinoza Alvarez"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T21:08:26Z","email":"adrian.espinoza1252@gmail.com","name":"Carlos Adrian Espinoza Alvarez"},"message":"docs: manual de despliegue (E5) y cierre de la compuerta 8\n\ndocs/MANUAL-DESPLIEGUE.md — el entregable E5, a partir del quickstart. Requisito\núnico (Docker 24 con Compose v2), arranque, qué se levanta, los cuatro usuarios\nde prueba, verificación, operación, configuración por variables de entorno y una\ntabla de problemas frecuentes con su causa.\n\nIncluye lo que costó descubrir durante el desarrollo y no está en ningún otro\nsitio: qué hacer si el puerto 8080 está ocupado, por qué un cambio de código no\nse refleja sin --build, y que cambiar las contraseñas de base con el volumen ya\ncreado deja a los servicios sin poder conectarse.\n\nCompuerta 8 — dos desfases que la revisión final encontró:\n\n- workspace.dsl no conocía el UserController. Solo tenía el AuthController, que\n  es el que quedó tras renombrarlo en la fase 2; las rutas de /api/usuarios\n  existen desde US4 y el diagrama no las mostraba. Se añade como componente\n  propio, con la relación del gateway diferenciada: /api/auth es público y\n  /api/usuarios exige ADMINISTRADOR. UserService declara ahora FR-048, como\n  CourtService declara RN-07.\n- El informe seguía diciendo que la gestión de usuarios estaba pendiente y que\n  faltaba una de las cuatro historias. Se cerró en la fase 6.\n\nLas 24 figuras se regeneran y se verifican vista por vista contra la marca que\ncada una debía traer, no solo comprobando que el archivo existe: el exportador\nllegó a producir SVG de la vista anterior sin avisar, y el arreglo de la fase 4\nmerece confirmarse cada vez.\n\nEl informe queda en 36 páginas, sin un solo marcador \\ph{} en sus diez secciones\ny sin ninguna figura ausente.\n\nspecs/: las 134 tareas quedan marcadas. Las nueve de esta fase eran de\nverificación, y tres de ellas encontraron trabajo real —el endpoint que faltaba,\nel UserController del diagrama y el informe desactualizado—, que es exactamente\npara lo que existen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VhxFpT5rG7tHhgQ3J939Z9","tree":{"sha":"76476c7a31cc25a72101af75f33b43ff4b253b07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguesj-hub/reserva-canchas/git/trees/76476c7a31cc25a72101af75f33b43ff4b253b07"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguesj-hub/reserva-canchas/git/commits/02ec100772fe033d3b47c0d486a05984c5ea2c84","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57201017?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AdrianEspinoza92","id":57201017,"login":"AdrianEspinoza92","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjAxMDE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/miguesj-hub/reserva-canchas/commit/02ec100772fe033d3b47c0d486a05984c5ea2c84","node_id":"C_kwDOT72o_toAKDAyZWMxMDA3NzJmZTAzM2QzYjQ3YzBkNDg2YTA1OTg0YzVlYTJjODQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/miguesj-hub/reserva-canchas/commit/499e40db6db6ad72a05931564370e962c295969a","sha":"499e40db6db6ad72a05931564370e962c295969a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguesj-hub/reserva-canchas/commits/499e40db6db6ad72a05931564370e962c295969a"}],"sha":"02ec100772fe033d3b47c0d486a05984c5ea2c84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguesj-hub/reserva-canchas/commits/02ec100772fe033d3b47c0d486a05984c5ea2c84"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57201017?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AdrianEspinoza92","id":57201017,"login":"AdrianEspinoza92","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjAxMDE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguesj-hub/reserva-canchas/commits/499e40db6db6ad72a05931564370e962c295969a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T21:08:08Z","email":"adrian.espinoza1252@gmail.com","name":"Carlos Adrian Espinoza Alvarez"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T21:08:08Z","email":"adrian.espinoza1252@gmail.com","name":"Carlos Adrian Espinoza Alvarez"},"message":"test: los tres contextLoads pasan de vacíos a verificar el esquema\n\nLos tres servicios con base arrastraban desde el esqueleto inicial (682dce5) el\ntest que genera Spring Initializr:\n\n    @SpringBootTest\n    class MsCanchasApplicationTests { @Test void contextLoads() { } }\n\nUn método vacío que levanta la aplicación entera. En cuanto esos proyectos\ntuvieron JPA y Flyway, arrancar el contexto pasó a exigir una conexión real a\nPostgreSQL, y en el entorno de pruebas no hay ninguna: \"Connection to\nlocalhost:5432 refused\". Fallaba desde la fase 2, se verificó entonces sobre un\nms-canchas aún sin tocar para descartar que lo hubiera roto el código nuevo, y\nse fue reportando fase a fase sin arreglarlo porque la solución toca tres\npom.xml y esa no es una decisión que quepa dentro de \"implementa US2\".\n\nAhora cada uno levanta un PostgreSQL efímero con Testcontainers, y deja de ser\nun test vacío. Lo que comprueba es que **las migraciones de Flyway y el mapeo de\nlas entidades concuerdan**: el servicio arranca con ddl-auto: validate, así que\nuna columna que diverja de su campo impide cargar el contexto y pone el test en\nrojo. Es justo el fallo que validate existe para atrapar, y que hasta ahora solo\nse descubría levantando los once contenedores.\n\nEl de ms-reservas es el más valioso: en su arranque Flyway crea la restricción\nEXCLUDE que implementa RN-02. Necesita btree_gist, que en el despliegue instala\ninfra/postgres/init/02-extensiones.sql y aquí instala un script de\ninicialización del contenedor, para no tocar las migraciones de producción.\n\nDos detalles del camino, por si vuelven a aparecer:\n\n- Testcontainers 2.x renombró sus artefactos: testcontainers-postgresql y\n  testcontainers-junit-jupiter, no postgresql ni junit-jupiter. Toda la\n  documentación que circula usa los nombres de la 1.x.\n- Las versiones no se fijan a mano: las gestiona el testcontainers-bom que\n  spring-boot-dependencies ya importa.\n\nResultado: 70 pruebas en los cinco servicios, 0 fallos, BUILD SUCCESS en todos.\nEl precio es que las pruebas de arranque necesitan acceso al demonio de Docker.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VhxFpT5rG7tHhgQ3J939Z9","tree":{"sha":"41ad0b29d8f0ad41b1b72c976116b7e28607de03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguesj-hub/reserva-canchas/git/trees/41ad0b29d8f0ad41b1b72c976116b7e28607de03"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguesj-hub/reserva-canchas/git/commits/499e40db6db6ad72a05931564370e962c295969a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57201017?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AdrianEspinoza92","id":57201017,"login":"AdrianEspinoza92","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjAxMDE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/miguesj-hub/reserva-canchas/commit/499e40db6db6ad72a05931564370e962c295969a","node_id":"C_kwDOT72o_toAKDQ5OWU0MGRiNmRiNmFkNzJhMDU5MzE1NjQzNzBlOTYyYzI5NTk2OWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/miguesj-hub/reserva-canchas/commit/8dc097da8b2cd64dc8c6057c15c08c506016277f","sha":"8dc097da8b2cd64dc8c6057c15c08c506016277f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguesj-hub/reserva-canchas/commits/8dc097da8b2cd64dc8c6057c15c08c506016277f"}],"sha":"499e40db6db6ad72a05931564370e962c295969a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguesj-hub/reserva-canchas/commits/499e40db6db6ad72a05931564370e962c295969a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57201017?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AdrianEspinoza92","id":57201017,"login":"AdrianEspinoza92","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjAxMDE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguesj-hub/reserva-canchas/commits/8dc097da8b2cd64dc8c6057c15c08c506016277f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T21:08:08Z","email":"adrian.espinoza1252@gmail.com","name":"Carlos Adrian Espinoza Alvarez"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T21:08:08Z","email":"adrian.espinoza1252@gmail.com","name":"Carlos Adrian Espinoza Alvarez"},"message":"feat(reservas): GET /api/reservas/{id}, que el contrato pedía y no existía\n\nLo destapó la compuerta 6 al comparar el Swagger publicado de cada servicio con\nsu contrato: contracts/reservas.yaml documentaba la consulta puntual de una\nreserva, con su regla y sus códigos, pero ninguna tarea la había pedido y el\nservicio no la tenía. Cuatro rutas publicadas contra cinco contratadas.\n\nSe implementa en lugar de recortar el contrato, al revés que con el denominador\nde la ocupación. La diferencia está en el coste y en la trazabilidad: aquello\nexigía un histórico de activación que ningún requisito pide, mientras que esto\nson quince líneas y la regla ya estaba escrita —RN-03 aplicada a la lectura—.\n\nUn USUARIO_FINAL solo consulta las suyas; sobre una ajena recibe 403 y no 404,\npor lo mismo que al cancelar: fingir que no existe ocultaría el motivo real y\ncomplicaría depurar. El ADMINISTRADOR consulta cualquiera.\n\nDos pruebas nuevas en BookingServiceCancelacionTest, donde ya vive el resto de\nRN-03. Verificado además contra el sistema en marcha: 200 sobre la propia, 403\nsobre la ajena, 200 para el administrador, 404 si no existe.\n\nCon esto los cuatro Swagger coinciden exactamente con contracts/.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VhxFpT5rG7tHhgQ3J939Z9","tree":{"sha":"89fa988026f9200a95d651270c137b1584f44c89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguesj-hub/reserva-canchas/git/trees/89fa988026f9200a95d651270c137b1584f44c89"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguesj-hub/reserva-canchas/git/commits/8dc097da8b2cd64dc8c6057c15c08c506016277f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57201017?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AdrianEspinoza92","id":57201017,"login":"AdrianEspinoza92","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjAxMDE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrianEspinoza92/receiv