":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/ee19f95f2f460f2ddc597aa953d7ed3f5affb4aa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T21:35:34Z","email":"github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T21:35:34Z","email":"github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"message":"chore: auto-update @wolffm/* to latest","tree":{"sha":"2e41ad9c72f90ebab4b1bab6d853e498574c4119","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/2e41ad9c72f90ebab4b1bab6d853e498574c4119"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/ee19f95f2f460f2ddc597aa953d7ed3f5affb4aa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/ee19f95f2f460f2ddc597aa953d7ed3f5affb4aa","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKGVlMTlmOTVmMmY0NjBmMmRkYzU5N2FhOTUzZDdlZDNmNWFmZmI0YWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/f415cea291a1e1bb76fa7fcb9ad1eaf7e1c635d6","sha":"f415cea291a1e1bb76fa7fcb9ad1eaf7e1c635d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/f415cea291a1e1bb76fa7fcb9ad1eaf7e1c635d6"}],"sha":"ee19f95f2f460f2ddc597aa953d7ed3f5affb4aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/ee19f95f2f460f2ddc597aa953d7ed3f5affb4aa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/f415cea291a1e1bb76fa7fcb9ad1eaf7e1c635d6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T21:23:04Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T21:23:04Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(board): send the archetypes, so a column can be named\n\nThree columns all headed \"Everything\". Grouping and NAMING come from two\ndifferent fields — `facts[].archetype` decides which column a fact is in,\n`archetypes` supplies the heading — and only the first was being sent.\n\n`toSetDetailJson` never carried `archetypes`, and `FactSchema` never declared\n`archetype`. The file export had both from the start, which is why every\nround-trip check passed and the thing the app actually renders from was the\none shape nobody looked at. schemas.test.ts calls itself \"exactly the shape\nGET /sets/{id} puts in data.set\" and it was the test that caught this the\nmoment the field became required — it just had to be asked.\n\nThe fallback is better too. A column with a name now falls back to that NAME,\ntitle-cased, because an author-chosen key beats any guess made from the\nquestions underneath it. \"Everything\" survives only for the implicit column of\na set that declares no archetypes, which genuinely is one undifferentiated\ndeck.\n\nDELETE now takes the same tier as PATCH and PUT. It was held back on the\ngrounds that an edit is recoverable from an export and a delete is not — true,\nbut it made the tier mean two different things on two verbs, and an agent that\ncan replace every fact with nothing already holds the destructive power, just\nspelled less honestly. Ownership still does not move, and taking a set is\nstill admin-only.\n\n131 worker tests, 173 UI tests, full `pnpm check` green.","tree":{"sha":"9a99b25a8362d50afa97fc861afb4fcdc9ef6749","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/9a99b25a8362d50afa97fc861afb4fcdc9ef6749"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/f415cea291a1e1bb76fa7fcb9ad1eaf7e1c635d6","verification":{"payload":"tree 9a99b25a8362d50afa97fc861afb4fcdc9ef6749\nparent 428544b697cb7a9103a31a76017fa765ef01a4f2\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788643384 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788643384 -0700\n\nfix(board): send the archetypes, so a column can be named\n\nThree columns all headed \"Everything\". Grouping and NAMING come from two\ndifferent fields — `facts[].archetype` decides which column a fact is in,\n`archetypes` supplies the heading — and only the first was being sent.\n\n`toSetDetailJson` never carried `archetypes`, and `FactSchema` never declared\n`archetype`. The file export had both from the start, which is why every\nround-trip check passed and the thing the app actually renders from was the\none shape nobody looked at. schemas.test.ts calls itself \"exactly the shape\nGET /sets/{id} puts in data.set\" and it was the test that caught this the\nmoment the field became required — it just had to be asked.\n\nThe fallback is better too. A column with a name now falls back to that NAME,\ntitle-cased, because an author-chosen key beats any guess made from the\nquestions underneath it. \"Everything\" survives only for the implicit column of\na set that declares no archetypes, which genuinely is one undifferentiated\ndeck.\n\nDELETE now takes the same tier as PATCH and PUT. It was held back on the\ngrounds that an edit is recoverable from an export and a delete is not — true,\nbut it made the tier mean two different things on two verbs, and an agent that\ncan replace every fact with nothing already holds the destructive power, just\nspelled less honestly. Ownership still does not move, and taking a set is\nstill admin-only.\n\n131 worker tests, 173 UI tests, full `pnpm check` green.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQBfZyq9mEr6eykfXly+R3lYg8AbM7NVVoHAnaF9GTrzZnbpSNC0ApGyzvLNZbO8pC5\nQvuvW7yHN24TuEgo1Tug8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-05T21:23:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/f415cea291a1e1bb76fa7fcb9ad1eaf7e1c635d6","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKGY0MTVjZWEyOTFhMWUxYmI3NmZhN2ZjYjlhZDFlYWY3ZTFjNjM1ZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/428544b697cb7a9103a31a76017fa765ef01a4f2","sha":"428544b697cb7a9103a31a76017fa765ef01a4f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/428544b697cb7a9103a31a76017fa765ef01a4f2"}],"sha":"f415cea291a1e1bb76fa7fcb9ad1eaf7e1c635d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/f415cea291a1e1bb76fa7fcb9ad1eaf7e1c635d6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/428544b697cb7a9103a31a76017fa765ef01a4f2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T23:12:40Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T23:12:40Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat(sets): service tier and above may write a set it does not own\n\nAn agent restructuring somebody''s set holds a service key and is not the\nowner, so PATCH and PUT came back 404 — indistinguishable from \"no such set\" —\nand the API was unusable for exactly the work it exists to support. The set had\nto be edited by hand or not at all.\n\nOwner, or SERVICE and above, by RANK. The ladder is\npublic < friend < service < wife < admin, so this admits every machine\ncredential and every human tier above friend, and holds an ordinary friend to\nthe sets they own — one friend still cannot touch another''s.\n\nTwo properties deliberately unchanged:\n\n  - Ownership does not move. An elevated write updates content and leaves\n    owner_user_id alone, so editing a set is not a way to take one. Taking is\n    still POST /sets/{id}/owner, still admin-only. That asymmetry is the same\n    one the transfer route already draws: you can give a set away, not take it.\n  - A friend-tier caller still gets the same 404 for someone else''s set as for\n    one that does not exist, so probing ids reveals nothing.\n\nEvery write stays attributable: setEvent records the CALLER''s userId, so an\nelevated edit reads as made by that key rather than by the owner.\n\nDELETE is NOT extended, and the asymmetry is the point: an edit is recoverable\nfrom an export, a delete takes the facts, the ratings, the attempt ledger and\nevery reader''s saved progress with it. Owner or admin, as before.\n\nA separate loader rather than a flag on loadSetForWrite — its own comment\nwarns that \"a boolean that turns an access check off is a boolean somebody\neventually passes by accident\", and this follows the shape the transfer route\nalready established for admin.\n\nmayWriteAnySet is exported so the policy is tested rather than buried in a\nloader. Mutation-tested: swapping tierAtLeast for `=== ''service''` fails the\ncase covering wife and admin — the equality bug this ecosystem has shipped\ntwice — and lowering the bar to friend fails the case that keeps one friend\nout of another''s sets.","tree":{"sha":"e69b61115716e229d81c5f649095bcdccf650ff6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/e69b61115716e229d81c5f649095bcdccf650ff6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/428544b697cb7a9103a31a76017fa765ef01a4f2","verification":{"payload":"tree e69b61115716e229d81c5f649095bcdccf650ff6\nparent 362cf506ac5587d105d6e94ad19c07d6bdc42162\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788477160 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788477160 -0700\n\nfeat(sets): service tier and above may write a set it does not own\n\nAn agent restructuring somebody''s set holds a service key and is not the\nowner, so PATCH and PUT came back 404 — indistinguishable from \"no such set\" —\nand the API was unusable for exactly the work it exists to support. The set had\nto be edited by hand or not at all.\n\nOwner, or SERVICE and above, by RANK. The ladder is\npublic < friend < service < wife < admin, so this admits every machine\ncredential and every human tier above friend, and holds an ordinary friend to\nthe sets they own — one friend still cannot touch another''s.\n\nTwo properties deliberately unchanged:\n\n  - Ownership does not move. An elevated write updates content and leaves\n    owner_user_id alone, so editing a set is not a way to take one. Taking is\n    still POST /sets/{id}/owner, still admin-only. That asymmetry is the same\n    one the transfer route already draws: you can give a set away, not take it.\n  - A friend-tier caller still gets the same 404 for someone else''s set as for\n    one that does not exist, so probing ids reveals nothing.\n\nEvery write stays attributable: setEvent records the CALLER''s userId, so an\nelevated edit reads as made by that key rather than by the owner.\n\nDELETE is NOT extended, and the asymmetry is the point: an edit is recoverable\nfrom an export, a delete takes the facts, the ratings, the attempt ledger and\nevery reader''s saved progress with it. Owner or admin, as before.\n\nA separate loader rather than a flag on loadSetForWrite — its own comment\nwarns that \"a boolean that turns an access check off is a boolean somebody\neventually passes by accident\", and this follows the shape the transfer route\nalready established for admin.\n\nmayWriteAnySet is exported so the policy is tested rather than buried in a\nloader. Mutation-tested: swapping tierAtLeast for `=== ''service''` fails the\ncase covering wife and admin — the equality bug this ecosystem has shipped\ntwice — and lowering the bar to friend fails the case that keeps one friend\nout of another''s sets.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQHPxydw/uSe6enXoZDAJTfDpEjy8NYnnQBdsT5XcXOV8gTWTtq9zs76EcqOLM+/7m2\nDcKge8G2JCuXVQksy5UwE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-03T23:12:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/428544b697cb7a9103a31a76017fa765ef01a4f2","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKDQyODU0NGI2OTdjYjdhOTEwM2EzMWE3NjAxN2ZhNzY1ZWYwMWE0ZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/362cf506ac5587d105d6e94ad19c07d6bdc42162","sha":"362cf506ac5587d105d6e94ad19c07d6bdc42162","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/362cf506ac5587d105d6e94ad19c07d6bdc42162"}],"sha":"428544b697cb7a9103a31a76017fa765ef01a4f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/428544b697cb7a9103a31a76017fa765ef01a4f2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/362cf506ac5587d105d6e94ad19c07d6bdc42162/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T01:26:42Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T01:26:42Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(ui): stop telling a reader what they just did\n\n\"You''ve answered 1 time here.\" and \"Hardest for you right now\" were commentary\nnobody asked for. A reader who has just played knows they played, and their\nhardest questions are the deck they are already looking at, reordered — the\nsame class of useless extra info as the board''s \"42 questions are not on the\nboard\", removed for the same reason.\n\nWhat is left is owner-only and is not a quip: which questions play has rated\nwell away from the tier their author chose. That disagreement is the one thing\nan author can act on, and it is not visible anywhere else — a rating alone\nmeans nothing without something to compare it against. The panel now renders\nonly for an owner, since the reader''s half was its only other reason to exist.\n\nstanding__head goes with it, and standing__sub inherits its styling: it was a\nSECOND heading under the removed one, so it carried a top margin instead of\nthe type treatment it now needs as the panel''s only heading.","tree":{"sha":"547f151bda55b34fcb6451a90620c37268e35951","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/547f151bda55b34fcb6451a90620c37268e35951"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/362cf506ac5587d105d6e94ad19c07d6bdc42162","verification":{"payload":"tree 547f151bda55b34fcb6451a90620c37268e35951\nparent d3bd7d367bef0c076c22d7ea6859775ae0228439\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788398802 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788398802 -0700\n\nfix(ui): stop telling a reader what they just did\n\n\"You''ve answered 1 time here.\" and \"Hardest for you right now\" were commentary\nnobody asked for. A reader who has just played knows they played, and their\nhardest questions are the deck they are already looking at, reordered — the\nsame class of useless extra info as the board''s \"42 questions are not on the\nboard\", removed for the same reason.\n\nWhat is left is owner-only and is not a quip: which questions play has rated\nwell away from the tier their author chose. That disagreement is the one thing\nan author can act on, and it is not visible anywhere else — a rating alone\nmeans nothing without something to compare it against. The panel now renders\nonly for an owner, since the reader''s half was its only other reason to exist.\n\nstanding__head goes with it, and standing__sub inherits its styling: it was a\nSECOND heading under the removed one, so it carried a top margin instead of\nthe type treatment it now needs as the panel''s only heading.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAA