s://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/f7c4dfafe917bce6e8bf9a073baa728bba2243b6","sha":"f7c4dfafe917bce6e8bf9a073baa728bba2243b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/f7c4dfafe917bce6e8bf9a073baa728bba2243b6"}],"sha":"b1b3f025fdb05c8e2c32b3a8f96103fe745ff12f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/b1b3f025fdb05c8e2c32b3a8f96103fe745ff12f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/f7c4dfafe917bce6e8bf9a073baa728bba2243b6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T05:30:01Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T05:30:01Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"refactor(ci): the fleet manager owns node selection\n\n    - ${{ fromJSON(vars.CI_RUNNER || ''[\"self-hosted\",\"hadoku-builder\"]'') }}\n    + ${{ fromJSON(vars.CI_RUNNER) }}\n\nThat fallback was fleet internals pasted into every workflow: the label the\ntier monitor owns, the variable''s name, and the semantics of unset. Fleet-wide\nit was 107 workflows across 27 repos, so @wolffm/fleet-manager could not change\nhow it is addressed without editing the whole ecosystem.\n\nSafe because CI_RUNNER is already set here. fleet-manager 0.5.0 writes the\nfleet target to every covered repo instead of deleting the variable, and it is\nPERSISTENT repo state — if the fleet manager stops, the last value stays and CI\nkeeps scheduling.\n\nWhere a job carries the fork-PR author_association guard, only the trailing\nfleet fallback is removed; the guard that sends untrusted PRs to hosted runners\nis untouched.","tree":{"sha":"d4207ccb884275c13b4c0b3354aa887c3c313b2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/d4207ccb884275c13b4c0b3354aa887c3c313b2b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/f7c4dfafe917bce6e8bf9a073baa728bba2243b6","verification":{"payload":"tree d4207ccb884275c13b4c0b3354aa887c3c313b2b\nparent 68d9cb7563c1bd7c46ff7ed705d67f992ea4fb26\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788067801 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788067801 -0700\n\nrefactor(ci): the fleet manager owns node selection\n\n    - ${{ fromJSON(vars.CI_RUNNER || ''[\"self-hosted\",\"hadoku-builder\"]'') }}\n    + ${{ fromJSON(vars.CI_RUNNER) }}\n\nThat fallback was fleet internals pasted into every workflow: the label the\ntier monitor owns, the variable''s name, and the semantics of unset. Fleet-wide\nit was 107 workflows across 27 repos, so @wolffm/fleet-manager could not change\nhow it is addressed without editing the whole ecosystem.\n\nSafe because CI_RUNNER is already set here. fleet-manager 0.5.0 writes the\nfleet target to every covered repo instead of deleting the variable, and it is\nPERSISTENT repo state — if the fleet manager stops, the last value stays and CI\nkeeps scheduling.\n\nWhere a job carries the fork-PR author_association guard, only the trailing\nfleet fallback is removed; the guard that sends untrusted PRs to hosted runners\nis untouched.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLTBaGmB46GZHs25GwvxF8Do2d3nqz+01rwyt2g0Rb3HLvD8RT1Pog7wuDhVEuum11\ndH9TbF6GypFzkt1nmK8Qc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T05:30:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/f7c4dfafe917bce6e8bf9a073baa728bba2243b6","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKGY3YzRkZmFmZTkxN2JjZTZlOGJmOWEwNzNiYWE3MjhiYmEyMjQzYjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/68d9cb7563c1bd7c46ff7ed705d67f992ea4fb26","sha":"68d9cb7563c1bd7c46ff7ed705d67f992ea4fb26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/68d9cb7563c1bd7c46ff7ed705d67f992ea4fb26"}],"sha":"f7c4dfafe917bce6e8bf9a073baa728bba2243b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/f7c4dfafe917bce6e8bf9a073baa728bba2243b6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/68d9cb7563c1bd7c46ff7ed705d67f992ea4fb26/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T01:05:51Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T01:05:51Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(sets): hand a set over by NAME, resolved — the 2026-08-25 incident, closed\n\n`POST /sets/{id}/owner` took a `userId` out of the request body and stored it\nunlooked-up. The reasoning was that a userId is not a credential, so accepting\none is safe. True, and beside the point: what made it unsafe is that nothing\nRESOLVED it. On 2026-08-25 `{\"userId\": \"hadoku\"}` was accepted — `hadoku` is a\nDISPLAY NAME, the registry row is `Hadoku` and its userId is `de5c2a05-…` — and\na published set was owned by nobody for two days.\n\nThe first fix was a UUID regex, and it was deleted for being a format opinion.\nBoth were the wrong axis. A registry lookup rejects `hadoku` AND a well-formed\nUUID belonging to nobody, which a regex waves through. The rule is not \"check\nthe shape\", it is NEVER STORE AN IDENTIFIER YOU DID NOT RESOLVE.\n\nSo the endpoint takes a display `name`, resolves it through\n@wolffm/worker-utils/identity, stores the resulting userId, and echoes name +\ntier back so a human can confirm the identity before a change their previous\nowner cannot undo alone. 404 NAME_NOT_FOUND, 409 for a key that never signed in\n— the same wire shape hadoku-task uses.\n\nThe input schema is STRICT, and that is load-bearing. zod strips an unknown key\nsilently, which would turn an old client''s `{\"userId\": …}` into an empty body —\ni.e. a silent SELF-CLAIM, assigning the set to the caller instead of the person\nthey named, with nothing reporting it. Strict makes the retired field a 400.\n\nThe empty-body self-claim is otherwise untouched: it needs no lookup, the\ncaller''s identity was already resolved at the edge, and it is the branch that\nRECOVERED the incident.\n\nschemas.owner.test.ts stays, inverted. It used to assert `{userId: ''hadoku''}`\nwas valid, commented \"This is a real identity.\" It now asserts the whole class\nis rejected, including a well-formed UUID.\n\nContract: docs/architecture/IDENTITY_MODEL.md in hadoku_site.","tree":{"sha":"13d5fe6dd246433d3af75dd35dfb5bc5579f18fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/13d5fe6dd246433d3af75dd35dfb5bc5579f18fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/68d9cb7563c1bd7c46ff7ed705d67f992ea4fb26","verification":{"payload":"tree 13d5fe6dd246433d3af75dd35dfb5bc5579f18fa\nparent bd69a524cbedb00d49c5fbe897f53d5f454a3273\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787879151 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787879151 -0700\n\nfix(sets): hand a set over by NAME, resolved — the 2026-08-25 incident, closed\n\n`POST /sets/{id}/owner` took a `userId` out of the request body and stored it\nunlooked-up. The reasoning was that a userId is not a credential, so accepting\none is safe. True, and beside the point: what made it unsafe is that nothing\nRESOLVED it. On 2026-08-25 `{\"userId\": \"hadoku\"}` was accepted — `hadoku` is a\nDISPLAY NAME, the registry row is `Hadoku` and its userId is `de5c2a05-…` — and\na published set was owned by nobody for two days.\n\nThe first fix was a UUID regex, and it was deleted for being a format opinion.\nBoth were the wrong axis. A registry lookup rejects `hadoku` AND a well-formed\nUUID belonging to nobody, which a regex waves through. The rule is not \"check\nthe shape\", it is NEVER STORE AN IDENTIFIER YOU DID NOT RESOLVE.\n\nSo the endpoint takes a display `name`, resolves it through\n@wolffm/worker-utils/identity, stores the resulting userId, and echoes name +\ntier back so a human can confirm the identity before a change their previous\nowner cannot undo alone. 404 NAME_NOT_FOUND, 409 for a key that never signed in\n— the same wire shape hadoku-task uses.\n\nThe input schema is STRICT, and that is load-bearing. zod strips an unknown key\nsilently, which would turn an old client''s `{\"userId\": …}` into an empty body —\ni.e. a silent SELF-CLAIM, assigning the set to the caller instead of the person\nthey named, with nothing reporting it. Strict makes the retired field a 400.\n\nThe empty-body self-claim is otherwise untouched: it needs no lookup, the\ncaller''s identity was already resolved at the edge, and it is the branch that\nRECOVERED the incident.\n\nschemas.owner.test.ts stays, inverted. It used to assert `{userId: ''hadoku''}`\nwas valid, commented \"This is a real identity.\" It now asserts the whole class\nis rejected, including a well-formed UUID.\n\nContract: docs/architecture/IDENTITY_MODEL.md in hadoku_site.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJ+a+ePVX8Mx/gxafpxK3vs84njSiFSEexFwHrvqA5/kRXdzvP36cPQkQD+NrTpzvU\n8TN+uaQR0hKJQDF05eSA4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-28T01:06:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/68d9cb7563c1bd7c46ff7ed705d67f992ea4fb26","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKDY4ZDljYjc1NjNjMWJkN2M0NmZmN2VkNzA1ZDY3Zjk5MmVhNGZiMjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/bd69a524cbedb00d49c5fbe897f53d5f454a3273","sha":"bd69a524cbedb00d49c5fbe897f53d5f454a3273","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/bd69a524cbedb00d49c5fbe897f53d5f454a3273"}],"sha":"68d9cb7563c1bd7c46ff7ed705d67f992ea4fb26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/68d9cb7563c1bd7c46ff7ed705d67f992ea4fb26"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/bd69a524cbedb00d49c5fbe897f53d5f454a3273/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T17:59:25Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T17:59:25Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"ci(publish): corepack instead of pnpm/action-setup — the last file the migration missed\n\npublish.yml was the only workflow in this repo still on pnpm/action-setup;\nci.yml and update-wolffm.yml were migrated already. The action defaults to\n`dest: ~/setup-pnpm`, and every per-repo runner install on a claw shares\nHOME=/home/hadoku — so the 13:00 fleet auto-update wave has several publish\njobs installing pnpm into ONE directory at once.\n\nBoth faces of that race landed at the same second on 2026-08-26T13:03:51Z:\n\n  hadoku-study   ENOTEMPTY: rmdir ''/home/hadoku/setup-pnpm/.../semver''\n  hadoku-hopper  ENOENT: open ''/home/hadoku/setup-pnpm/package.json''\n\nOne job was deleting the tree while the other read it. Same bug, and the\ndigest filed them in different buckets — study as red-right-now, hopper as\nbriefly-failed — which is why it read as two problems.\n\ncorepack ships with the Node that setup-node just installed and resolves the\nversion from package.json \"packageManager\" (pnpm@11.5.0 here), so there is no\nshared mutable install directory to race on. Byte-identical to the block\nci.yml in this repo already runs.\n\n`cache: pnpm` goes with it: corepack now runs AFTER setup-node, so pnpm is not\non PATH at the point that input is evaluated.","tree":{"sha":"95a612a23bc2ce9e8c98db8a50c4bf2e200fedac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/95a612a23bc2ce9e8c98db8a50c4bf2e200fedac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/bd69a524cbedb00d49c5fbe897f53d5f454a3273","verification":{"payload":"tree 95a612a23bc2ce9e8c98db8a50c4bf2e200fedac\nparent cbcd4d38665e64830bf7afca86f3ce475c608c42\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787853565 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787853565 -0700\n\nci(publish): corepack instead of pnpm/action-setup — the last file the migration missed\n\npublish.yml was the only workflow in this repo still on pnpm/action-setup;\nci.yml and update-wolffm.yml were migrated already. The action defaults to\n`dest: ~/setup-pnpm`, and every per-repo runner install on a claw shares\nHOME=/home/hadoku — so the 13:00 fleet auto-update wave has several publish\njobs installing pnpm into ONE directory at once.\n\nBoth faces of that race landed at the same second on 2026-08-26T13:03:51Z:\n\n  hadoku-study   ENOTEMPTY: rmdir ''/home/hadoku/setup-pnpm/.../semver''\n  hadoku-hopper  ENOENT: open ''/home/hadoku/setup-pnpm/package.json''\n\nOne job was deleting the tree while the other read it. Same bug, and the\ndigest filed them in different buckets — study as red-right-now, hopper as\nbriefly-failed — which is why it read as two problems.\n\ncorepack ships with the Node that setup-node just installed and resolves the\nversion from package.json \"packageManager\" (pnpm@11.5.0 here), so there is no\nshared mutable install directory to race on. Byte-identical to the block\nci.yml in this repo already runs.\n\n`cache: pnpm` goes with it: corepack now runs AFTER setup-node, so pnpm is not\non PATH at the point that input is evaluated.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQIAWIrItbFS1r7cd16WH79MbetyumwEYrwcjJXdlAHWKVbUVw17yXL1trY4cHr/LFX\nf+48zwY2tNKa4sn7M9KAY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T17:59:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/bd69a524cbedb00d49c5fbe897f53d5f454a3273","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKGJkNjlhNTI0Y2JlZGIwMGQ0OWM1ZmJlODk3ZjUzZDVmNDU0YTMyNzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/cbcd4d38665e64830bf7afca86f3ce475c608c42","sha":"cbcd4d38665e64830bf7afca86f3ce475c608c42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/cbcd4d38665e64830bf7afca86f3ce475c608c42"}],"sha":"bd69a524cbedb00d49c5fbe897f53d5f454a3273","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/bd69a524cbedb00d49c5fbe897f53d5f454a3273"},{"a