atars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/3f1241c5c5c21c48b50f4b56cad24710694b6cca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T20:35:58Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T20:35:58Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(ui): a mode tile says what it is called, and nothing else\n\nYou asked for this once and I did half of it. I removed the blurb and kept\nthe summary, arguing it was data rather than explanation. On the page it\nreads:\n\n    22 facts\n    62 questions\n\n    Study\n    62 questions from 22 facts\n\nThe second line restates the first. That is the interface talking about\nitself, which is what was being objected to, and the distinction I drew to\nkeep it was not a real one.\n\nBoth are gone now, and `summary` is removed from GameAvailability rather\nthan left unrendered — a field nothing draws is worse than no field.\n`blocked` stays: it is the only prose a game gets, and it says why a mode\nis unavailable, which the page cannot say for itself.\n\nTakes four tests and the .mode__summary style with it.","tree":{"sha":"b6db81e2fb50c03b5d8f45b46f51d3a3dead5afa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/b6db81e2fb50c03b5d8f45b46f51d3a3dead5afa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/3f1241c5c5c21c48b50f4b56cad24710694b6cca","verification":{"payload":"tree b6db81e2fb50c03b5d8f45b46f51d3a3dead5afa\nparent 37098cee21abe9386eb26749e2b0e370eb80f7c5\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787690158 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787690158 -0700\n\nfix(ui): a mode tile says what it is called, and nothing else\n\nYou asked for this once and I did half of it. I removed the blurb and kept\nthe summary, arguing it was data rather than explanation. On the page it\nreads:\n\n    22 facts\n    62 questions\n\n    Study\n    62 questions from 22 facts\n\nThe second line restates the first. That is the interface talking about\nitself, which is what was being objected to, and the distinction I drew to\nkeep it was not a real one.\n\nBoth are gone now, and `summary` is removed from GameAvailability rather\nthan left unrendered — a field nothing draws is worse than no field.\n`blocked` stays: it is the only prose a game gets, and it says why a mode\nis unavailable, which the page cannot say for itself.\n\nTakes four tests and the .mode__summary style with it.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJJON5UP9n9RbgyOybbHrVUfU1keKObYbEk+fo4JORAzApAR2FAH/w2DzSVbJCB8r+\n5+5THyGbdyNWfcIbht/gI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T20:36:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/3f1241c5c5c21c48b50f4b56cad24710694b6cca","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKDNmMTI0MWM1YzVjMjFjNDhiNTBmNGI1NmNhZDI0NzEwNjk0YjZjY2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/37098cee21abe9386eb26749e2b0e370eb80f7c5","sha":"37098cee21abe9386eb26749e2b0e370eb80f7c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/37098cee21abe9386eb26749e2b0e370eb80f7c5"}],"sha":"3f1241c5c5c21c48b50f4b56cad24710694b6cca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/3f1241c5c5c21c48b50f4b56cad24710694b6cca"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/37098cee21abe9386eb26749e2b0e370eb80f7c5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T20:23:52Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T20:23:52Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(ui): a small button should be as tall as a small button\n\nThe tools row rendered at 64x44 with 12px text and 2px of padding — the\ntext floating in a void at 3.7x its own height. `.btn` sets a 44px\nmin-height because that is the floor a thumb needs, and `.btn--sm` shrinks\nthe font without touching it, so the height came entirely from the floor\nand none from proportion.\n\nIt was invisible while those buttons had no border. Giving them one last\nrelease is what made it obvious.\n\nThe floor is a TOUCH rule, so it is relaxed only under `pointer: fine`,\nwhere padding decides the height instead: 32px, 2.7x the text, and wider\ntoo since the horizontal padding goes 4px to 12px. A device that does not\nmatch the query keeps the 44px target, which is the safe direction to\nfail.\n\nMeasured against production before and after rather than eyeballed.","tree":{"sha":"f5e5b66cee81a630832f2f7c788c2a34df13567b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/f5e5b66cee81a630832f2f7c788c2a34df13567b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/37098cee21abe9386eb26749e2b0e370eb80f7c5","verification":{"payload":"tree f5e5b66cee81a630832f2f7c788c2a34df13567b\nparent 718e3fc44ef3fd18340e30d6c99052776ed63f4f\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787689432 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787689432 -0700\n\nfix(ui): a small button should be as tall as a small button\n\nThe tools row rendered at 64x44 with 12px text and 2px of padding — the\ntext floating in a void at 3.7x its own height. `.btn` sets a 44px\nmin-height because that is the floor a thumb needs, and `.btn--sm` shrinks\nthe font without touching it, so the height came entirely from the floor\nand none from proportion.\n\nIt was invisible while those buttons had no border. Giving them one last\nrelease is what made it obvious.\n\nThe floor is a TOUCH rule, so it is relaxed only under `pointer: fine`,\nwhere padding decides the height instead: 32px, 2.7x the text, and wider\ntoo since the horizontal padding goes 4px to 12px. A device that does not\nmatch the query keeps the 44px target, which is the safe direction to\nfail.\n\nMeasured against production before and after rather than eyeballed.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQIXb4r+68hDuHIrrXVpMJNgdVwB7TSeX8s13cFlDv32rcLDA7MNiUc6P2obANeGseR\ntMAu0DlaZh0ebnQW/UpgY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T20:24:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/37098cee21abe9386eb26749e2b0e370eb80f7c5","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKDM3MDk4Y2VlMjFhYmU5Mzg2ZWIyNjc0OWUyYjBlMzcwZWI4MGY3YzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/718e3fc44ef3fd18340e30d6c99052776ed63f4f","sha":"718e3fc44ef3fd18340e30d6c99052776ed63f4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/718e3fc44ef3fd18340e30d6c99052776ed63f4f"}],"sha":"37098cee21abe9386eb26749e2b0e370eb80f7c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/37098cee21abe9386eb26749e2b0e370eb80f7c5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/718e3fc44ef3fd18340e30d6c99052776ed63f4f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:18:58Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:19:39Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(api): a userId is an opaque string, not a UUID\n\nI shipped a UUID regex on the transfer endpoint one release ago and it was\nwrong. registry.ts mints a UUID only for records it CREATES —\n`existing?.userId ?? crypto.randomUUID()` — so an identity seeded any\nother way keeps whatever id it was given. `hadoku` is a real one, and the\nregex made a legitimate owner unassignable.\n\nThat regex was the only place in this codebase asserting a userId format,\nand it was asserting the wrong one; every other userId here is already a\nplain string. Guarding against a typo by refusing the correct value is a\nworse failure than the typo.\n\nWhat is checked now is what a store needs rather than what a format\nimplies: non-empty, trimmed, bounded, no whitespace. That still stops a\npasted line-break from becoming an owner nobody can authenticate as, and\nadmin remains the rescue for one that does.","tree":{"sha":"ea15cc4f209e7b450a5c16b8a5b2c8427c7cbfc7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/ea15cc4f209e7b450a5c16b8a5b2c8427c7cbfc7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/718e3fc44ef3fd18340e30d6c99052776ed63f4f","verification":{"payload":"tree ea15cc4f209e7b450a5c16b8a5b2c8427c7cbfc7\nparent 3fe391b848c7616b18b637d57ed12c926b7a0756\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787671138 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787671179 -0700\n\nfix(api): a userId is an opaque string, not a UUID\n\nI shipped a UUID regex on the transfer endpoint one release ago and it was\nwrong. registry.ts mints a UUID only for records it CREATES —\n`existing?.userId ?? crypto.randomUUID()` — so an identity seeded any\nother way keeps whatever id it was given. `hadoku` is a real one, and the\nregex made a legitimate owner unassignable.\n\nThat regex was the only place in this codebase asserting a userId format,\nand it was asserting the wrong one; every other userId here is already a\nplain string. Guarding against a typo by refusing the correct value is a\nworse failure than the typo.\n\nWhat is checked now is what a store needs rather than what a format\nimplies: non-empty, trimmed, bounded, no whitespace. That still stops a\npasted line-break from becoming an owner nobody can authenticate as, and\nadmin remains the rescue for one that does.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLyGujRUsCbLHw81YoBiwC0C98ERSJ/YWPQXQlvFln3NG7IZhJAKrJrdI433zMgwTv\n8CpS0t0zPAvbNrq+OHXwE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T15:20:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/718e3fc44ef3fd18340e30d6c99052776ed63f4f","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKDcxOGUzZmM0NGVmM2ZkMTgzNDBlMzBkNmM5OTA1Mjc3NmVkNjNmNGY","par