//api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/9799ac455223a9de5fc7848b9ac5827006007ff4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T06:00:32Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T06:00:32Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat(api): a set can be given away, by userId\n\nPOST /sets/{id}/owner. The asymmetry is the design: the current owner may\nhand a set to any userId, an admin may move any set, and everyone else\ngets the same 404 a non-existent set gets. You can give a set away; you\ncannot take one. There is no claim and no adopt.\n\nA userId is not a credential — it is the registry''s per-user UUID, and\nknowing one grants nothing. The platform had already settled that:\n/session/keys/by-repo hands out userId, name and tier at SERVICE tier,\ndeliberately not admin, because the response carries nothing\nbearer-shaped. So naming a recipient by userId is safe to accept, log and\npublish; the security lives in the owner check, not in the id being\nsecret. Worth stating plainly, because the instinct is to treat the id as\nsensitive and then build the wrong protections around it.\n\nThe UUID shape is validated for a different reason: a typo assigns the set\nto a userId nobody holds a key for, and it is then unreachable through the\nAPI. Admin can rescue it — that is what the admin path is for, and why an\nomitted userId means \"give it to me\".\n\n`loadSetById` is the only loader that ignores who is asking. Kept as its\nown function rather than a flag on loadSetForWrite, because a boolean that\nturns an access check off is a boolean somebody eventually passes by\naccident.\n\nAlso retires the ''cards-replaced'' telemetry verb, which named a route\ndeleted back in 0003.","tree":{"sha":"c2ce46be56ebf12ef692bf1c0ea930b8800e752f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/c2ce46be56ebf12ef692bf1c0ea930b8800e752f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/9799ac455223a9de5fc7848b9ac5827006007ff4","verification":{"payload":"tree c2ce46be56ebf12ef692bf1c0ea930b8800e752f\nparent 8dde651ad0dc560f4ef71a5b351dcd142d2b4a4d\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787637632 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787637632 -0700\n\nfeat(api): a set can be given away, by userId\n\nPOST /sets/{id}/owner. The asymmetry is the design: the current owner may\nhand a set to any userId, an admin may move any set, and everyone else\ngets the same 404 a non-existent set gets. You can give a set away; you\ncannot take one. There is no claim and no adopt.\n\nA userId is not a credential — it is the registry''s per-user UUID, and\nknowing one grants nothing. The platform had already settled that:\n/session/keys/by-repo hands out userId, name and tier at SERVICE tier,\ndeliberately not admin, because the response carries nothing\nbearer-shaped. So naming a recipient by userId is safe to accept, log and\npublish; the security lives in the owner check, not in the id being\nsecret. Worth stating plainly, because the instinct is to treat the id as\nsensitive and then build the wrong protections around it.\n\nThe UUID shape is validated for a different reason: a typo assigns the set\nto a userId nobody holds a key for, and it is then unreachable through the\nAPI. Admin can rescue it — that is what the admin path is for, and why an\nomitted userId means \"give it to me\".\n\n`loadSetById` is the only loader that ignores who is asking. Kept as its\nown function rather than a flag on loadSetForWrite, because a boolean that\nturns an access check off is a boolean somebody eventually passes by\naccident.\n\nAlso retires the ''cards-replaced'' telemetry verb, which named a route\ndeleted back in 0003.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLCSWt7QSu2yfcK/ucRDpfQbH52nQgFdeVk+J/DN1KwLpCnkAcXxmVpKNrl9+yojF8\n/WfycldZ7266rqZSkcWAQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T06:00:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/9799ac455223a9de5fc7848b9ac5827006007ff4","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKDk3OTlhYzQ1NTIyM2E5ZGU1ZmM3ODQ4YjlhYzU4MjcwMDYwMDdmZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/8dde651ad0dc560f4ef71a5b351dcd142d2b4a4d","sha":"8dde651ad0dc560f4ef71a5b351dcd142d2b4a4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/8dde651ad0dc560f4ef71a5b351dcd142d2b4a4d"}],"sha":"9799ac455223a9de5fc7848b9ac5827006007ff4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/9799ac455223a9de5fc7848b9ac5827006007ff4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/8dde651ad0dc560f4ef71a5b351dcd142d2b4a4d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T05:30:17Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T05:30:17Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat: upload a set over this one, after showing what it would do\n\nA PUT replaces content wholesale, so on the wire \"here is the new version\"\nis indistinguishable from \"delete eleven facts\". Upload JSON parses, lints\nand diffs the file BEFORE anything is sent, and asks.\n\nThe diff is ordered by what it costs to get wrong rather than by what\nchanged most. Two things are permanent and invisible in the JSON, so they\nare stated first and in words:\n\n- Facts that came back WITHOUT their id but match one already here. That\n  is not an edit, it is a delete and a fresh insert, and every rating and\n  answer the fact earned goes with it. It is the easiest mistake an agent\n  can make and there is no error anywhere when it happens. Matched by slot\n  VALUE rather than name, so renaming slots cannot hide it, and at a\n  threshold high enough that two facts sharing a where and a when are not\n  mistaken for one.\n- Facts simply being deleted, with their history.\n\nThen the lint errors, the metadata changes, and a per-fact list that skips\nthe unchanged majority. Publication is never touched: a file describes\ncontent, not who may read it.\n\nAlso makes the editor usable on an authored set. Rich facts were forced\nopen, which turned 22 facts into a wall nobody could scan; they now\ncollapse to a summary — what the fact holds and how many ways it is asked\n— and open on click. Every fact stays visible without every fact being\nunrolled. \"Edit cards\" is \"Edit set\", which is what it edits.","tree":{"sha":"473fa84ef6936b711b4558939cb3e239df467581","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/473fa84ef6936b711b4558939cb3e239df467581"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/8dde651ad0dc560f4ef71a5b351dcd142d2b4a4d","verification":{"payload":"tree 473fa84ef6936b711b4558939cb3e239df467581\nparent 7b0636c7d435474daf8ce6a88217f57b47301680\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787635817 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787635817 -0700\n\nfeat: upload a set over this one, after showing what it would do\n\nA PUT replaces content wholesale, so on the wire \"here is the new version\"\nis indistinguishable from \"delete eleven facts\". Upload JSON parses, lints\nand diffs the file BEFORE anything is sent, and asks.\n\nThe diff is ordered by what it costs to get wrong rather than by what\nchanged most. Two things are permanent and invisible in the JSON, so they\nare stated first and in words:\n\n- Facts that came back WITHOUT their id but match one already here. That\n  is not an edit, it is a delete and a fresh insert, and every rating and\n  answer the fact earned goes with it. It is the easiest mistake an agent\n  can make and there is no error anywhere when it happens. Matched by slot\n  VALUE rather than name, so renaming slots cannot hide it, and at a\n  threshold high enough that two facts sharing a where and a when are not\n  mistaken for one.\n- Facts simply being deleted, with their history.\n\nThen the lint errors, the metadata changes, and a per-fact list that skips\nthe unchanged majority. Publication is never touched: a file describes\ncontent, not who may read it.\n\nAlso makes the editor usable on an authored set. Rich facts were forced\nopen, which turned 22 facts into a wall nobody could scan; they now\ncollapse to a summary — what the fact holds and how many ways it is asked\n— and open on click. Every fact stays visible without every fact being\nunrolled. \"Edit cards\" is \"Edit set\", which is what it edits.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQKJ18JvAFPPXKgCKhynwVmdBr15fUq7A6MOvN9yfvbynIsP471xJodD7Z1Mb3lgF8c\nTzAOY9PmMBcooXwYaYogE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T05:30:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/8dde651ad0dc560f4ef71a5b351dcd142d2b4a4d","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKDhkZGU2NTFhZDBkYzU2MGY0ZWY3MWE1YjM1MWRjZDE0MmQyYjRhNGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/7b0636c7d435474daf8ce6a88217f57b47301680","sha":"7b0636c7d435474daf8ce6a88217f57b47301680","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/7b0636c7d435474daf8ce6a88217f57b47301680"}],"sha":"8dde651ad0dc560f4ef71a5b351dcd142d2b4a4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/8dde651ad0dc560f4ef71a5b351dcd142d2b4a4d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/7b0636c7d435474daf8ce6a88217f57b47301680/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T05:16:26Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T05:16:26Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(ui): call it Copy JSON, drop the mode blurbs, make three buttons look like buttons\n\nThree bits of chrome that were explaining rather than working.\n\n\"Copy for agent\" is now \"Copy JSON\" — it says what it gives you rather than\nnaming a use case. The brief still rides in front of the file, and the\nhandler comment now says not to strip it to make the label literally true:\neach paragraph in agentBrief.ts prevents a specific kind of bad output, and\n\"Export file\" is already the no-brief version.\n\nThe mode blurbs are gone entirely, not blanked — a required field nobody\nrenders is worse than no field. \"Study\" and \"Play as board\" say what they\nare. The per-set summary underneath stays, because that is data about this\nset rather than an explanation of the mode.\n\nAnd `.btn--quiet` was transparent on both the background AND the border, so\nExport / Copy JSON / Copy link rendered as a row of stray words. \"Quiet\"\nturned out to mean invisible. An outline is enough to say \"press me\"\nwithout competing with the modes; the fill and the weight rank them.","tree":{"sha":"563e4f4dc570dedb8ea3ebdaace6b69c155fc7f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/563e4f4dc570dedb8ea3ebdaace6b69c155fc7f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/7b0636c7d435474daf8ce6a88217f57b47301680","verification":{"payload":"tree 563e4f4dc570dedb8ea3ebdaace6b69c155fc7f2\nparent a9536277dec637142981c195aa3c8148a1ede289\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787634986 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787634986 -0700\n\nfix(ui): call it Copy JSON, drop the mode blurbs, make three buttons look like buttons\n\nThree bits of chrome that were explaining rather than working.\n\n\"Copy for agent\" is now \"Copy JSON\" — it says what it gives you rather than\nnaming a use case. The brief still rides in front of the file, and the\nhandler comment now says not to strip it to make the label literally true:\neach paragraph in agentBrief.ts prevents a specific kind of bad output, and\n\"Export file\" is already the no-brief version.\n\nThe mode blurbs are gone entirely, not blanked — a required field nobody\nrenders is worse than no field. \"Study\" and \"Play as board\" say what they\nare. The per-set summary underneath stays, because that is data about this\nset rather than an explanation of the mode.\n\nAnd `.btn--quiet` was transparent on both the background AND the border, so\nExport / Copy JSON / Copy link rendered as a row of stray words. \"Quiet\"\nturned out to mean invisible. An outline is enough to say \"press me\"\nwithout competing with the modes; the fill and the weight rank them.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQH+RRhQZXgAr1UrNPlcHBa16DVJ3KYe/bbsDkwjS6PJ3UjuQ3MmDxqG0kn07Dedqlx\nkPsV8+/aAnY2IVYF+3RA0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T05:16:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/7b0636c7d435474daf8ce6a88217f57b47301680","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKDdiMDYzNmM3ZDQzNTQ3NGRhZjhjZTZhODgyMTdmNTdiNDczMDE2ODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/a9536277dec637142981c195aa3c8148a1ede289","sha":"a9536277dec637142981c195aa3c8148a1ede289","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/a9536277dec637142981c195aa3c8148a1ede289"}],"sha":"7b0636c7d435474daf8ce6a88217f57b47301680","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/7b0636c7d435474daf8ce6a88217f57b47301680"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/a9536277dec637142981c195aa3c8148a1ede289/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T04:38:41Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T04:39:36Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"docs: make the authoring rules checkable, and stop the docs lying about v1\n\nThe README was still describing v1 in full — `cards` with front/back, an\n`attrs.board` example for a field that no longer exists, `cardCount`, and a\nclaim that D1 migrations are not automatic. It is the front door, and every\nword of the format section was wrong.\n\nThe agent brief was accurate but incomplete in the way that matters: it\ndescribed `given` as a difficulty lever, which is how I produced the bug\nthat reached production — an authored prompt plus its givens printing the\nsame sentence twice, once large and once small. `given` is what gets DRAWN\nbeside the prompt. A written prompt almost always wants `\"given\": []`.\n\nAdds the three rules the brief was missing, all of them mistakes made here\nwhile writing the set with full knowledge of the model: never put the\nanswer in the prompt, one fact per thing that is true, and a fact is asked\nat most once per board so a column needs five different facts.\n\nAnd makes them checkable rather than hopeful. The API rejects a malformed\nfile; it cannot reject a well-formed one that is simply bad. `model/lint.ts`\nruns over whatever an agent hands back, in the editor, before it is saved —\nanswer leakage measured as a ratio rather than a substring, because the\nleak that happens is a paraphrase; context that repeats what the prompt\nalready said; a declaration asking a slot the fact does not have, which the\nserver skips so the question silently never appears. Its tests are the real\nbad content, verbatim.\n\nIt is pure and client-side because none of it needs a variant key: an\nanswer is slots[ask] and the context is given ?? every other slot. That\nalso let `askedSlots` go — the editor''s board preview derived the same\nthing separately, and now nothing does.\n\nSweeps the stale forward-references out of the source: comments still\nsaying \"v1 is a plain drill\", a promise that v2 would judge typed answers\nwith an LLM (it does not, and that was a decision), and a HANDOFF section\nclaiming rich facts are read-only until Phase 3.","tree":{"sha":"1622426b075fb017f3578ff73eddaaa4d2d7a2f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/1622426b075fb017f3578ff73eddaaa4d2d7a2f4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/a9536277dec637142981c195aa3c8148a1ede289","verification":{"payload":"tree 1622426b075fb017f3578ff73eddaaa4d2d7a2f4\nparent 414ae8d41fad369f4cd61cca409bd212038b2f66\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787632721 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787632776 -0700\n\ndocs: make the authoring rules checkable, and stop the docs lying about v1\n\nThe README was still describing v1 in full — `cards` with front/back, an\n`attrs.board` example for a field that no longer exists, `cardCount`, and a\nclaim that D1 migrations are not automatic. It is the front door, and every\nword of the format section was wrong.\n\nThe agent brief was accurate but incomplete in the way that matters: it\ndescribed `given` as a difficulty lever, which is how I produced the bug\nthat reached production — an authored prompt plus its givens printing the\nsame sentence twice, once large and once small. `given` is what gets DRAWN\nbeside the prompt. A written prompt almost always wants `\"given\": []`.\n\nAdds the three rules the brief was missing, all of them mistakes made here\nwhile writing the set with full knowledge of the model: never put the\nanswer in the prompt, one fact per thing that is true, and a fact is asked\nat most once per board so a column needs five different facts.\n\nAnd makes them checkable rather than hopeful. The API rejects a malformed\nfile; it cannot reject a well-formed one that is simply bad. `model/lint.ts`\nruns over whatever an agent hands back, in the editor, before it is saved —\nanswer leakage measured as a ratio rather than a substring, because the\nleak that happens is a paraphrase; context that repeats what the prompt\nalready said; a declaration asking a slot the fact does not have, which the\nserver skips so the question silently never appears. Its tests are the real\nbad content, verbatim.\n\nIt is pure and client-side because none of it needs a variant key: an\nanswer is slots[ask] and the context is given ?? every other slot. That\nalso let `askedSlots` go — the editor''s board preview derived the same\nthing separately, and now nothing does.\n\nSweeps the stale forward-references out of the source: comments still\nsaying \"v1 is a plain drill\", a promise that v2 would judge typed answers\nwith an LLM (it does not, and that was a decision), and a HANDOFF section\nclaiming rich facts are read-only until Phase 3.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQDS7GW7BuqJ2iRf48AFm5ljJZd0/2RJHJ3MVNFn0/QJPjsJythsQkpO5FP/Fiiy1o8\nHKxGioh0iNqvh/Lmy/NQY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T04:40:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/a9536277dec637142981c195aa3c8148a1ede289","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKGE5NTM2Mjc3ZGVjNjM3MTQyOTgxYzE5NWFhM2M4MTQ4YTFlZGUyODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/414ae8d41fad369f4cd61cca409bd212038b2f66","sha":"414ae8d41fad369f4cd61cca409bd212038b2f66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/414ae8d41fad369f4cd61cca409bd212038b2f66"}],"sha":"a9536277dec637142981c195aa3c8148a1ede289","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/a9536277dec637142981c195aa3c8148a1ede289"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/414ae8d41fad369f4cd61cca409bd212038b2f66/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T03:09:18Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T03:09:18Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"chore: drop the dead husky devDependency from worker/\n\nNothing invokes the husky binary any more: `prepare` wires core.hooksPath\ndirectly and the hooks in .husky/ are run by git itself. This was the last\ncopy, tucked in the workspace''s worker package where the root-level cleanup\ndid not reach it.","tree":{"sha":"ecb2f0d159513f6f78108cbce72993ff0c556a9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/ecb2f0d159513f6f78108cbce72993ff0c556a9e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/414ae8d41fad369f4cd61cca409bd212038b2f66","verification":{"payload":"tree ecb2f0d159513f6f78108cbce72993ff0c556a9e\nparent 60c4047c7c071202cb1f60175bbc457a46c016bf\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787627358 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787627358 -0700\n\nchore: drop the dead husky devDependency from worker/\n\nNothing invokes the husky binary any more: `prepare` wires core.hooksPath\ndirectly and the hooks in .husky/ are run by git itself. This was the last\ncopy, tucked in the workspace''s worker package where the root-level cleanup\ndid not reach it.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQF+Wb+mfS5/4xBQ5EY+ydATnBs5zEw3KL3X5rZ70G6rgug7i7hq+NQnM14gXBgM5lD\nWqAH0kh3IpU7ZZtDjyUQk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T03:09:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/414ae8d41fad369f4cd61cca409bd212038b2f66","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKDQxNGFlOGQ0MWZhZDM2OWY0Y2Q2MWNjYTQwOWJkMjEyMDM4YjJmNjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/60c4047c7c071202cb1f60175bbc457a46c016bf","sha":"60c4047c7c071202cb1f60175bbc457a46c016bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/60c4047c7c071202cb1f60175bbc457a46c016bf"}],"sha":"414ae8d41fad369f4cd61cca409bd212038b2f66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/414ae8d41fad369f4cd61cca409bd212038b2f66"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/60c4047c7c071202cb1f60175bbc457a46c016bf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T02:59:27Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T02:59:27Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix: run git hooks from a tracked directory so worktrees keep their gates\n\ncore.hooksPath pointed at .husky/_, which husky GENERATES and its own\n.gitignore excludes. git resolves a relative core.hooksPath against the\nworking tree root, and the setting lives in the shared config — so a\nlinked worktree inherited the setting but had no .husky/_ to run, and git\nexecuted no hook at all. Silently: no warning, no non-zero exit. Every\ncommit made from a worktree skipped the lint/typecheck gates and the\nversion bump.\n\n.husky/pre-commit and .husky/post-commit are tracked, so pointing straight\nat .husky is present in every worktree by construction. `prepare` sets it\ninstead of calling husky, husky comes out of devDependencies, and the hooks\nget their executable bit in the index — the generated shim used to run them\nwith `sh -e`, which covered for that.\n\nFiring the hook is only half of it: a fresh worktree has no node_modules\nand every gate needs one, so pre-commit borrows the main checkout''s. pnpm\nlays node_modules out as a symlink farm over its own .pnpm store, so a\nworktree on the same dependency set can point at it; a branch that changes\ndependencies fails loudly on the missing package instead.\n\nAlso drops the trailing slash from node_modules in .gitignore — it matches\ndirectories only, so it never matched the worktree symlink.","tree":{"sha":"880608a8cf9561d58c22529f6e1fc15c3cab4b06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/880608a8cf9561d58c22529f6e1fc15c3cab4b06"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/60c4047c7c071202cb1f60175bbc457a46c016bf","verification":{"payload":"tree 880608a8cf9561d58c22529f6e1fc15c3cab4b06\nparent 4f5506d3da845323c83d8ce4d4e8a6ff59c92258\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787626767 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787626767 -0700\n\nfix: run git hooks from a tracked directory so worktrees keep their gates\n\ncore.hooksPath pointed at .husky/_, which husky GENERATES and its own\n.gitignore excludes. git resolves a relative core.hooksPath against the\nworking tree root, and the setting lives in the shared config — so a\nlinked worktree inherited the setting but had no .husky/_ to run, and git\nexecuted no hook at all. Silently: no warning, no non-zero exit. Every\ncommit made from a worktree skipped the lint/typecheck gates and the\nversion bump.\n\n.husky/pre-commit and .husky/post-commit are tracked, so pointing straight\nat .husky is present in every worktree by construction. `prepare` sets it\ninstead of calling husky, husky comes out of devDependencies, and the hooks\nget their executable bit in the index — the generated shim used to run them\nwith `sh -e`, which covered for that.\n\nFiring the hook is only half of it: a fresh worktree has no node_modules\nand every gate needs one, so pre-commit borrows the main checkout''s. pnpm\nlays node_modules out as a symlink farm over its own .pnpm store, so a\nworktree on the same dependency set can point at it; a branch that changes\ndependencies fails loudly on the missing package instead.\n\nAlso drops the trailing slash from node_modules in .gitignore — it matches\ndirectories only, so it never matched the worktree symlink.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQPVmMe7gfGJoc5eEX517uZffCYnmvp8HRvL07WOHJNj/Q4DqOGOjfRXZxeHvlGilcG\ngiupnk3xPfHaMr/QROOQ8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T02:59:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/60c4047c7c071202cb1f60175bbc457a46c016bf","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKDYwYzQwNDdjN2MwNzEyMDJjYjFmNjAxNzViYmM0NTdhNDZjMDE2YmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/4f5506d3da845323c83d8ce4d4e8a6ff59c92258","sha":"4f5506d3da845323c83d8ce4d4e8a6ff59c92258","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/4f5506d3da845323c83d8ce4d4e8a6ff59c92258"}],"sha":"60c4047c7c071202cb1f60175bbc457a46c016bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/60c4047c7c071202cb1f60175bbc457a46c016bf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/4f5506d3da845323c83d8ce4d4e8a6ff59c92258/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T20:31:54Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T20:31:54Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat: say what a sitting did, and where a set stands\n\nv2 phase 5. Everything here reads data the earlier phases already write —\nno migration, and nothing depends on it.\n\nPOST /attempts now returns what each answer MOVED, as a RatingChange\nrather than a plain Rating. Two schemas instead of one with an always-zero\ndelta on reads, which would be a field every caller has to know not to\ntrust. Deltas accumulate across a request, because a flushed outbox can\nname the same question twice and reporting only the last move would\nunderstate it.\n\nThe recap keeps the FIRST outcome and the LATEST rating, and both rules\nare there because the obvious version is wrong. The drill re-queues a\nmissed question until you get it, so the last outcome of every question in\na completed pass is \"got\" — a recap built from that would report a clean\nsweep of every pass you fought through. And a question missed twice then\ngot has moved three times; the honest report is where it landed and how\nfar it went.\n\nA movement is recorded even when nothing reached the server. The recap''s\njob is to say what you got wrong, which is true signed-out and offline; it\njust stays quiet about ratings that did not move.\n\nThe standing panel answers two questions from one dataset. \"Hardest for\nyou\" is your highest local ratings among questions you have answered —\nwhich is what a local rating IS, so re-deriving it from the ledger would\nbe computing an answer the rating already holds. \"Not where you put them\"\nis for the owner: questions whose global rating has drifted past a\nthreshold from the tier they chose. The threshold exists because ratings\nwander by a few points constantly, and reporting that as news trains\npeople to ignore the panel.\n\nThe editor deliberately shows no ratings. It was planned and dropped: the\neditor holds DECLARATIONS, and mapping one to its rating means deriving a\nvariant key, which is server-only by design. The standing panel reads\nresolved variants instead, which already carry the key and the seed tier —\nthe same information without a second key implementation.","tree":{"sha":"adf9ab9de91d0bb876638127d1916c8ece47de6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/adf9ab9de91d0bb876638127d1916c8ece47de6f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/4f5506d3da845323c83d8ce4d4e8a6ff59c92258","verification":{"payload":"tree adf9ab9de91d0bb876638127d1916c8ece47de6f\nparent 4905772ff8208eb7c8923ce1eedea8678d866109\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787603514 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787603514 -0700\n\nfeat: say what a sitting did, and where a set stands\n\nv2 phase 5. Everything here reads data the earlier phases already write —\nno migration, and nothing depends on it.\n\nPOST /attempts now returns what each answer MOVED, as a RatingChange\nrather than a plain Rating. Two schemas instead of one with an always-zero\ndelta on reads, which would be a field every caller has to know not to\ntrust. Deltas accumulate across a request, because a flushed outbox can\nname the same question twice and reporting only the last move would\nunderstate it.\n\nThe recap keeps the FIRST outcome and the LATEST rating, and both rules\nare there because the obvious version is wrong. The drill re-queues a\nmissed question until you get it, so the last outcome of every question in\na completed pass is \"got\" — a recap built from that would report a clean\nsweep of every pass you fought through. And a question missed twice then\ngot has moved three times; the honest report is where it landed and how\nfar it went.\n\nA movement is recorded even when nothing reached the server. The recap''s\njob is to say what you got wrong, which is true signed-out and offline; it\njust stays quiet about ratings that did not move.\n\nThe standing panel answers two questions from one dataset. \"Hardest for\nyou\" is your highest local ratings among questions you have answered —\nwhich is what a local rating IS, so re-deriving it from the ledger would\nbe computing an answer the rating already holds. \"Not where you put them\"\nis for the owner: questions whose global rating has drifted past a\nthreshold from the tier they chose. The threshold exists because ratings\nwander by a few points constantly, and reporting that as news trains\npeople to ignore the panel.\n\nThe editor deliberately shows no ratings. It was planned and dropped: the\neditor holds DECLARATIONS, and mapping one to its rating means deriving a\nvariant key, which is server-only by design. The standing panel reads\nresolved variants instead, which already carry the key and the seed tier —\nthe same information without a second key implementation.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQCa4jvJF4Mr2vR6vdC0YzaTe8vkLZuzV8B0cSoGDm4p9LhLaxGiIVRiG9FK87dwULW\njWHxTqlBZPSblRS4gIQw0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-24T20:32:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/4f5506d3da845323c83d8ce4d4e8a6ff59c92258","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKDRmNTUwNmQzZGE4NDUzMjNjODNkOGNlNGQ0ZThhNmZmNTljOTIyNTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/4905772ff8208eb7c8923ce1eedea8678d866109","sha":"4905772ff8208eb7c8923ce1eedea8678d866109","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/4905772ff8208eb7c8923ce1eedea8678d866109"}],"sha":"4f5506d3da845323c83d8ce4d4e8a6ff59c92258","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/4f5506d3da845323c83d8ce4d4e8a6ff59c92258"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/4905772ff8208eb7c8923ce1eedea8678d866109/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T03:57:28Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T03:57:28Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix: a set that asks one kind of question is not a board\n\nRemoving three dead exports surfaced a real bug in one of them.\n\n`isPlayable` was never called — the game definition gated on\n`buildBoard(...).clueCount === 0` instead. But isPlayable also enforced the\ntwo-column minimum and buildBoard did not, so a set asking only one kind\nof question would have been offered a single-column board: the deck with a\nnumber on it. Two answers to one question, and the one nobody called was\nthe correct one.\n\nFixed by moving the minimum into buildBoard, so there is one decision and\nno predicate to disagree with it. The tests now assert against the same\npath the game actually uses.\n\nAlso drops `countQuestions` (the API returns variantCount, so nothing ever\ncounted client-side — it had a test for a caller and no caller) and\n`OPEN_SLOTS` (openness is per QUESTION and arrives on the variant, so a\nclient list of which slots default to open never had a reader).","tree":{"sha":"5c318dee0f364b7ddb3ca75935b1d9e68537615a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/5c318dee0f364b7ddb3ca75935b1d9e68537615a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/4905772ff8208eb7c8923ce1eedea8678d866109","verification":{"payload":"tree 5c318dee0f364b7ddb3ca75935b1d9e68537615a\nparent 8facb6e55059f4d2a1d65f3d497df22bcc7c3573\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787543848 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787543848 -0700\n\nfix: a set that asks one kind of question is not a board\n\nRemoving three dead exports surfaced a real bug in one of them.\n\n`isPlayable` was never called — the game definition gated on\n`buildBoard(...).clueCount === 0` instead. But isPlayable also enforced the\ntwo-column minimum and buildBoard did not, so a set asking only one kind\nof question would have been offered a single-column board: the deck with a\nnumber on it. Two answers to one question, and the one nobody called was\nthe correct one.\n\nFixed by moving the minimum into buildBoard, so there is one decision and\nno predicate to disagree with it. The tests now assert against the same\npath the game actually uses.\n\nAlso drops `countQuestions` (the API returns variantCount, so nothing ever\ncounted client-side — it had a test for a caller and no caller) and\n`OPEN_SLOTS` (openness is per QUESTION and arrives on the variant, so a\nclient list of which slots default to open never had a reader).\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQEYGSMfyIm186eFNyxakxjtEpcwiYvgLX9XyjUKiYsjI59rF0LQdn3qLlrZa5lCRYZ\nF4KEB1Dve/TgVvL5q7LQ4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-24T03:57:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/4905772ff8208eb7c8923ce1eedea8678d866109","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKDQ5MDU3NzJmZjgyMDhlYjdjODkyM2NlMWVlZGVhODY3OGQ4NjYxMDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/8facb6e55059f4d2a1d65f3d497df22bcc7c3573","sha":"8facb6e55059f4d2a1d65f3d497df22bcc7c3573","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/8facb6e55059f4d2a1d65f3d497df22bcc7c3573"}],"sha":"4905772ff8208eb7c8923ce1eedea8678d866109","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/4905772ff8208eb7c8923ce1eedea8678d866109"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/8facb6e55059f4d2a1d65f3d497df22bcc7c3573/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T03:53:10Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T03:53:10Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat: boards are dealt from the content, not tagged into existence\n\nv2 phase 4. A column is an asked SLOT — \"Name that year\" is every question\nwhose answer is a `when`. Nothing is tagged for the board, so the\n`attrs.board` namespace that held a per-fact category is gone: it had no\nreader left, and a schema describing a field nothing reads is how a dead\nfeature keeps looking alive.\n\nThat change is what finally gives the no-repeated-facts rule teeth. Under\nper-fact categories every question about a fact shared a column, so a fact\ncould only appear once anyway. Asking by slot scatters one fact''s\nquestions across four columns, and \"where did Luther meet Charles V\" now\ngenuinely collides with \"who did Luther meet at Worms\".\n\nSo filling the grid became an assignment problem, not four independent\npicks: a fact taken by one column is gone from every other, and picking\neach column''s best can strand a column whose options have all been\nclaimed. Rather than backtracking with a retry budget, this uses maximum\nbipartite matching — shorter, always finds a full board when one exists,\nnothing to tune. Cells state a preference (spread across the column''s\ndifficulty range) and the matching honours it where it can. The test that\nseparates the two approaches is pinned: two columns, two rows, one shared\nfact; greedy strands a column, matching makes the first give one back.\n\nAt least one column is explain-it when the set has one, displacing the\nweakest otherwise-chosen column so the guarantee costs the least coverage.\nRows shrink before columns, so a thin set renders 4x2 rather than 2x5. A\nplain flashcard deck yields no columns at all and is not offered as a\nboard — its only slots are prompt and answer, and a column headed \"Answer\"\nis the whole deck with a number on it.\n\nDealt from the real Reformation set: 4 columns, 20 clues, 20 distinct\nfacts, 6000 points, 37 questions held back in the deck.","tree":{"sha":"542ab47adf121297de48a92e5211a2f5f381564a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/542ab47adf121297de48a92e5211a2f5f381564a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/8facb6e55059f4d2a1d65f3d497df22bcc7c3573","verification":{"payload":"tree 542ab47adf121297de48a92e5211a2f5f381564a\nparent 88693de3a45ac423ca5527e0f39b85248a6afdff\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787543590 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787543590 -0700\n\nfeat: boards are dealt from the content, not tagged into existence\n\nv2 phase 4. A column is an asked SLOT — \"Name that year\" is every question\nwhose answer is a `when`. Nothing is tagged for the board, so the\n`attrs.board` namespace that held a per-fact category is gone: it had no\nreader left, and a schema describing a field nothing reads is how a dead\nfeature keeps looking alive.\n\nThat change is what finally gives the no-repeated-facts rule teeth. Under\nper-fact categories every question about a fact shared a column, so a fact\ncould only appear once anyway. Asking by slot scatters one fact''s\nquestions across four columns, and \"where did Luther meet Charles V\" now\ngenuinely collides with \"who did Luther meet at Worms\".\n\nSo filling the grid became an assignment problem, not four independent\npicks: a fact taken by one column is gone from every other, and picking\neach column''s best can strand a column whose options have all been\nclaimed. Rather than backtracking with a retry budget, this uses maximum\nbipartite matching — shorter, always finds a full board when one exists,\nnothing to tune. Cells state a preference (spread across the column''s\ndifficulty range) and the matching honours it where it can. The test that\nseparates the two approaches is pinned: two columns, two rows, one shared\nfact; greedy strands a column, matching makes the first give one back.\n\nAt least one column is explain-it when the set has one, displacing the\nweakest otherwise-chosen column so the guarantee costs the least coverage.\nRows shrink before columns, so a thin set renders 4x2 rather than 2x5. A\nplain flashcard deck yields no columns at all and is not offered as a\nboard — its only slots are prompt and answer, and a column headed \"Answer\"\nis the whole deck with a number on it.\n\nDealt from the real Reformation set: 4 columns, 20 clues, 20 distinct\nfacts, 6000 points, 37 questions held back in the deck.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQPZwha1elHq9+UzqV7NPlC17jGJHJT4KN4jVe1N6kEnx6vRByMVMpK32WIcOnBQy0P\ne9AqUCZCZa+7WlqPvCYQw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-24T03:53:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/8facb6e55059f4d2a1d65f3d497df22bcc7c3573","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKDhmYWNiNmU1NTA1OWY0ZDJhMWQ2NWYzZDQ5N2RmMjJiY2M3YzM1NzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/88693de3a45ac423ca5527e0f39b85248a6afdff","sha":"88693de3a45ac423ca5527e0f39b85248a6afdff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/88693de3a45ac423ca5527e0f39b85248a6afdff"}],"sha":"8facb6e55059f4d2a1d65f3d497df22bcc7c3573","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/8facb6e55059f4d2a1d65f3d497df22bcc7c3573"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/88693de3a45ac423ca5527e0f39b85248a6afdff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T03:36:26Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T03:36:26Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat: authoring — one file endpoint, one row model, a brief for agents\n\nv2 phase 3, the tooling half.\n\nGET /sets/{id}/file returns the set as a bare document, and the editor''s\nExport button now fetches it instead of serializing the set it already has\nin memory. Two implementations of \"what an export contains\" would\neventually disagree, and the symptom would be a UI export behaving\ndifferently from a scripted one for reasons nobody could see. It is the\none route here that answers unwrapped: a document a person copies should\nnot arrive inside an envelope they have to unwrap first.\n\nMoving the writer server-side also makes the export-is-import property\ndirectly assertable — toSetFile''s output is parsed by ReplaceSetInput in\nthe same test file, rather than inferred across a boundary.\n\nCopy for agent adds the paragraph that has to go with the JSON. Every line\nof it exists because leaving it out produces a specific kind of bad\noutput: an agent that guesses the slot vocabulary, invents its own\nphrasing, or drops the fact ids and silently discards every rating the set\nhas earned.\n\nThe editor collapses to ONE row model holding a whole FactInput, drawn two\nways. Phase 1 kept two row shapes and passed rich facts through untouched\n— safe, but it meant the editor could show you a fact it could not let you\nchange. A fact two inputs cannot hold is always expanded regardless of the\ntoggle, so the toggle can never hide something it cannot show.\n\nTwo of the extracted edits are quietly destructive if wrong, and both are\nnow tested: renaming a slot has to carry through the declarations naming\nit, or the question stops resolving and vanishes from the set; removing\none has to take the questions that asked it.","tree":{"sha":"5c5f2ef37b202a94991373ef0093006e5226b2c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/5c5f2ef37b202a94991373ef0093006e5226b2c2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/88693de3a45ac423ca5527e0f39b85248a6afdff","verification":{"payload":"tree 5c5f2ef37b202a94991373ef0093006e5226b2c2\nparent cd16ad657e9cb8ef29513da955dd9e24873f0ad9\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787542586 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787542586 -0700\n\nfeat: authoring — one file endpoint, one row model, a brief for agents\n\nv2 phase 3, the tooling half.\n\nGET /sets/{id}/file returns the set as a bare document, and the editor''s\nExport button now fetches it instead of serializing the set it already has\nin memory. Two implementations of \"what an export contains\" would\neventually disagree, and the symptom would be a UI export behaving\ndifferently from a scripted one for reasons nobody could see. It is the\none route here that answers unwrapped: a document a person copies should\nnot arrive inside an envelope they have to unwrap first.\n\nMoving the writer server-side also makes the export-is-import property\ndirectly assertable — toSetFile''s output is parsed by ReplaceSetInput in\nthe same test file, rather than inferred across a boundary.\n\nCopy for agent adds the paragraph that has to go with the JSON. Every line\nof it exists because leaving it out produces a specific kind of bad\noutput: an agent that guesses the slot vocabulary, invents its own\nphrasing, or drops the fact ids and silently discards every rating the set\nhas earned.\n\nThe editor collapses to ONE row model holding a whole FactInput, drawn two\nways. Phase 1 kept two row shapes and passed rich facts through untouched\n— safe, but it meant the editor could show you a fact it could not let you\nchange. A fact two inputs cannot hold is always expanded regardless of the\ntoggle, so the toggle can never hide something it cannot show.\n\nTwo of the extracted edits are quietly destructive if wrong, and both are\nnow tested: renaming a slot has to carry through the declarations naming\nit, or the question stops resolving and vanishes from the set; removing\none has to take the questions that asked it.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQH3JKWzoSrwyI1KGoABQhGYMBXorFylTMgxSZvM1CQBwZvjE8kaRu3v9H+EXuQK2fg\nhSL92f463VHSIcLNB2Qg8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-24T03:36:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/88693de3a45ac423ca5527e0f39b85248a6afdff","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKDg4NjkzZGUzYTQ1YWM0MjNjYTU1MjdlMGYzOWI4NTI0OGE2YWZkZmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/cd16ad657e9cb8ef29513da955dd9e24873f0ad9","sha":"cd16ad657e9cb8ef29513da955dd9e24873f0ad9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/cd16ad657e9cb8ef29513da955dd9e24873f0ad9"}],"sha":"88693de3a45ac423ca5527e0f39b85248a6afdff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/88693de3a45ac423ca5527e0f39b85248a6afdff"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/cd16ad657e9cb8ef29513da955dd9e24873f0ad9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T03:26:06Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T03:26:06Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat: ratings that drift, and a ledger that keeps every answer\n\nv2 phase 2. The tables have been sitting empty in production since 0003;\nthis fills them.\n\nElo''s skeleton with the opponent swapped. There is no player rating —\nwhat we want to learn is how hard a QUESTION is, not how good you are — so\nthe adversary is the field, the set''s mean rating, and a question wins when\nyou miss it. Cards ranked against each other, and still self-correcting:\nmissing one already rated brutal confirms what we knew and moves almost\nnothing, while nailing it is a surprise and drops it hard.\n\nThree knobs. K is confidence, so twenty plays are not overturned by one. M\nis the streak, counting the attempt that extends it — scoring at the\nprevious run length lags by one and a two-attempt streak would never get a\nmultiplier at all. E is the field.\n\nGlobal starts at seedTier; local starts at whatever global says the first\ntime YOU attempt that question. Per question rather than per set, which is\nbetter than the plan''s \"copy everything on first engagement\": a question\nyou have never seen still starts from what global has since learned.\nNothing is materialised — an unrated question sits at a real estimate\ncomputed on read, so playing a set writes no rows until you answer.\n\nA board row stops being a stored tier and becomes a RANK, which is the\nwhole reason a board responds to play. The board is dealt once and never\nre-sorted: re-ranking mid-game would slide tiles from under a thumb\nalready moving toward one. One fact may be asked only once per board, and\nthe claim applies as a column fills — filtering once up front let two\nvariants of one fact into the same column, which the tests caught.\n\nEvery answer goes through one recorder both games call. A mode that forgot\nto record would look completely healthy and teach the system nothing. A\nfailed POST is queued and flushed on the same request as the next answer,\noldest first, so a streak spanning an offline patch is still a streak; the\nqueue is cleared before the send so a failure re-queues once rather than\nduplicating what it held.\n\nSigned-out readers write nothing — no identity to attribute an attempt to,\nand no way to tell one anonymous reader from a thousand. Their board still\nranks by seedTier, exactly as it did before ratings existed.\n\nAlso extracts factRows.ts: two routes now read a stored fact, and a second\ncopy of that would end with two endpoints disagreeing about what questions\na fact asks.","tree":{"sha":"f82ab6f0b84dc8691d715c382b8f8ebc2e4b865c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/f82ab6f0b84dc8691d715c382b8f8ebc2e4b865c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/cd16ad657e9cb8ef29513da955dd9e24873f0ad9","verification":{"payload":"tree f82ab6f0b84dc8691d715c382b8f8ebc2e4b865c\nparent c20e20cc6c79201db2d0e1b62292c600c06cbca4\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787541966 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787541966 -0700\n\nfeat: ratings that drift, and a ledger that keeps every answer\n\nv2 phase 2. The tables have been sitting empty in production since 0003;\nthis fills them.\n\nElo''s skeleton with the opponent swapped. There is no player rating —\nwhat we want to learn is how hard a QUESTION is, not how good you are — so\nthe adversary is the field, the set''s mean rating, and a question wins when\nyou miss it. Cards ranked against each other, and still self-correcting:\nmissing one already rated brutal confirms what we knew and moves almost\nnothing, while nailing it is a surprise and drops it hard.\n\nThree knobs. K is confidence, so twenty plays are not overturned by one. M\nis the streak, counting the attempt that extends it — scoring at the\nprevious run length lags by one and a two-attempt streak would never get a\nmultiplier at all. E is the field.\n\nGlobal starts at seedTier; local starts at whatever global says the first\ntime YOU attempt that question. Per question rather than per set, which is\nbetter than the plan''s \"copy everything on first engagement\": a question\nyou have never seen still starts from what global has since learned.\nNothing is materialised — an unrated question sits at a real estimate\ncomputed on read, so playing a set writes no rows until you answer.\n\nA board row stops being a stored tier and becomes a RANK, which is the\nwhole reason a board responds to play. The board is dealt once and never\nre-sorted: re-ranking mid-game would slide tiles from under a thumb\nalready moving toward one. One fact may be asked only once per board, and\nthe claim applies as a column fills — filtering once up front let two\nvariants of one fact into the same column, which the tests caught.\n\nEvery answer goes through one recorder both games call. A mode that forgot\nto record would look completely healthy and teach the system nothing. A\nfailed POST is queued and flushed on the same request as the next answer,\noldest first, so a streak spanning an offline patch is still a streak; the\nqueue is cleared before the send so a failure re-queues once rather than\nduplicating what it held.\n\nSigned-out readers write nothing — no identity to attribute an attempt to,\nand no way to tell one anonymous reader from a thousand. Their board still\nranks by seedTier, exactly as it did before ratings existed.\n\nAlso extracts factRows.ts: two routes now read a stored fact, and a second\ncopy of that would end with two endpoints disagreeing about what questions\na fact asks.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQE/adPWUD+vdIL/b5U/wC9chXqoL5ZVqMtTy16Fog4dDiSIflYl1itC/Vg8xtr/upI\nS2ULJ3AG9U3jPC2IJQwAA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-24T03:26:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/cd16ad657e9cb8ef29513da955dd9e24873f0ad9","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKGNkMTZhZDY1N2U5Y2I4ZWYyOTUxM2RhOTU1ZGQ5ZTI0ODczZjBhZDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/c20e20cc6c79201db2d0e1b62292c600c06cbca4","sha":"c20e20cc6c79201db2d0e1b62292c600c06cbca4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/c20e20cc6c79201db2d0e1b62292c600c06cbca4"}],"sha":"cd16ad657e9cb8ef29513da955dd9e24873f0ad9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/cd16ad657e9cb8ef29513da955dd9e24873f0ad9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/c20e20cc6c79201db2d0e1b62292c600c06cbca4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T03:12:07Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T03:12:07Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"docs: record what phase 1 taught, and stop a summary explaining itself\n\nTwo things production surfaced.\n\nThe set page read \"25 questions from 25 facts\" for the Reformation set,\nwhich is every set imported off v1 — one question per fact, so the second\nhalf is the system explaining its own model rather than telling you\nanything. Say it only when the numbers differ.\n\nAnd the deploy window is structural, not incidental: one hadoku_site\ncommit carries both the lockfile bump that rebuilds the UI and the worker\npackage bump that triggers its deploy, and they run in parallel. Free for\na change that only adds fields; this one renamed `cards` to `facts`, which\nis the kind where the new UI briefly meets the old API. Nobody was looking\nat 03:00, but the next shape change should read tolerantly for a release\nor ship the additive half first.\n\nAlso records the fact model itself, the id-preservation rule, why variants\nare server-derived, and that study-api now applies its own migrations.","tree":{"sha":"900495019cfe79262e22691253bbb17b3cf0cae3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/900495019cfe79262e22691253bbb17b3cf0cae3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/c20e20cc6c79201db2d0e1b62292c600c06cbca4","verification":{"payload":"tree 900495019cfe79262e22691253bbb17b3cf0cae3\nparent 86c7a9ce2a4c44807638379fb2fe98e37b920f87\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787541127 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787541127 -0700\n\ndocs: record what phase 1 taught, and stop a summary explaining itself\n\nTwo things production surfaced.\n\nThe set page read \"25 questions from 25 facts\" for the Reformation set,\nwhich is every set imported off v1 — one question per fact, so the second\nhalf is the system explaining its own model rather than telling you\nanything. Say it only when the numbers differ.\n\nAnd the deploy window is structural, not incidental: one hadoku_site\ncommit carries both the lockfile bump that rebuilds the UI and the worker\npackage bump that triggers its deploy, and they run in parallel. Free for\na change that only adds fields; this one renamed `cards` to `facts`, which\nis the kind where the new UI briefly meets the old API. Nobody was looking\nat 03:00, but the next shape change should read tolerantly for a release\nor ship the additive half first.\n\nAlso records the fact model itself, the id-preservation rule, why variants\nare server-derived, and that study-api now applies its own migrations.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQIYJKBvWlqgkwL9dTPCmf3k8IRRoBPN2FamliODn4ksuLZqnqqwW4QIqXn6iOTTjWq\nGF45UU2kzw2K6cc/D37Qk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-24T03:12:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/c20e20cc6c79201db2d0e1b62292c600c06cbca4","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKGMyMGUyMGNjNmM3OTIwMWRiMmQwZTFiNjIyOTJjNjAwYzA2Y2JjYTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/86c7a9ce2a4c44807638379fb2fe98e37b920f87","sha":"86c7a9ce2a4c44807638379fb2fe98e37b920f87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/86c7a9ce2a4c44807638379fb2fe98e37b920f87"}],"sha":"c20e20cc6c79201db2d0e1b62292c600c06cbca4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/c20e20cc6c79201db2d0e1b62292c600c06cbca4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/86c7a9ce2a4c44807638379fb2fe98e37b920f87/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T03:04:38Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T03:04:38Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat: a fact is the unit of storage, not a question\n\nv2 phase 1. Nothing visibly changes — the board is the same board, the\ndrill is the same drill — and everything underneath is new.\n\nA card fused two things a study set actually has: the thing that is true,\nand the question you ask about it. One row was both, so a set could not\nask \"who met Charles V at Worms in 1521?\" and \"in what year did Luther\nmeet Charles V at Worms?\" without storing Worms and 1521 twice, and there\nwas nowhere to hang a rating that meant anything — a rating on a\nfront/back pair cannot say the year is harder to recall than the place.\n\nNow `slots` holds what is true and a VARIANT is one question over it: pick\na slot to ask, show some of the rest. Front and back are a render, not a\nshape anything is stored in. Dropping givens becomes a difficulty ladder\nnobody declares, since the given set is part of the question''s identity —\n`when<what,where,who>` and `when<where>` rate independently. And \"never\nask two questions about one fact on a board\" stops being a rule anyone\nenforces: it is one claim per fact.\n\nVariants are expanded in the worker, on read, and nowhere else. Their keys\nare what ratings will hang off, and a key computed in two places is a key\nthat eventually disagrees with itself — silently, splitting one question''s\nhistory in two. The client renders what it is handed and builds no keys.\n\nThe response carries both `questions` (authored) and `variants`\n(resolved). Only the first is content: exporting from `variants` alone\nwould bake this build''s fallback phrasings in as though a person wrote\nthem, freezing a template into the set on every round trip.\n\nFacts keep their ids across a save. Saving replaces content wholesale, so\nwithout this every edit would discard a set''s play history — not corrupt\nit, delete it, with no error anywhere. Exports carry the id, PUT hands it\nback, an id from another set is refused.\n\nSlot names are restricted to [A-Za-z0-9_-] because a key is\n`ask<given,given>`: a name holding a delimiter would produce a key that\nreads back as a different question and merge two ratings into one row.\n\nThe editor represents a two-slot flashcard and nothing else. A richer fact\nis shown read-only and passed through byte for byte — flattening one to\nfit two text inputs would destroy authoring silently, on save, in the sets\nwith the most work in them. Editing them properly is phase 3; until then\nthe file is their editor, which works because the export is the import.\n\nRemoves PUT /sets/:id/cards. Nothing called it and PUT /sets/:id does\nstrictly more.\n\nVerified against the real Reformation set: 25 cards migrate to 25 facts,\nexpand to exactly 25 variants rendering the same front and back, and land\nin the identical 25 board cells. 0003 is already applied in production.","tree":{"sha":"f76a618fcf2aeeadbbab19bfc9b8f308f3107c21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/f76a618fcf2aeeadbbab19bfc9b8f308f3107c21"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/86c7a9ce2a4c44807638379fb2fe98e37b920f87","verification":{"payload":"tree f76a618fcf2aeeadbbab19bfc9b8f308f3107c21\nparent 9e595ec0000be958d531cb98d391277049f7bfa3\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787540678 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787540678 -0700\n\nfeat: a fact is the unit of storage, not a question\n\nv2 phase 1. Nothing visibly changes — the board is the same board, the\ndrill is the same drill — and everything underneath is new.\n\nA card fused two things a study set actually has: the thing that is true,\nand the question you ask about it. One row was both, so a set could not\nask \"who met Charles V at Worms in 1521?\" and \"in what year did Luther\nmeet Charles V at Worms?\" without storing Worms and 1521 twice, and there\nwas nowhere to hang a rating that meant anything — a rating on a\nfront/back pair cannot say the year is harder to recall than the place.\n\nNow `slots` holds what is true and a VARIANT is one question over it: pick\na slot to ask, show some of the rest. Front and back are a render, not a\nshape anything is stored in. Dropping givens becomes a difficulty ladder\nnobody declares, since the given set is part of the question''s identity —\n`when<what,where,who>` and `when<where>` rate independently. And \"never\nask two questions about one fact on a board\" stops being a rule anyone\nenforces: it is one claim per fact.\n\nVariants are expanded in the worker, on read, and nowhere else. Their keys\nare what ratings will hang off, and a key computed in two places is a key\nthat eventually disagrees with itself — silently, splitting one question''s\nhistory in two. The client renders what it is handed and builds no keys.\n\nThe response carries both `questions` (authored) and `variants`\n(resolved). Only the first is content: exporting from `variants` alone\nwould bake this build''s fallback phrasings in as though a person wrote\nthem, freezing a template into the set on every round trip.\n\nFacts keep their ids across a save. Saving replaces content wholesale, so\nwithout this every edit would discard a set''s play history — not corrupt\nit, delete it, with no error anywhere. Exports carry the id, PUT hands it\nback, an id from another set is refused.\n\nSlot names are restricted to [A-Za-z0-9_-] because a key is\n`ask<given,given>`: a name holding a delimiter would produce a key that\nreads back as a different question and merge two ratings into one row.\n\nThe editor represents a two-slot flashcard and nothing else. A richer fact\nis shown read-only and passed through byte for byte — flattening one to\nfit two text inputs would destroy authoring silently, on save, in the sets\nwith the most work in them. Editing them properly is phase 3; until then\nthe file is their editor, which works because the export is the import.\n\nRemoves PUT /sets/:id/cards. Nothing called it and PUT /sets/:id does\nstrictly more.\n\nVerified against the real Reformation set: 25 cards migrate to 25 facts,\nexpand to exactly 25 variants rendering the same front and back, and land\nin the identical 25 board cells. 0003 is already applied in production.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQGHgZnFw9p/oWy0dPcKwsFMUqhQRMFvZsUBI8Gz1g0C3dtK8h9JTP2UvxnjyQUMvt0\nTp13K2wTKpScH+JH1M4Ac=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-24T03:04:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/86c7a9ce2a4c44807638379fb2fe98e37b920f87","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKDg2YzdhOWNlMmE0YzQ0ODA3NjM4Mzc5ZmIyZmU5OGUzN2I5MjBmODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/9e595ec0000be958d531cb98d391277049f7bfa3","sha":"9e595ec0000be958d531cb98d391277049f7bfa3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/9e595ec0000be958d531cb98d391277049f7bfa3"}],"sha":"86c7a9ce2a4c44807638379fb2fe98e37b920f87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/86c7a9ce2a4c44807638379fb2fe98e37b920f87"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/9e595ec0000be958d531cb98d391277049f7bfa3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T19:12:55Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T19:12:55Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"docs: record the two things that only production taught us\n\nHANDOFF is the map, and it was missing the two facts that cost the most this\nweek — both of which are invisible locally and will be re-learned the same\nexpensive way otherwise.\n\n- **D1 binds 100 parameters per statement, not SQLite''s 999.** The original\n  constant claimed 999, chunked at 50 rows, and broke every set over 20 cards\n  from launch until the first 25-clue board found it. Written down with the\n  reason INSERT_CHUNK derives rather than being chosen, so the next person to\n  add a column does not silently lower the ceiling again.\n- **Who logs what.** edge-router already records a row per request, so this app\n  logs only what the edge cannot see: failure causes, business events, and the\n  board completion no HTTP log can observe. Says why `apiResponse` is called on\n  the success path only, and records the client telemetry sink as an open\n  decision rather than an oversight.\n\nAlso extends the colours constraint with the accent-as-text rule, which is now\nthe second time that mistake has shipped.","tree":{"sha":"5e9a94c6d8ed8e132534a00e88a3db5d4daa7bc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/5e9a94c6d8ed8e132534a00e88a3db5d4daa7bc3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/9e595ec0000be958d531cb98d391277049f7bfa3","verification":{"payload":"tree 5e9a94c6d8ed8e132534a00e88a3db5d4daa7bc3\nparent 05e83d610662f0ecb8dc2789e0bdba61e61bd0aa\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787512375 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787512375 -0700\n\ndocs: record the two things that only production taught us\n\nHANDOFF is the map, and it was missing the two facts that cost the most this\nweek — both of which are invisible locally and will be re-learned the same\nexpensive way otherwise.\n\n- **D1 binds 100 parameters per statement, not SQLite''s 999.** The original\n  constant claimed 999, chunked at 50 rows, and broke every set over 20 cards\n  from launch until the first 25-clue board found it. Written down with the\n  reason INSERT_CHUNK derives rather than being chosen, so the next person to\n  add a column does not silently lower the ceiling again.\n- **Who logs what.** edge-router already records a row per request, so this app\n  logs only what the edge cannot see: failure causes, business events, and the\n  board completion no HTTP log can observe. Says why `apiResponse` is called on\n  the success path only, and records the client telemetry sink as an open\n  decision rather than an oversight.\n\nAlso extends the colours constraint with the accent-as-text rule, which is now\nthe second time that mistake has shipped.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQKRLvuVWIJJVxAnVlQlvs04Sb0dK2oaP8LiBBIsiVqdCeDxrn6F/iCbADshbOnTWRX\nkXCG3ARfAH/CH1p6p7iQ8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T19:13:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","