oreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T13:03:32Z","email":"github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"message":"chore: auto-update @wolffm/* to latest","tree":{"sha":"f10e0641c47d3bb0c62c38d7d20d17e290ace491","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/f10e0641c47d3bb0c62c38d7d20d17e290ace491"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/05e83d610662f0ecb8dc2789e0bdba61e61bd0aa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/05e83d610662f0ecb8dc2789e0bdba61e61bd0aa","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKDA1ZTgzZDYxMDY2MmYwZWNiOGRjMjc4OWUwYmRiYTYxZTYxYmQwYWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/f885b1ef09b3613387be24ef8da154b9f5174939","sha":"f885b1ef09b3613387be24ef8da154b9f5174939","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/f885b1ef09b3613387be24ef8da154b9f5174939"}],"sha":"05e83d610662f0ecb8dc2789e0bdba61e61bd0aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/05e83d610662f0ecb8dc2789e0bdba61e61bd0aa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/f885b1ef09b3613387be24ef8da154b9f5174939/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T18:01:38Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T18:01:38Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(ui): the board had no padding, no reset, and the wrong tokens\n\nThree separate faults, all visible on the live board at once.\n\n## It sat in a container that strips padding\n\n`[data-fullscreen]` sets `padding: 0` so the drill''s card can own the screen\nedge to edge. Correct for one card; wrong for a grid of tap targets. The board\nhad none of its own, so its outer tiles pressed against the viewport and the\nscore clipped off the right-hand side. It now carries its own padding, a max\nwidth — a 5x5 board stretched across a desktop window becomes a row of\nletterboxes and stops reading as a board — and centres what is left.\n\n## Nothing in this file set box-sizing\n\n`width: 100%` beside padding is the ordinary way to write a full-width block,\nand under content-box it overflows by exactly the padding: 398px of content in\na 390px viewport, a horizontal scrollbar on every phone, and the last column\npushed off-screen. That trap was armed for every component, not just this one,\nso the reset is global rather than a patch on .board. Re-checked the set page,\nthe drill and the clue sheet afterwards — no layout moved.\n\n## The tiles used a tint where they wanted a fill\n\n`--color-primary-bg` is a subtle tint meant for badges. On a board it left the\ntiles reading as empty outlines, in some themes barely separable from the page\nbehind them — which is what the live page actually looked like. They now use\nthe fill pair (`--color-primary` / `--color-on-primary`), checked across four\nthemes: white on blue, black on lavender, black on cyan, black on orange.\n\n## And three accent-as-text mistakes of my own\n\n`.mode__name`, `.board__sheet-val` and `.board__answer-text` set\n`color: var(--color-primary)` on plain card and page surfaces. This file''s own\nheader warns against exactly that — an accent used as text lands unvalidated\nand misses AA in most themes — and the .btn--danger-ghost note records the\nsame lesson. All three take `--color-text` now; weight and size were already\ncarrying the emphasis, and the tile''s border and hover carry the affordance.","tree":{"sha":"6ce64d65734bd180ecfd15c90cfc5976ae830ba4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/6ce64d65734bd180ecfd15c90cfc5976ae830ba4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/f885b1ef09b3613387be24ef8da154b9f5174939","verification":{"payload":"tree 6ce64d65734bd180ecfd15c90cfc5976ae830ba4\nparent ea8a423f376f4e51fc42ade40c8a93436408c953\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787335298 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787335298 -0700\n\nfix(ui): the board had no padding, no reset, and the wrong tokens\n\nThree separate faults, all visible on the live board at once.\n\n## It sat in a container that strips padding\n\n`[data-fullscreen]` sets `padding: 0` so the drill''s card can own the screen\nedge to edge. Correct for one card; wrong for a grid of tap targets. The board\nhad none of its own, so its outer tiles pressed against the viewport and the\nscore clipped off the right-hand side. It now carries its own padding, a max\nwidth — a 5x5 board stretched across a desktop window becomes a row of\nletterboxes and stops reading as a board — and centres what is left.\n\n## Nothing in this file set box-sizing\n\n`width: 100%` beside padding is the ordinary way to write a full-width block,\nand under content-box it overflows by exactly the padding: 398px of content in\na 390px viewport, a horizontal scrollbar on every phone, and the last column\npushed off-screen. That trap was armed for every component, not just this one,\nso the reset is global rather than a patch on .board. Re-checked the set page,\nthe drill and the clue sheet afterwards — no layout moved.\n\n## The tiles used a tint where they wanted a fill\n\n`--color-primary-bg` is a subtle tint meant for badges. On a board it left the\ntiles reading as empty outlines, in some themes barely separable from the page\nbehind them — which is what the live page actually looked like. They now use\nthe fill pair (`--color-primary` / `--color-on-primary`), checked across four\nthemes: white on blue, black on lavender, black on cyan, black on orange.\n\n## And three accent-as-text mistakes of my own\n\n`.mode__name`, `.board__sheet-val` and `.board__answer-text` set\n`color: var(--color-primary)` on plain card and page surfaces. This file''s own\nheader warns against exactly that — an accent used as text lands unvalidated\nand misses AA in most themes — and the .btn--danger-ghost note records the\nsame lesson. All three take `--color-text` now; weight and size were already\ncarrying the emphasis, and the tile''s border and hover carry the affordance.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQI2uR8y4YDnOJntwDQBKU1/M9eMZeQUQfBfjJxnklxWJ9THGehr/wkXAE291iKs959\na8HQg6Pnk9zYmCoVUGGws=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T18:01:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/f885b1ef09b3613387be24ef8da154b9f5174939","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKGY4ODViMWVmMDliMzYxMzM4N2JlMjRlZjhkYTE1NGI5ZjUxNzQ5Mzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/ea8a423f376f4e51fc42ade40c8a93436408c953","sha":"ea8a423f376f4e51fc42ade40c8a93436408c953","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/ea8a423f376f4e51fc42ade40c8a93436408c953"}],"sha":"f885b1ef09b3613387be24ef8da154b9f5174939","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/f885b1ef09b3613387be24ef8da154b9f5174939"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/ea8a423f376f4e51fc42ade40c8a93436408c953/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T17:25:11Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T17:25:11Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(ui): rebuild the set page, and fix the button that could not stack\n\nThe set page read as a wall of identical slabs, and one of them was plainly\nbroken: \"Play as board25 clues · 7500 points\", label and count welded\ntogether with no space.\n\n## The bug\n\n`.btn` never set `display`, so a <button> stayed inline-block and the\n`flex-direction: column` meant to stack that button''s two children did\nnothing at all — they laid out as inline text with no separator. `.btn` is now\ninline-flex, centred, with a gap. Checked the other buttons for regressions:\nthe drill''s grade pair still splits evenly, the board sheet''s actions still\nmatch, and the editor''s remove-card × is still a 44x44 square.\n\n## The layout\n\nThree tiers of weight, where there was one:\n\n- **Modes** are tiles now, not full-width buttons. Choosing how to study is a\n  CHOICE, and two identical slabs gave no way to tell the options apart or to\n  see what either would be like. Each carries a label, a line on what the mode\n  does, and — for the board — its clue count and score.\n- **Export / copy link** drop to text weight. Useful to have; not what anyone\n  came here for.\n- **Owner actions** stay grouped under a rule, subordinate to both.\n\nThe title also went back up to the size it was: I had swapped it to\n--hdk-text-lg, which is the largest type token at 24px and too close to body\ncopy for the one thing on the page that should dominate.\n\n## Games describe themselves\n\n`GameDefinition` gains `blurb` (static: what this mode IS) alongside the\nexisting dynamic `availability().summary` (what THIS set is in it), and an\noptional `Preview` component. The board supplies a miniature of its own grid,\nso a full 5x5 and a half-empty one are visibly different propositions — which\na clue count cannot express. The set page renders whatever a game hands it and\nstill knows nothing about grids. A test pins that every game has both strings,\nsince a game shipping without a blurb renders as a bare verb beside a\ndescribed one.\n\nEvery colour is a theme token; verified light and dark, phone and desktop.","tree":{"sha":"7cdd9f51c4ada9070041ea0bd0c2cf7c9b0280a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/7cdd9f51c4ada9070041ea0bd0c2cf7c9b0280a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/ea8a423f376f4e51fc42ade40c8a93436408c953","verification":{"payload":"tree 7cdd9f51c4ada9070041ea0bd0c2cf7c9b0280a7\nparent 8242f0dbe5e7f6bb68f605fd71f7758584f033c4\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787333111 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787333111 -0700\n\nfix(ui): rebuild the set page, and fix the button that could not stack\n\nThe set page read as a wall of identical slabs, and one of them was plainly\nbroken: \"Play as board25 clues · 7500 points\", label and count welded\ntogether with no space.\n\n## The bug\n\n`.btn` never set `display`, so a <button> stayed inline-block and the\n`flex-direction: column` meant to stack that button''s two children did\nnothing at all — they laid out as inline text with no separator. `.btn` is now\ninline-flex, centred, with a gap. Checked the other buttons for regressions:\nthe drill''s grade pair still splits evenly, the board sheet''s actions still\nmatch, and the editor''s remove-card × is still a 44x44 square.\n\n## The layout\n\nThree tiers of weight, where there was one:\n\n- **Modes** are tiles now, not full-width buttons. Choosing how to study is a\n  CHOICE, and two identical slabs gave no way to tell the options apart or to\n  see what either would be like. Each carries a label, a line on what the mode\n  does, and — for the board — its clue count and score.\n- **Export / copy link** drop to text weight. Useful to have; not what anyone\n  came here for.\n- **Owner actions** stay grouped under a rule, subordinate to both.\n\nThe title also went back up to the size it was: I had swapped it to\n--hdk-text-lg, which is the largest type token at 24px and too close to body\ncopy for the one thing on the page that should dominate.\n\n## Games describe themselves\n\n`GameDefinition` gains `blurb` (static: what this mode IS) alongside the\nexisting dynamic `availability().summary` (what THIS set is in it), and an\noptional `Preview` component. The board supplies a miniature of its own grid,\nso a full 5x5 and a half-empty one are visibly different propositions — which\na clue count cannot express. The set page renders whatever a game hands it and\nstill knows nothing about grids. A test pins that every game has both strings,\nsince a game shipping without a blurb renders as a bare verb beside a\ndescribed one.\n\nEvery colour is a theme token; verified light and dark, phone and desktop.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQPhHrHHA+2KKbSWHr6EbKh3qK3g0x+VHcd/57goqdEKcYnxPAk8xKHou23ycj83bmb\naneRYaNVon4hjQvfiTQg8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T17:25:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/ea8a423f376f4e51fc42ade40c8a93436408c953","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKGVhOGE0MjNmMzc2ZjRlNTFmYzQyYWRlNDBjOGE5MzQzNjQwOGM5NTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/8242f0dbe5e7f6bb68f605fd71f7758584f033c4","sha":"8242f0dbe5