fbb6321dc3e67385bf1f77142829"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/8242f0dbe5e7f6bb68f605fd71f7758584f033c4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/8242f0dbe5e7f6bb68f605fd71f7758584f033c4","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKDgyNDJmMGRiZTVlN2Y2YmI2OGY2MDVmZDcxZjc3NTg1ODRmMDMzYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/167938b482e52791f0bc57b9474ed1820305d225","sha":"167938b482e52791f0bc57b9474ed1820305d225","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/167938b482e52791f0bc57b9474ed1820305d225"}],"sha":"8242f0dbe5e7f6bb68f605fd71f7758584f033c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/8242f0dbe5e7f6bb68f605fd71f7758584f033c4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/167938b482e52791f0bc57b9474ed1820305d225/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T05:39:54Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T05:39:54Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat: log what the edge cannot see, on both sides of the API\n\nThe worker logged nothing at all and the UI logged two lines, so the only\nrecord of a study action was edge-router''s request row. That row says\n`POST /study/api/sets 500`; it cannot say WHY, and it cannot say what the\nrequest did.\n\n## Worker\n\nA study-named logger (not worker-utils'' generic `worker` default, which makes\nevery entry indistinguishable from every other worker''s) emitting exactly the\ntwo things the edge cannot observe from outside:\n\n- The cause of a failure. `createErrorHandlers` console.errors the raw error —\n  captured by Cloudflare, but unstructured and outside the pipeline, so it\n  cannot be queried next to the request row it belongs to. That gap is what\n  made today''s D1 parameter-limit bug cost a bisection against production when\n  the underlying error names the problem outright.\n- Business events: set created / replaced / updated / deleted / cards\n  replaced, each with a deck summary. Counts, never content — a log line is no\n  place for someone''s cards, and the questions worth asking are about size and\n  shape. `boardClues` and `games` make \"how many sets are actually playable,\n  and as what\" answerable without reading D1.\n\nDeliberately NOT re-logging method/path/status/duration: edge-router already\nrecords those, and duplicating them doubles volume for nothing.\n\n## UI\n\nUses the logger''s own helpers instead of hand-rolled strings — `component()`\nfor mount/unmount, `apiRequest`/`apiResponse` around every call, `preference()`\nfor a settings change — so these land as typed events rather than as text\nsomeone has to grep.\n\nThe failure path is the real gain. Every caller turned a rejection into a\nmessage on screen and nothing else, so a 500 left no trace in the browser at\nall. Now a network failure, a non-JSON body and an error status each log once,\nwith method, path, status, duration and the server''s message.\n\n`apiResponse` is called only for successes, because the helper escalates every\nnon-2xx to ERROR: a 404 is the DESIGNED answer for a private set and a 403 for\na signed-out writer, and routing those through it logged one event twice at\ntwo different levels. Verified in a browser against production — a missing set\nnow produces a single WARN carrying \"Set not found\".\n\nA completed board emits `study.board.completed`. It is the one action no HTTP\nlog can ever see, because the whole game runs client-side once the set is\nfetched.","tree":{"sha":"e0265a2cf132be60db98698cab0e9f0382bfc17b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/e0265a2cf132be60db98698cab0e9f0382bfc17b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/167938b482e52791f0bc57b9474ed1820305d225","verification":{"payload":"tree e0265a2cf132be60db98698cab0e9f0382bfc17b\nparent 6ec0b12668f7bb7d6838cf9be377baf0a786e3c8\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787290794 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787290794 -0700\n\nfeat: log what the edge cannot see, on both sides of the API\n\nThe worker logged nothing at all and the UI logged two lines, so the only\nrecord of a study action was edge-router''s request row. That row says\n`POST /study/api/sets 500`; it cannot say WHY, and it cannot say what the\nrequest did.\n\n## Worker\n\nA study-named logger (not worker-utils'' generic `worker` default, which makes\nevery entry indistinguishable from every other worker''s) emitting exactly the\ntwo things the edge cannot observe from outside:\n\n- The cause of a failure. `createErrorHandlers` console.errors the raw error —\n  captured by Cloudflare, but unstructured and outside the pipeline, so it\n  cannot be queried next to the request row it belongs to. That gap is what\n  made today''s D1 parameter-limit bug cost a bisection against production when\n  the underlying error names the problem outright.\n- Business events: set created / replaced / updated / deleted / cards\n  replaced, each with a deck summary. Counts, never content — a log line is no\n  place for someone''s cards, and the questions worth asking are about size and\n  shape. `boardClues` and `games` make \"how many sets are actually playable,\n  and as what\" answerable without reading D1.\n\nDeliberately NOT re-logging method/path/status/duration: edge-router already\nrecords those, and duplicating them doubles volume for nothing.\n\n## UI\n\nUses the logger''s own helpers instead of hand-rolled strings — `component()`\nfor mount/unmount, `apiRequest`/`apiResponse` around every call, `preference()`\nfor a settings change — so these land as typed events rather than as text\nsomeone has to grep.\n\nThe failure path is the real gain. Every caller turned a rejection into a\nmessage on screen and nothing else, so a 500 left no trace in the browser at\nall. Now a network failure, a non-JSON body and an error status each log once,\nwith method, path, status, duration and the server''s message.\n\n`apiResponse` is called only for successes, because the helper escalates every\nnon-2xx to ERROR: a 404 is the DESIGNED answer for a private set and a 403 for\na signed-out writer, and routing those through it logged one event twice at\ntwo different levels. Verified in a browser against production — a missing set\nnow produces a single WARN carrying \"Set not found\".\n\nA completed board emits `study.board.completed`. It is the one action no HTTP\nlog can ever see, because the whole game runs client-side once the set is\nfetched.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQEZHBh+yMzdjd1BnhznPMsrhDybtFTsOuf5uu1rG2Z1+OKf2oHnhRTP66R6zGqf/Fu\nHB5FyqNb2cPxvUgvvAFQU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T05:40:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/167938b482e52791f0bc57b9474ed1820305d225","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKDE2NzkzOGI0ODJlNTI3OTFmMGJjNTdiOTQ3NGVkMTgyMDMwNWQyMjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/6ec0b12668f7bb7d6838cf9be377baf0a786e3c8","sha":"6ec0b12668f7bb7d6838cf9be377baf0a786e3c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/6ec0b12668f7bb7d6838cf9be377baf0a786e3c8"}],"sha":"167938b482e52791f0bc57b9474ed1820305d225","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/167938b482e52791f0bc57b9474ed1820305d225"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/6ec0b12668f7bb7d6838cf9be377baf0a786e3c8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T05:24:11Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T05:24:11Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(worker): create a set and its cards in one transaction\n\nPOST /sets wrote the set row, then the cards, as two awaited statements. When\nthe card write failed the set survived — an empty, titled set the owner had to\nfind and delete by hand.\n\nThat is not hypothetical: every import over 14 cards 500d against D1''s\nparameter ceiling today, and each attempt left one behind. Five of them had to\nbe swept up manually.\n\nBoth now go in a single D1 batch, which runs in an implicit transaction, so a\ncreate lands whole or not at all. It is the same rule the card replacement\nalready followed and said so in a comment — the create path just never got it.","tree":{"sha":"a0ec6db6f4950b6bf51b6daa6db523b9ccb0d718","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/a0ec6db6f4950b6bf51b6daa6db523b9ccb0d718"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/6ec0b12668f7bb7d6838cf9be377baf0a786e3c8","verification":{"payload":"tree a0ec6db6f4950b6bf51b6daa6db523b9ccb0d718\nparent f0bd62388045e07d84ab4cf2effc89c65fb58289\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787289851 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787289851 -0700\n\nfix(worker): create a set and its cards in one transaction\n\nPOST /sets wrote the set row, then the cards, as two awaited statements. When\nthe card write failed the set survived — an empty, titled set the owner had to\nfind and delete by hand.\n\nThat is not hypothetical: every import over 14 cards 500d against D1''s\nparameter ceiling today, and each attempt left one behind. Five of them had to\nbe swept up manually.\n\nBoth now go in a single D1 batch, which runs in an implicit transaction, so a\ncreate lands whole or not at all. It is the same rule the card replacement\nalready followed and said so in a comment — the create path just never got it.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQGo2ru2+E5VEQ5wBqHGMlmxzxEsSmDLTLFCV/wDRZTPNK953I+4m3767sqI8GhJVS/\niLgQKYkvWGBmquv9Nd4AA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T05:24:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/6ec0b12668f7bb7d6838cf9be377baf0a786e3c8","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKDZlYzBiMTI2NjhmN2JiN2Q2ODM4Y2Y5YmUzNzdiYWYwYTc4NmUzYzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/f0bd62388045e07d84ab4cf2effc89c65fb58289","sha":"f0bd62388045e07d84ab4cf2effc89c65fb58289","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/f0bd62388045e07d84ab4cf2effc89c65fb58289"}],"sha":"6ec0b12668f7bb7d6838cf9be377baf0a786e3c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/6ec0b12668f7bb7d6838cf9be377baf0a786e3c8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/f0bd62388045e07d84ab4cf2effc89c65fb58289/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T05:22:29Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T05:22:29Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(worker): chunk card inserts to D1''s parameter limit, not SQLite''s\n\nImporting a 25-clue board 500d on every attempt. D1 caps bound parameters at\n100 per statement; this file claimed SQLite''s 999 and chunked at 50 rows.\n\nThe bug shipped at launch and hid. With the five columns `cards` had then the\nbreak was at 20 cards, and nothing in the system was that big — the gallery\nwas empty. Adding `detail` and `attrs` took each row to seven parameters,\nwhich moved the break to 14, and the first real board walked into it. Verified\nagainst production: 14 cards (98 params) creates, 15 (105) returns 500.\n\nINSERT_CHUNK now DERIVES from the limit rather than being chosen, because a\nhand-picked constant has to be revisited by whoever next adds a column and\ngives no signal when they forget. sets.chunking.test.ts pins the arithmetic —\nthe chunk fits the ceiling, uses it fully, and keeps a 500-card set to a sane\nstatement count.\n\nFound only by writing a real set through the deployed API. Every unit test\npassed throughout, because the limit belongs to D1 and nothing local knows it.","tree":{"sha":"b34a9574f263b9a86f30e3604555704e80979e8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/b34a9574f263b9a86f30e3604555704e80979e8b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/f0bd62388045e07d84ab4cf2effc89c65fb58289","verification":{"payload":"tree b34a9574f263b9a86f30e3604555704e80979e8b\nparent f4093b6ddaa1aa53f9aeb6f50b156dcd18d0f90a\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787289749 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787289749 -0700\n\nfix(worker): chunk card inserts to D1''s parameter limit, not SQLite''s\n\nImporting a 25-clue board 500d on every attempt. D1 caps bound parameters at\n100 per statement; this file claimed SQLite''s 999 and chunked at 50 rows.\n\nThe bug shipped at launch and hid. With the five columns `cards` had then the\nbreak was at 20 cards, and nothing in the system was that big — the gallery\nwas empty. Adding `detail` and `attrs` took each row to seven parameters,\nwhich moved the break to 14, and the first real board walked into it. Verified\nagainst production: 14 cards (98 params) creates, 15 (105) returns 500.\n\nINSERT_CHUNK now DERIVES from the limit rather than being chosen, because a\nhand-picked constant has to be revisited by whoever next adds a column and\ngives no signal when they forget. sets.chunking.test.ts pins the arithmetic —\nthe chunk fits the ceiling, uses it fully, and keeps a 500-card set to a sane\nstatement count.\n\nFound only by writing a real set through the deployed API. Every unit test\npassed throughout, because the limit belongs to D1 and nothing local knows it.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQFh9Fc6r2yh5aZfWwQ9naJLECAtin5rVXG2me+bouW/6o2Q2CjDXYiFw1hHHJCXCD4\neZbzhTtnJH8jQDeh6xHwg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T05:22:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/f0bd62388045e07d84ab4cf2effc89c65fb58289","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKGYwYmQ2MjM4ODA0NWUwN2Q4NGFiNGNmMmVmZmM4OWM2NWZiNTgyODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/f4093b6ddaa1aa53f9aeb6f50b156dcd18d0f90a","sha":"f4093b6ddaa1aa53f9aeb6f50b156dcd18d0f90a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/f4093b6ddaa1aa53f9aeb6f50b156dcd18d0f90a"}],"sha":"f0bd62388045e07d84ab4cf2effc89c65fb58289","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/f0bd62388045e07d84ab4cf2effc89c65fb58289"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/f4093b6ddaa1aa53f9aeb6f50b156dcd18d0f90a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T05:17:27Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T05:17:27Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"chore(devvault): declare study''s identity mapping\n\nMints nothing by itself — the key (`study-service-key`, vault item\nKEY_SERVICE_STUDY, registry tier service, associated to WolffM/hadoku-study)\nwas created through the mgmt-api lifecycle broker, which writes both stores and\nverifies they agree. This file is the half that belongs in the repo: the env\nvar → vault key mapping that ../hadoku_site/scripts/secrets/dev-vault.mjs reads\nfrom cwd. No secrets here; the caller key lives in .devvault.local.json, which\nis gitignored and mode 0600.\n\nDeliberately ONE entry. ACL rows are granted FROM this file, so every mapping\nadded is read access granted. study-api itself needs nothing here — it\nauthenticates end users via X-User-Key/X-Session-Id resolved by edge-router, and\nits only Cloudflare binding is the shared EDGE_AUTH_SECRET pushed from\nhadoku_site''s update_cloudflare_secrets config. This credential is for study\ncalling other hadoku services AS ITSELF, and for commands run from this repo.","tree":{"sha":"b1a129a2d36476abd091cab59e5710897cb1f3d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/b1a129a2d36476abd091cab59e5710897cb1f3d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/f4093b6ddaa1aa53f9aeb6f50b156dcd18d0f90a","verification":{"payload":"tree b1a129a2d36476abd091cab59e5710897cb1f3d5\nparent bfcedcb049f07da8c1b88b310899fd4f5593c7dc\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787289447 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787289447 -0700\n\nchore(devvault): declare study''s identity mapping\n\nMints nothing by itself — the key (`study-service-key`, vault item\nKEY_SERVICE_STUDY, registry tier service, associated to WolffM/hadoku-study)\nwas created through the mgmt-api lifecycle broker, which writes both stores and\nverifies they agree. This file is the half that belongs in the repo: the env\nvar → vault key mapping that ../hadoku_site/scripts/secrets/dev-vault.mjs reads\nfrom cwd. No secrets here; the caller key lives in .devvault.local.json, which\nis gitignored and mode 0600.\n\nDeliberately ONE entry. ACL rows are granted FROM this file, so every mapping\nadded is read access granted. study-api itself needs nothing here — it\nauthenticates end users via X-User-Key/X-Session-Id resolved by edge-router, and\nits only Cloudflare binding is the shared EDGE_AUTH_SECRET pushed from\nhadoku_site''s update_cloudflare_secrets config. This credential is for study\ncalling other hadoku services AS ITSELF, and for commands run from this repo.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQPIiYmhXRmaqemOSNc+/XuPtwvZiX794ONw+/HjprLMHbT4faNbaobTm81FMECYm25\nEf7Y3hU/ickIWrcsqirQs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T05:17:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/f4093b6ddaa1aa53f9aeb6f50b156dcd18d0f90a","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKGY0MDkzYjZkZGFhMWFhNTNmOWFlYjZmNTBiMTU2ZGNkMThkMGY5MGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/bfcedcb049f07da8c1b88b310899fd4f5593c7dc","sha":"bfcedcb049f07da8c1b88b310899fd4f5593c7dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/bfcedcb049f07da8c1b88b310899fd4f5593c7dc"}],"sha":"f4093b6ddaa1aa53f9aeb6f50b156dcd18d0f90a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/f4093b6ddaa1aa53f9aeb6f50b156dcd18d0f90a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/bfcedcb049f07da8c1b88b310899fd4f5593c7dc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T05:00:22Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T05:00:22Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat: play a set as a game, and leave room for more of them\n\nAdds a Jeopardy-style board — but the point is the seam it arrives through,\nso the next game needs no migration and no edits outside its own directory.\n\n## Games are registered, not special-cased\n\n`src/games/registry.ts` lists every playable mode; the drill is one entry and\nthe board is another. The set page walks that list, asks each game whether\nthis set can be played, and renders a button for the ones that say yes. It\ndoes not know what a board is. Adding a mode is a directory under `src/games/`\nand one registry entry.\n\nA game''s id is three things at once, deliberately: its key in a card''s attrs\nbag, its value in `?play=`, and its identity in the registry. One name, so\nthere is nowhere for the three to drift apart. An unknown id resolves to the\nset page rather than a blank screen, so a link to a retired game still lands.\n\n## Cards carry a bag, not a column per game\n\nTwo columns, doing different jobs:\n\n- `detail` is a real column because it is CROSS-CUTTING — the drill, the board\n  and every quiz mode sketched so far want an explanation after the answer.\n  A field every mode uses belongs in the schema, typed and in the spec.\n- `attrs` is JSON namespaced by game: {\"board\": {\"category\", \"difficulty\"}}.\n\nThe namespace is the point: two games that both want `difficulty` collide in a\nflat bag, and resolving that later is the migration this column exists to\navoid. Known namespaces stay fully typed in zod and published in the spec, so\nan agent still reads a real schema. Unknown ones round-trip untouched through\nthe API, the file format and the editor — a game can be prototyped entirely\nclient-side before the server knows it exists. That is also why attrs is\nsize-capped in the schema: passing unknown keys through unvalidated is exactly\nwhat makes an unbounded blob store possible without one.\n\nThe editor preserves other games'' namespaces on save, because editing a card\nin one mode must not quietly delete another mode''s data.\n\n## Playability is derived, never stored\n\nA set whose cards carry attrs.board can be played as a board. No `mode` column\non sets — that would be a second answer to a question the cards already\nanswer, free to drift out of step with them.\n\nThe asymmetry runs one way: every board is already a deck, because a clue is a\ncard with a front and a back, so the drill plays a board unchanged. A deck\nbecomes a board only once someone has done the authoring. Half-tagged sets are\ntherefore normal — untagged cards stay in the deck, sit off the grid, and the\neditor reports what is missing rather than enforcing a silent threshold.\n\nEach game validates its own namespace on read, since the bag passes anything\nthrough: a card that cannot be read is simply not a clue and must never take\nthe board down.\n\n## The board is phone-first\n\nMeasured on a 390x844 viewport, not eyeballed: 25 tiles at 73x48 — past the\n44px tap minimum — the whole board inside 341px, no sideways scroll.\n\n- A tile shows only its points, which is what lets 25 targets fit; the\n  category names carry the meaning once, along the top.\n- The clue opens as a full-screen sheet, not an inline panel that would put\n  the answer below the fold on a phone.\n- Actions are pinned to the bottom, so revealing grows content ABOVE them.\n  Verified they hold to the pixel across a reveal — the flip card''s rule, for\n  the flip card''s reason.\n- Wider screens get larger tiles and a centred dialog.\n\nScoring matches the honor-system original: correct adds its tier value, a miss\nadds nothing, 25 clues cap at 7500.\n\nEvery colour is a @wolffm/themes token; filled tiles take their text from the\nmatching --color-on-* so they stay legible in every theme.\n\nNeeds 0002_card_attrs.sql applied to study-db before this deploys.","tree":{"sha":"5d4a9c328d8e7c988eea898d0224e41f8d41e238","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/5d4a9c328d8e7c988eea898d0224e41f8d41e238"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/bfcedcb049f07da8c1b88b310899fd4f5593c7dc","verification":{"payload":"tree 5d4a9c328d8e7c988eea898d0224e41f8d41e238\nparent 66da0f63b3cef9a2e2dda4cbaabf8bc3f334a07e\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787288422 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787288422 -0700\n\nfeat: play a set as a game, and leave room for more of them\n\nAdds a Jeopardy-style board — but the point is the seam it arrives through,\nso the next game needs no migration and no edits outside its own directory.\n\n## Games are registered, not special-cased\n\n`src/games/registry.ts` lists every playable mode; the drill is one entry and\nthe board is another. The set page walks that list, asks each game whether\nthis set can be played, and renders a button for the ones that say yes. It\ndoes not know what a board is. Adding a mode is a directory under `src/games/`\nand one registry entry.\n\nA game''s id is three things at once, deliberately: its key in a card''s attrs\nbag, its value in `?play=`, and its identity in the registry. One name, so\nthere is nowhere for the three to drift apart. An unknown id resolves to the\nset page rather than a blank screen, so a link to a retired game still lands.\n\n## Cards carry a bag, not a column per game\n\nTwo columns, doing different jobs:\n\n- `detail` is a real column because it is CROSS-CUTTING — the drill, the board\n  and every quiz mode sketched so far want an explanation after the answer.\n  A field every mode uses belongs in the schema, typed and in the spec.\n- `attrs` is JSON namespaced by game: {\"board\": {\"category\", \"difficulty\"}}.\n\nThe namespace is the point: two games that both want `difficulty` collide in a\nflat bag, and resolving that later is the migration this column exists to\navoid. Known namespaces stay fully typed in zod and published in the spec, so\nan agent still reads a real schema. Unknown ones round-trip untouched through\nthe API, the file format and the editor — a game can be prototyped entirely\nclient-side before the server knows it exists. That is also why attrs is\nsize-capped in the schema: passing unknown keys through unvalidated is exactly\nwhat makes an unbounded blob store possible without one.\n\nThe editor preserves other games'' namespaces on save, because editing a card\nin one mode must not quietly delete another mode''s data.\n\n## Playability is derived, never stored\n\nA set whose cards carry attrs.board can be played as a board. No `mode` column\non sets — that would be a second answer to a question the cards already\nanswer, free to drift out of step with them.\n\nThe asymmetry runs one way: every board is already a deck, because a clue is a\ncard with a front and a back, so the drill plays a board unchanged. A deck\nbecomes a board only once someone has done the authoring. Half-tagged sets are\ntherefore normal — untagged cards stay in the deck, sit off the grid, and the\neditor reports what is missing rather than enforcing a silent threshold.\n\nEach game validates its own namespace on read, since the bag passes anything\nthrough: a card that cannot be read is simply not a clue and must never take\nthe board down.\n\n## The board is phone-first\n\nMeasured on a 390x844 viewport, not eyeballed: 25 tiles at 73x48 — past the\n44px tap minimum — the whole board inside 341px, no sideways scroll.\n\n- A tile shows only its points, which is what lets 25 targets fit; the\n  category names carry the meaning once, along the top.\n- The clue opens as a full-screen sheet, not an inline panel that would put\n  the answer below the fold on a phone.\n- Actions are pinned to the bottom, so revealing grows content ABOVE them.\n  Verified they hold to the pixel across a reveal — the flip card''s rule, for\n  the flip card''s reason.\n- Wider screens get larger tiles and a centred dialog.\n\nScoring matches the honor-system original: correct adds its tier value, a miss\nadds nothing, 25 clues cap at 7500.\n\nEvery colour is a @wolffm/themes token; filled tiles take their text from the\nmatching --color-on-* so they stay legible in every theme.\n\nNeeds 0002_card_attrs.sql applied to study-db before this deploys.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQCZTfTwmrRGjGG0a19Yu86F5A6fwD8d14GiFn2HZtI/m5Hli69+1mjz0rRigbcbILT\n837m4q9u3f9L6ReRUbhw0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T05:03:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/bfcedcb049f07da8c1b88b310899fd4f5593c7dc","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKGJmY2VkY2IwNDlmMDdkYThjMWI4OGIzMTA4OTlmZDRmNTU5M2M3ZGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/66da0f63b3cef9a2e2dda4cbaabf8bc3f334a07e","sha":"66da0f63b3cef9a2e2dda4cbaabf8bc3f334a07e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/66da0f63b3cef9a2e2dda4cbaabf8bc3f334a07e"}],"sha":"bfcedcb049f07da8c1b88b310899fd4f5593c7dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/bfcedcb049f07da8c1b88b310899fd4f5593c7dc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/66da0f63b3cef9a2e2dda4cbaabf8bc3f334a07e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T20:16:58Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T20:17:57Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat: make sets portable as one file, and the OpenAPI spec usable by agents\n\n## The spec was not consumable\n\nTwo defects at /study/api/openapi.json, both live since the app shipped, and\nneither breaks anything until someone trusts the document:\n\n- servers[].url was https://hadoku.me/study/api while every path ALSO began\n  /study/api, so a generated client requested /study/api/study/api/... and\n  404d on its first call. The server URL is now the origin only.\n- components.securitySchemes was empty, so nothing in the spec said how to\n  authenticate — while every write is friend+. X-User-Key and X-Session-Id\n  are now declared and attached per operation, with an empty requirement on\n  the operations genuinely readable signed-out.\n\nspec.test.ts asserts both rather than leaving them to break again silently.\nThis is also why there is no MCP server: an MCP for one app would be a second\nauth path wrapping the same eleven endpoints, and the fleet-level version of\nthat idea would be built on these specs anyway.\n\n## A set is a single file\n\nThe format is not a new schema — it is a subset of what GET /sets/:id already\nreturns, and it round-trips because zod strips unknown keys instead of\nrejecting them, so an exported set imports verbatim, server-owned fields and\nall. schemas.test.ts pins that property, which is otherwise a silent default\none .strict() away from breaking.\n\n- POST /sets takes `published`, so importing a public set is one request.\n- PUT /sets/:id replaces a whole set — metadata and every card in ONE D1\n  batch, so an import cannot land the new title against the old deck.\n  Omitting `published` leaves visibility alone: a file describes content, and\n  must not be able to silently unshare a set.\n\nIn the app, Export file is on every set you can read — including someone\nelse''s published set, whose cards you can already see — and the editor''s\nImport a file takes that document back, plus a raw API envelope, a bare JSON\narray, or a tab/comma paste out of a spreadsheet. One parser, because from\nthe outside they are all the same gesture.\n\nSaving an existing set is now that single PUT instead of PATCH → card PUT →\nre-GET: three round trips on a phone, with a window in which the set had the\nnew title and the old deck.\n\n## Also\n\n- vitest in both packages, wired into `pnpm check` (27 tests).\n- `pnpm dev` proxies /study/api to production; without it the dev harness\n  could not reach the API at all and every view rendered its error state.\n- Drop an unreachable card-count check in PUT /sets/:id/cards — the zod\n  schema caps the array first, so the manual branch could never run.","tree":{"sha":"873403048e86495f139a7d78a52930a51510aba0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/873403048e86495f139a7d78a52930a51510aba0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/66da0f63b3cef9a2e2dda4cbaabf8bc3f334a07e","verification":{"payload":"tree 873403048e86495f139a7d78a52930a51510aba0\nparent 180b4c476d9b477f35629004f8f54034b31b2101\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787170618 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787170677 -0700\n\nfeat: make sets portable as one file, and the OpenAPI spec usable by agents\n\n## The spec was not consumable\n\nTwo defects at /study/api/openapi.json, both live since the app shipped, and\nneither breaks anything until someone trusts the document:\n\n- servers[].url was https://hadoku.me/study/api while every path ALSO began\n  /study/api, so a generated client requested /study/api/study/api/... and\n  404d on its first call. The server URL is now the origin only.\n- components.securitySchemes was empty, so nothing in the spec said how to\n  authenticate — while every write is friend+. X-User-Key and X-Session-Id\n  are now declared and attached per operation, with an empty requirement on\n  the operations genuinely readable signed-out.\n\nspec.test.ts asserts both rather than leaving them to break again silently.\nThis is also why there is no MCP server: an MCP for one app would be a second\nauth path wrapping the same eleven endpoints, and the fleet-level version of\nthat idea would be built on these specs anyway.\n\n## A set is a single file\n\nThe format is not a new schema — it is a subset of what GET /sets/:id already\nreturns, and it round-trips because zod strips unknown keys instead of\nrejecting them, so an exported set imports verbatim, server-owned fields and\nall. schemas.test.ts pins that property, which is otherwise a silent default\none .strict() away from breaking.\n\n- POST /sets takes `published`, so importing a public set is one request.\n- PUT /sets/:id replaces a whole set — metadata and every card in ONE D1\n  batch, so an import cannot land the new title against the old deck.\n  Omitting `published` leaves visibility alone: a file describes content, and\n  must not be able to silently unshare a set.\n\nIn the app, Export file is on every set you can read — including someone\nelse''s published set, whose cards you can already see — and the editor''s\nImport a file takes that document back, plus a raw API envelope, a bare JSON\narray, or a tab/comma paste out of a spreadsheet. One parser, because from\nthe outside they are all the same gesture.\n\nSaving an existing set is now that single PUT instead of PATCH → card PUT →\nre-GET: three round trips on a phone, with a window in which the set had the\nnew title and the old deck.\n\n## Also\n\n- vitest in both packages, wired into `pnpm check` (27 tests).\n- `pnpm dev` proxies /study/api to production; without it the dev harness\n  could not reach the API at all and every view rendered its error state.\n- Drop an unreachable card-count check in PUT /sets/:id/cards — the zod\n  schema caps the array first, so the manual branch could never run.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJYMPFhUj5+aDwiQkOTmgbCwIhQo71iHhhDTeod8xG0ZqIgeLkaOADg/Xr3S3Gh7ZL\nWT040fj248l1Eh6WWKDwY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T20:18:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/66da0f63b3cef9a2e2dda4cbaabf8bc3f334a07e","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKDY2ZGEwZjYzYjNjZWY5YTJlMmRkYTRjYmFhYmY4YmMzZjMzNGEwN2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/180b4c476d9b477f35629004f8f54034b31b2101","sha":"180b4c476d9b477f35629004f8f54034b31b2101","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/180b4c476d9b477f35629004f8f54034b31b2101"}],"sha":"66da0f63b3cef9a2e2dda4cbaabf8bc3f334a07e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/66da0f63b3cef9a2e2dda4cbaabf8bc3f334a07e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/180b4c476d9b477f35629004f8f54034b31b2101/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T19:17:26Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T19:17:26Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"ci: authenticate npm installs with HADOKU_NPM_READ_TOKEN\n\nHADOKU_SITE_TOKEN carries repo + workflow — on a classic PAT that is read AND\nWRITE across every repo the account can see. It was presented to\nnpm.pkg.github.com purely to install @wolffm packages, so a leak of it was an\naccount compromise rather than a nuisance.\n\nHADOKU_NPM_READ_TOKEN can only read packages. It is already seeded on this repo\n(22 repos, 44/44 verified) and its rotation entry enforces a scope CEILING, so it\ncannot silently regain write access at the next mint.\n\nOnly npm-auth references moved. Anything that pushes, checks out, or dispatches\nstill uses HADOKU_SITE_TOKEN and still needs repo scope.","tree":{"sha":"c1950ec28eb9aa60aa39c9db0494ee3d402b125c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/c1950ec28eb9aa60aa39c9db0494ee3d402b125c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/180b4c476d9b477f35629004f8f54034b31b2101","verification":{"payload":"tree c1950ec28eb9aa60aa39c9db0494ee3d402b125c\nparent 340fd4b336087c4999f12f9bab79f06770331589\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787167046 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787167046 -0700\n\nci: authenticate npm installs with HADOKU_NPM_READ_TOKEN\n\nHADOKU_SITE_TOKEN carries repo + workflow — on a classic PAT that is read AND\nWRITE across every repo the account can see. It was presented to\nnpm.pkg.github.com purely to install @wolffm packages, so a leak of it was an\naccount compromise rather than a nuisance.\n\nHADOKU_NPM_READ_TOKEN can only read packages. It is already seeded on this repo\n(22 repos, 44/44 verified) and its rotation entry enforces a scope CEILING, so it\ncannot silently regain write access at the next mint.\n\nOnly npm-auth references moved. Anything that pushes, checks out, or dispatches\nstill uses HADOKU_SITE_TOKEN and still needs repo scope.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQL+ILmI8nMjpG9Js59hAeqcXhXxpCNSY5qOarQKt5O70GcLSg3+Y0q/Xo4UxQDXQyw\nHexh/HuIaPqWXQtBXnFwc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T19:17:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/180b4c476d9b477f35629004f8f54034b31b2101","node_id":"C_kwDOT7-redoAKDE4MGI0YzQ3NmQ5YjQ3N2YzNTYyOTAwNGY4ZjU0MDM0YjMxYjIxMDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-study/commit/340fd4b336087c4999f12f9bab79f06770331589","sha":"340fd4b336087c4999f12f9bab79f06770331589","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/340fd4b336087c4999f12f9bab79f06770331589"}],"sha":"180b4c476d9b477f35629004f8f54034b31b2101","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/180b4c476d9b477f35629004f8f54034b31b2101"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/commits/340fd4b336087c4999f12f9bab79f06770331589/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T22:48:07Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T22:48:07Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"docs: replace the scaffold README — it still said \"goes here\"\n\nLast of the template boilerplate in this repo. It described nothing about the\napp, and one section was actively wrong: it told you to set `data-theme` and\n`data-dark-theme` on the container yourself, which is exactly what\n<HadokuThemeRoot> already does. An app that follows that advice fights the\nprovider for the attribute — the drift the provider exists to prevent, and which\nCLAUDE.md warns about two files over.\n\nAlso: StudyProps was missing apiBaseUrl (the registry injects it, and the API\nclient reads it), and the logging section said the logger comes from\n@wolffm/task-ui-components while the code sample imported it from\n@wolffm/logger/client. The sample was right.\n\nNow says what the app is, points at HANDOFF.md for the reasoning, and names the\ntwo deploy steps that are not automatic.","tree":{"sha":"bb86b26b505174d4c64f1f592c45406f392096d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/trees/bb86b26b505174d4c64f1f592c45406f392096d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-study/git/commits/340fd4b336087c4999f12f9bab79f06770331589","verification":{"payload":"tree bb86b26b505174d4c64f1f592c45406f392096d1\nparent aa424687e74d338925b02d5f2d18da1d87143e9e\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787093287 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787093287 -0700\n\ndocs: replace the scaffold README — it still said \"goes here\"\n\nLast of the template boilerplate in this repo. It described nothing about the\napp, and one section was actively wrong: it told you to set `data-theme` and\n`data-dark-theme` on the container yourself, which is exactly what\n<HadokuThemeRoot> already does. An app that follows that advice fights the\nprovider for the attribute — the drift the provider exists to prevent, and which\nCLAUDE.md warns about two files over.\n\nAlso: StudyProps was missing apiBaseUrl (the registry injects it, and the API\nclient reads it), and the logging section said the logger comes from\n@wolffm/task-ui-components while the code sample imported it from\n@wolffm/logger/client. The sample was right.\n\nNow says what the app is, points at HANDOFF.md for the reasoning, and names the\ntwo deploy steps that are not automatic.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQIWwTKMmWOhwF8JGLiftvvTvvw+1Ca9Yi7cTN62H42jD/tZSO9+EBJ+c93eFxfCTAj\npMyjhJs0S+zNNlR2n8BgY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T22:48:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site