{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/1e7ad53a9ec99de4a9e67773e68f9c48858db232","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKDFlN2FkNTNhOWVjOTlkZTRhOWU2Nzc3M2U2OGY5YzQ4ODU4ZGIyMzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/279f87ebecd60d922934573f190812c8e95b0a48","sha":"279f87ebecd60d922934573f190812c8e95b0a48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/279f87ebecd60d922934573f190812c8e95b0a48"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/5595d19e0fa553542c16bab26540e5b34a4373fc","sha":"5595d19e0fa553542c16bab26540e5b34a4373fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/5595d19e0fa553542c16bab26540e5b34a4373fc"}],"sha":"1e7ad53a9ec99de4a9e67773e68f9c48858db232","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/1e7ad53a9ec99de4a9e67773e68f9c48858db232"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/5595d19e0fa553542c16bab26540e5b34a4373fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T00:57:09Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T00:57:09Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat: run against a Chromium this machine already has\n\n`chromium.launch()` took no options, so motu insisted on the exact build its pinned\nPlaywright expects and ignored a working browser sitting on disk. On a developer\nmachine that is right — `npx playwright install chromium` is one command. Everywhere\nthat command cannot reach the CDN it makes the entire runtime tier unrunnable: a\nhardened CI image, a distro- or nix-packaged chromium, an air-gapped build box, a\nsandbox whose egress policy does not list `cdn.playwright.dev`. All of them HAVE a\nbrowser.\n\n`MOTU_CHROMIUM_PATH` is honoured at both launch sites (the shared browser every check\ndrives, and the persistent context `record-frame` opens).\n\nNEVER SILENT. A build motu did not pin can render and behave differently from the one\nit did, so a green `--runtime` that used one is claiming slightly more than it checked\nunless it says so. Every runtime lane now reports:\n\n    ! browser  not the pinned Chromium — launched `…/chrome` via MOTU_CHROMIUM_PATH —\n               the runtime findings below hold for THAT build; a pinned run can still differ\n\nA warning rather than a note in passing, because it weakens every verdict under it —\nand a warning rather than an error, because using the browser a machine already has is\na legitimate way to run, not a fault.\n\nFound while trying to verify `operation-reach` in the browser lane: this container\ncarries chromium 1194 and motu pins the Playwright that wants 1234, and the download\nis refused by the egress policy (`CONNECT tunnel failed, 403`). Verified the pinned\nPlaywright 1.62.1 drives the 1194 build before adding the flag, rather than assuming\nit would.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tk7Qb4yknGZeQ2RLDmgL5q","tree":{"sha":"98c02706c5a7bf269acf184f34c7354513dafd2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/98c02706c5a7bf269acf184f34c7354513dafd2b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/5595d19e0fa553542c16bab26540e5b34a4373fc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/5595d19e0fa553542c16bab26540e5b34a4373fc","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKDU1OTVkMTllMGZhNTUzNTQyYzE2YmFiMjY1NDBlNWIzNGE0MzczZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/3bf27f97b94c0986fbebd70e029c3e7ec078b9f9","sha":"3bf27f97b94c0986fbebd70e029c3e7ec078b9f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/3bf27f97b94c0986fbebd70e029c3e7ec078b9f9"}],"sha":"5595d19e0fa553542c16bab26540e5b34a4373fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/5595d19e0fa553542c16bab26540e5b34a4373fc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/3bf27f97b94c0986fbebd70e029c3e7ec078b9f9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T00:36:52Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T00:36:52Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat: operation-reach — does the thing the region asked for exist?\n\n`provenance` records every outbound ask and validates none of them. It cannot: an\noperation is a fact about the BACKEND, and motu has no view of one. So a region can\nask for a route that does not exist and the check prints it, green, forever.\n\nGiven the backend''s own list of operations it can answer. The wire door already\nrecords `route:<METHOD> <path>` and `fn:<name>` — `reachEntry()` in\n`@motu/runtime/postgrest-fetch` — which is an identifier an operation is keyed by, so\nno new instrumentation was needed, only the comparison.\n\nTWO DIRECTIONS, AND ONLY ONE IS AN ERROR.\n\nAn ask that resolves to no operation is an error: either the path is wrong, or the\nbackend has an operation its own declarations have never covered. Both are real and\nboth are silent today.\n\nAn operation the region DECLARES it reaches that no flow asked for is a warning, and\nnarrowed hard. The universe is the whole backend — 59 operations in the project this\nwas built against, 35 of them app routes — and a login region will never ask for an\nadmin route, so reporting the universe per region would be wrong dozens of times on\nday one, which is how a check teaches people to ignore it. The narrowing uses motu''s\nOWN existing declaration (`reaches` / `contract.effects`, via `declaredReach`), so\nboth sides are artifacts the project already maintains and there is no third list to\nrot.\n\nASKS THAT NAME NO OPERATION ARE COUNTED AND NAMED, never dropped. A contract call is\n`service.method` and a traced host module is a bare function name; a table or an rpc\nis a PostgREST identifier. None of them says which backend thing answered, and\nquietly ignoring the doors that cannot be checked is how this check would come to\nclaim more than it examined.\n\nOPAQUE, ON PURPOSE. `operations` in motu.config.json is a PATH, read for its names\nonly. The file is assay''s `.assay/operations.json` in practice, which also declares\ntables, RLS and prohibitions — none of it read here, because the moment motu\ninterprets a declaration''s contents it has married one backend tool. An OpenAPI\ndocument, a tRPC router or a hand-written array can fill the same slot.\n\nA route file is a PATTERN, not a string. `app/api/admin/email-previews/[id]/route.ts`\nanswers `/api/admin/email-previews/9f3c`, so routes are indexed by segments with\n`[id]`, `[...all]`, `[[...opt]]` and route groups handled — a string compare would\nhave reported that real, declared, successfully-answered ask as naming an operation\nnobody declares, which is an ERROR, so a false one costs a red run.\n\nPlaced beside `provenanceCheck` because it reads the same ledger: no extra page, no\nnavigation, and it inherits the `--fast` skip, which is right — a wire ask only\nexists where islands mounted in a browser.\n\nEmpty cases, deliberately: unconfigured is a skip that names the key; a file that is\nmissing, malformed or holds no names is INCONCLUSIVE (exit 2, retry, do not repair)\nrather than an empty universe that would make every ask unreachable; and a region\nwhose flows made no wire ask hands `seen: 0` to `report.ok`, which the report turns\ninto a skip.\n\nTHE HATCH IS TESTED. `loadMotuConfig` returns a hand-built whitelist and silently\ndrops any key not on it — the `hostSources` bug. The test writes a key that is NOT\nwhitelisted, asserts it vanishes, and then asserts `operations` survives the same\npath; removing the whitelist line makes it fail, which was watched rather than\nassumed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tk7Qb4yknGZeQ2RLDmgL5q","tree":{"sha":"5b639481c38567a2e78151c8fc418635fc9fa6c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/5b639481c38567a2e78151c8fc418635fc9fa6c3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/3bf27f97b94c0986fbebd70e029c3e7ec078b9f9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/3bf27f97b94c0986fbebd70e029c3e7ec078b9f9","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKDNiZjI3Zjk3Yjk0YzA5ODZmYmViZDcwZTAyOWMzZTdlYzA3OGI5Zjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/279f87ebecd60d922934573f190812c8e95b0a48","sha":"279f87ebecd60d922934573f190812c8e95b0a48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/279f87ebecd60d922934573f190812c8e95b0a48"}],"sha":"3bf27f97b94c0986fbebd70e029c3e7ec078b9f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/3bf27f97b94c0986fbebd70e029c3e7ec078b9f9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","