ents{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/8e9759db8425a1733800429882253f50808cde91/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T01:16:30Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T01:16:30Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"message":"feat(react): page view under StrictMode, with channels — and it could not render a page\n\nThe gap a real application found: a page created a data source in `useMemo`, let\nit start loading, and disposed it in the effect''s cleanup. React StrictMode runs\neffects mount → cleanup → mount, so the simulated unmount killed the instance the\npage then went on using — the first load''s answers were dropped by the source''s\nown generation guard, nothing restarted it, and the screen kept its spinner for\never. Every motu check was green, because the lagoon installs a source through a\nCHANNEL and no React component owns it there.\n\nPage view is the only view that owns a page''s lifecycle; every other one mounts\nISLANDS. So it mounts under StrictMode now, and the two deferred limitations\naround it are closed:\n\n- CHANNELS FIRE, installed against the store once the page''s own region has\n  registered it. The doc called this \"fixable … not done, because the one project\n  this was built against declares no channels and a fix nobody can fail is not a\n  fix\". There is one now. Torn down with the root, or a channel keeps writing to\n  a store nobody reads.\n\n- AND THE PAGE IS RENDERED AS AN ELEMENT. It was `page(props)` — invoking the\n  component as a plain function, outside any render — so every hook in it threw\n  \"Invalid hook call\". That is every real page. The first project to declare\n  `page` would have found the view unusable, and none had, so nothing did. Found\n  by writing the first test that renders one.\n\n`packages/cli` gets a tsconfig, which its `.tsx` tests needed and never had: with\nno `jsx` setting the runtime falls back to classic, and JSX inside an imported\nmotu module becomes React.createElement against a module that imports React by\nnamed exports only. The existing test passed because the file it imports never\nreaches its own JSX.\n\nThe new test drives the real view and asserts the bug: the broken shape stays on\n\"Chargement…\", the fixed one renders. Its fake load is a MACROTASK, because a\nmicrotask resolves inside the act() that mounts — before StrictMode''s cleanup —\nand the bug would not reproduce for a reason unrelated to the bug.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"089c276c9ec291319298d9ecf6fd6972a529daa3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/089c276c9ec291319298d9ecf6fd6972a529daa3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/8e9759db8425a1733800429882253f50808cde91","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/8e9759db8425a1733800429882253f50808cde91","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKDhlOTc1OWRiODQyNWExNzMzODAwNDI5ODgyMjUzZjUwODA4Y2RlOTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/e8861d32d1884dd7993fb1c7a9a6e54f216d7240","sha":"e8861d32d1884dd7993fb1c7a9a6e54f216d7240","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/e8861d32d1884dd7993fb1c7a9a6e54f216d7240"}],"sha":"8e9759db8425a1733800429882253f50808cde91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/8e9759db8425a1733800429882253f50808cde91"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/e8861d32d1884dd7993fb1c7a9a6e54f216d7240/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T00:19:18Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T00:19:18Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"message":"fix(chrome): Asked for hands the wire door over, and the pin stays off phones\n\nTWO SECTIONS SAYING THE SAME THING. \"Asked for\" listed every outbound call as a\nset of names; Network now lists the wire ones with their payload, their order,\ntheir status and the gesture that caused them. On a project where everything\ngoes through the wire — which is every region here — the first was a worse copy\nof the second sitting above it.\n\nThe wire door moves out rather than the section being deleted, because the other\ntwo doors are real and Network cannot see either: a CONTRACT call goes through\nthe transport and a HOST-MODULE call through a stub, neither is a fetch, and on\nan ocean host or a project still using module stubs that section is the only\nsignal there is. It now hides itself when it has nothing to say, so it\ndisappears here and stays where it earns its place.\n\nAND THE PIN IS A DESKTOP CONTROL. On a phone the dock is a bottom sheet: there\nis no width to reserve, and making the body a containing block reflowed the\nwhole region around a panel that does not sit beside it — the screenshot was a\npage squeezed into a corner. Pinning is now inert below 760px and the button is\nhidden, while the preference survives, so rotating back to a wide viewport\nrestores it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a024648223df051334a535c4c728be54f7b36c48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/a024648223df051334a535c4c728be54f7b36c48"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/e8861d32d1884dd7993fb1c7a9a6e54f216d7240","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/e8861d32d1884dd7993fb1c7a9a6e54f216d7240","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKGU4ODYxZDMyZDE4ODRkZDc5OTNmYjFjN2E5YTZlNTRmMjE2ZDcyNDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/2aa4e01f9f70b9c6e7356b09677336262b0d57fd","sha":"2aa4e01f9f70b9c6e7356b09677336262b0d57fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/2aa4e01f9f70b9c6e7356b09677336262b0d57fd"}],"sha":"e8861d32d1884dd7993fb1c7a9a6e54f216d7240","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/e8861d32d1884dd7993fb1c7a9a6e54f216d7240"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/2aa4e01f9f70b9c6e7356b09677336262b0d57fd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T00:12:52Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T00:12:52Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"message":"fix(runtime,chrome): every save is called Enregistrer\n\nGrouping keyed on the LABEL, and on a real screen the agenda, the commitment\nbanner and the settings dialog all say \"Enregistrer\" — so two separate saves\nmerged into one run and the second one''s calls were reported as part of the\nfirst. Two bugs wearing one coat: the name did not identify the control, and the\ngrouping did not identify the press.\n\n- An id per press, generated where the gesture is noted. Two presses are two\n  runs whatever they are called.\n- The label carries WHERE. The island slot first — `data-motu-slot`, motu''s own\n  vocabulary — so a run reads \"session-tab · Enregistrer\" and names the region\n  piece that did it. A dialog cannot have one, since it portals to the body\n  element outside every island''s subtree, so its accessible name stands in:\n  \"Réglages du Conseil · Enregistrer\", which is what a person calls it anyway.\n\nVerified on a real region, pressing the two identically-named buttons in turn:\n\n    ↳ Réglages du Conseil · Enregistrer   14 calls\n    ↳ session-tab · Enregistrer            9 calls\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1988e62261e02ca8d06615955943a0f616f4d06b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/1988e62261e02ca8d06615955943a0f616f4d06b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/2aa4e01f9f70b9c6e7356b09677336262b0d57fd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/2aa4e01f9f70b9c6e7356b09677336262b0d57fd","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKDJhYTRlMDFmOWY3MGI5YzZlNzM1NmIwOTY3NzMzNjI2MmIwZDU3ZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/403a27e52245b43b6b7918789bfbe118e539f79b","sha":"403a27e52245b43b6b7918789bfbe118e539f79b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/403a27e52245b43b6b7918789bfbe118e539f79b"}],"sha":"2aa4e01f9f70b9c6e7356b09677336262b0d57fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/2aa4e01f9f70b9c6e7356b09677336262b0d57fd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/403a27e52245b43b6b7918789bfbe118e539f79b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T00:04:40Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T00:04:40Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"message":"feat(runtime,chrome): group calls by what you pressed, and stop covering modals\n\nWHAT DID MY CLICK JUST DO. `by` — the island or source a call is charged to — is\nwhat a CHECK needs, and it is `unattributed` for most real calls, because a\nsource fetches outside any island''s window. So on the screen where you just\npressed Enregistrer, every row said the same nothing and none of them said WHY.\n\nCalls are now tagged with the gesture in force when they left, and the panel\nheads each run with it: \"Enregistrer · 14 calls\". The label is the control''s\nACCESSIBLE NAME — the vocabulary `expectRender` already reads from, so the log\nnames what you pressed the way you would say it. A 2.5s window, generous\ndeliberately: a save is a write, a refetch and everything the refetch fans out\ninto, and cutting the tail off splits one action across two groups. It expires,\nbecause a poll adopted by the last button pressed is a lie that reads like the\ntruth.\n\nAND THE MODALS. Pinning reserved the page, and every dialog the application\nopened still landed under the dock: a portal renders into the body element and\nis positioned against the VIEWPORT, which no padding can move. That was stated\nas a limit and it is the right one for the 46px rail — nobody interacts around\nthat. Pinned it is not: the whole point is to work in the region.\n\nSo while pinned, the body element becomes the containing block for fixed\ndescendants and a viewport-fixed dialog resolves against the page''s own box.\nThe dock escapes by being reparented onto the document element, outside the\ntransform. Compensating with an offset was the first attempt and it was wrong in\nthe way that matters — the dock has several separately-positioned fixed parts,\neach would have needed its own counter-offset, and the next one added would\nsilently not.\n\nVerified on a real region: the Réglages dialog centres at 170..938 against a\npanel starting at 1163, and saving from inside it heads the log with\n\"↳ ENREGISTRER · 14 CALLS\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dd789e9b3ae17483e7916ea9312ecd2acf348dbc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/dd789e9b3ae17483e7916ea9312ecd2acf348dbc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/403a27e52245b43b6b7918789bfbe118e539f79b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/403a27e52245b43b6b7918789bfbe118e539f79b","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKDQwM2EyN2U1MjI0NWI0M2I2Yjc5MTg3ODliZmJlMTE4ZTUzOWY3OWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/c4697b59fbecdb1d067c9fe403bfa116eac1292e","sha":"c4697b59fbecdb1d067c9fe403bfa116eac1292e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/c4697b59fbecdb1d067c9fe403bfa116eac1292e"}],"sha":"403a27e52245b43b6b7918789bfbe118e539f79b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/403a27e52245b43b6b7918789bfbe118e539f79b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/c4697b59fbecdb1d067c9fe403bfa116eac1292e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T23:47:13Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T23:47:13Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"message":"fix(chrome,runtime): the pin measured the wrong width, and the log was a moment behind\n\nTwo bugs in the panel that shipped an hour ago, both found by using it.\n\nTHE RESERVE WAS A GUESS. It hardcoded 340px while the SEAMS tab is\n`width: min(560px, 46vw)` — it widens for a five-column table — so pinning still\ncovered 220px of the region, on exactly the tab the pin exists for. It now\nmeasures the rendered panel and re-measures on tab change and resize, so a\nfuture per-tab width needs no second edit.\n\nTHE LOG DID NOT REPAINT ON ITS OWN. The lens repaints on STORE WRITES, and a\ncall whose response changes no region key writes nothing — so pressing\nEnregistrer on an agenda put nine rows in the log and none of them on screen\nuntil something else moved. A panel that is a moment behind is worse than one\nshowing nothing, because it looks current, and \"I saved and nothing appeared\" is\nthe exact report this section exists to prevent.\n\n`subscribeWireCalls` is the third source the lens watches, beside store writes\nand the corpus. A subscriber that throws is caught: a panel''s bug must not stop\nthe fake answering the request the application is awaiting.\n\nVerified together on a real region: pinned on Seams, the reserve is 606px\n(46 rail + 560 panel), the region is clickable to its edge, and one save takes\nthe Network list from 9 rows to 18 with no other interaction.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"30687083c563710c725d1b40a62755eeaa9e5a8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/30687083c563710c725d1b40a62755eeaa9e5a8f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/c4697b59fbecdb1d067c9fe403bfa116eac1292e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/c4697b59fbecdb1d067c9fe403bfa116eac1292e","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKGM0Njk3YjU5ZmJlY2RiMWQwNjdjOWZlNDAzYmZhMTE2ZWFjMTI5MmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/e47c8bb7b29d396407ae71f25bd7103e477ec5f0","sha":"e47c8bb7b29d396407ae71f25bd7103e477ec5f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/e47c8bb7b29d396407ae71f25bd7103e477ec5f0"}],"sha":"c4697b59fbecdb1d067c9fe403bfa116eac1292e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/c4697b59fbecdb1d067c9fe403bfa116eac1292e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/e47c8bb7b29d396407ae71f25bd7103e477ec5f0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T23:40:03Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T23:40:03Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"message":"feat(chrome): open a Network row, and pin the panel beside the page\n\nTwo things the Network log needed the moment it existed, both asked for by the\nfirst person to use it.\n\nAN ACCORDION, because a title attribute was the wrong instrument: it cannot be\nselected, cannot be copied, does not wrap, and never appears at all on a touch\ndevice. The payload is the reason to look — a nested `p_sessions` is unreadable\nas one line and perfectly clear pretty-printed — so it gets a surface. The row\nis a button with `aria-expanded`/`aria-controls` and the body toggles `hidden`,\nso it opens from the keyboard and a collapsed payload is not announced. The\nretained payload cap goes 2 kB → 20 kB: a row you can open is only worth opening\nif the payload is there, and the largest real one here is about 21 kB.\n\nPINNED, as a choice rather than a new default. The dock reserves the rail and\noverlays the panel, deliberately — insetting on every open would reflow the\napplication each time the dock is touched. What that reasoning did not\nanticipate is a panel you WATCH while you work: reading the network log means\ndoing something on the page and seeing the call appear, and an overlay makes\nthat impossible on the half of the region it covers. So the reserve became a\ntoggle. Unpinned is unchanged; pinned costs one reflow, when asked for, and is\nremembered across reloads — the person who wants it is reloading a lot.\n\nVerified together: with the panel pinned, saving an agenda added 9 rows to the\nlog while the region under the pointer stayed clickable.\n\nThree times in one session I put backticks in this stylesheet, which is a JS\ntemplate literal, and once an octal escape in a comment ABOUT the escape.\n`stylesheets-parse` caught all four.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"899e34f5e6759c1e309924336373ac1610bc8644","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/899e34f5e6759c1e309924336373ac1610bc8644"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/e47c8bb7b29d396407ae71f25bd7103e477ec5f0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/e47c8bb7b29d396407ae71f25bd7103e477ec5f0","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKGU0N2M4YmI3YjI5ZDM5NjQwN2FlNzFmMjViZDcxMDNlNDc3ZWM1ZjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/140966abbbcf91c453abebd49c6af4dc4f514f7c","sha":"140966abbbcf91c453abebd49c6af4dc4f514f7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/140966abbbcf91c453abebd49c6af4dc4f514f7c"}],"sha":"e47c8bb7b29d396407ae71f25bd7103e477ec5f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/e47c8bb7b29d396407ae71f25bd7103e477ec5f0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/140966abbbcf91c453abebd49c6af4dc4f514f7c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T23:28:56Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T23:28:56Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"message":"feat(runtime,chrome): a Network section — the calls, not the set of names\n\n`DataReach` answers \"did this screen touch `team_schedules`\", which is the\nquestion a DECLARATION asks. Nothing answered \"did my save actually send the new\nhour\", which is the question a person asks when a screen appears to do nothing.\n\nAnd no other tool can answer it HERE. Intercepting `fetch` is the point of the\nlagoon, and the side effect is that the browser''s own Network panel is empty by\nconstruction: the fake replies without touching the network. motu removed the\nstandard instrument, so motu owes the replacement — the same argument\n`traced()`/`provenance` already makes one layer up for host modules (\"the lagoon\nshows the result and never the question\").\n\nMeasured cost of not having it: three separate \"the page does nothing\" reports\non one project, each of which was the same thing — a write RPC answering\n`{ success: true }` and recording nothing, so the refetch re-read what was\nalready there. One row separates that from \"the region is not wired\", and the\ndistinction took a diagnosis each time.\n\n- `postgrest-fetch.ts` retains each intercepted call: target in the\n  declaration''s own spelling, verb, payload, status, a one-line response\n  summary, and the `by` attribution `data-reach` already computes — so a row\n  says which ISLAND asked, which a network panel could not. Bounded ring (200);\n  payloads truncated and said to be.\n- The dock renders it BESIDE \"Asked for\" rather than replacing it: that section\n  is the merged declaration ledger across three doors, and folding the wire into\n  it would lose the other two.\n\nIt proves the CLIENT half only, and the panel says so. A request leaving with\nthe right payload does not mean the refetch happened, the response was merged,\nor anything re-rendered — so this is a log, deliberately not a check. \"A request\nfired, therefore the screen works\" is exactly the check that cannot fail.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"99bfc37bfd759bab700292e88887b4eb70ad798b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/99bfc37bfd759bab700292e88887b4eb70ad798b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/140966abbbcf91c453abebd49c6af4dc4f514f7c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/140966abbbcf91c453abebd49c6af4dc4f514f7c","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKDE0MDk2NmFiYmJjZjkxYzQ1M2FiZWJkNDljNmFmNGRjNGY1MTRmN2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/792b291f062130f07cc4b5b197363d210b8ad4a2","sha":"792b291f062130f07cc4b5b197363d210b8ad4a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/792b291f062130f07cc4b5b197363d210b8ad4a2"}],"sha":"140966abbbcf91c453abebd49c6af4dc4f514f7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/140966abbbcf91c453abebd49c6af4dc4f514f7c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/792b291f062130f07cc4b5b197363d210b8ad4a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T22:05:48Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T22:05:48Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"message":"fix(cli): parse `slots` too, and one of them had a hole\n\nThe sibling of the last commit, one keyword over. `verify` asked \"which slots\ndoes an island fill\" and `integrate check` asked \"which slot fills each root\nprop\" — the same declaration, two hand-rolled readers. `verify` was already\nIMPORTING a correct ts-morph reader for its half (`nestedSlots`) and using it\n400 lines above the regex that asked the same question.\n\n`declaredSlotNames` is new, and it closes a hole rather than tidying one. The\nold set took every `slot: ''…''` in the file, which includes the region-level\nmap''s own object form (`{ slot: ''auth-error'', when: ''authError'' }`). So a slot\nNAMED there and declared by no island entry counted as declared, and an island\nfilling it passed the very check that exists to catch that. Measured on a real\nproject with a planted ghost slot: old reader 0 errors, parser 1.\n\nEverything else is a shape the regexes had already been patched for, now a test:\na one-line region map that the multi-line pattern ran past — \"swallowing the\nisland entries below and reading their `bind` pairs as slot mappings\", five\nprops of one card reported as undeclared slots — and both patterns anchored at\ntwo spaces of indent, where a reformat yields an empty map that reads as \"this\nroot fills no slots\".\n\nVerified no behaviour change where the regexes were right: 44 findings across\nnine regions of a real project, identical before and after, warnings included.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fa8f524f17e4a9d8f9d35a998a6257fdc51b19b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/fa8f524f17e4a9d8f9d35a998a6257fdc51b19b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/792b291f062130f07cc4b5b197363d210b8ad4a2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/792b291f062130f07cc4b5b197363d210b8ad4a2","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKDc5MmIyOTFmMDYyMTMwZjA3Y2M0YjViMTk3MzYzZDIxMGI4YWQ0YTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/44e52aa689691316719b3c3eb159ad71ba154b69","sha":"44e52aa689691316719b3c3eb159ad71ba154b69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/44e52aa689691316719b3c3eb159ad71ba154b69"}],"sha":"792b291f062130f07cc4b5b197363d210b8ad4a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/792b291f062130f07cc4b5b197363d210b8ad4a2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/44e52aa689691316719b3c3eb159ad71ba154b69/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T21:52:38Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T21:52:38Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"message":"fix(cli): parse `sources`, and stop two regexes disagreeing about it\n\n`integrate check` and `verify` both read a region''s `sources`, and each had\ngrown its own regex over it. `verify` handled both declaration forms;\n`integrate check` matched only `(\\w+):\\s*\\{…\\}`, so a region declaring\n`teams: teamsSource` — the form the TYPE SYSTEM checks — skipped the check that\nsays the page installs the source. Not reported differently: absent. Moving a\nregion to the stronger declaration silently turned a check off, and the better\nshape ended up with less checking than the weaker one.\n\nThat is what two hand-rolled readers of one shape do. `integration.mjs` had\nalready reached this conclusion for the host''s JSX and said so — \"ts-morph is\nalready how every other host-source question here is answered; this was the last\nregex standing in the middle of it\". It was the last regex over HOST SOURCES.\nThe archipelago side was still matched, in both files, and the comment is why\nnobody looked.\n\n- `lib/declared-sources.mjs`: one ts-morph reader of `sources`, returning both\n  forms in one shape so a caller cannot handle one and forget the other.\n- Both commands use it. `integrate check` now covers by-reference sources:\n  verified against a real project, where the check went from ABSENT to `ok`,\n  and to `error` when the page stops importing the source.\n\nThe scars the regexes carried are gone with them: `verify` blanked every comment\nbefore matching, because an apostrophe in prose opens a string as far as a regex\nis concerned and \"the week''s missions\" became a key named ` missions, so it\ncomes...`; and `\\n  \\},` as a terminator meant the declaration had to sit at\nexactly two spaces of indent. Both are properties of the tool, not the language,\nand both are tests now.\n\n`slots` is still matched, in both files, and its comments already carry two bugs\npaid for the same way. Not fixed here; the stale \"last regex\" claim is corrected\nso the next reader can see it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"81b8b47676e5cfe930676662f5f77008de235b0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/81b8b47676e5cfe930676662f5f77008de235b0c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/44e52aa689691316719b3c3eb159ad71ba154b69","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/44e52aa689691316719b3c3eb159ad71ba154b69","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKDQ0ZTUyYWE2ODk2OTEzMTY3MTliM2MzZWIxNTlhZDcxYmExNTRiNjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/e7c20ee9ffefbc38ee07c75652aa44bb8bcfdfe0","sha":"e7c20ee9ffefbc38ee07c75652aa44bb8bcfdfe0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/e7c20ee9ffefbc38ee07c75652aa44bb8bcfdfe0"}],"sha":"44e52aa689691316719b3c3eb159ad71ba154b69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/44e52aa689691316719b3c3eb159ad71ba154b69"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/e7c20ee9ffefbc38ee07c75652aa44bb8bcfdfe0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T13:31:54Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T13:31:54Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"message":"docs(cli,overlay): say what to build, not just what to call\n\nThe warning is now visible, which makes what it says load-bearing. It said\n\"install the source with `channelFrom({ to, id, args })`\" — a call signature —\nand whoever reads it is usually mid-migration and has never written a source.\nAn agent asked to fix the warning gets the call and invents the rest.\n\nThe design was documented, in three places none of which the warning names:\n`sources`/`channelFrom` here, the port and its unit tests in 11, the runtime\ncontract in the `SourceInstance` type. Nothing was a recipe.\n\n- A \"Writing a source\" section, written from the two real ones: the port, the\n  factory, `intents`, the type-only declaration, and the two installs that\n  differ only in the port. Both the CLI message and the lens finding point at\n  it by name.\n- It also answers the question the split docs left open — WHEN a port earns its\n  place. Wire mocking substitutes data beneath the real service, so a port that\n  existed only to return different rows is redundant; what it still buys is a\n  seam for orchestration (a generation guard, a debounce), which is exactly the\n  logic no rendered state distinguishes and the reason those sources get unit\n  tests.\n- And it restates the boundary rather than hiding it: the adapter on the far\n  side of the port is proved by none of this.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5ff07852278405f15f480d36aed969091702e169","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/5ff07852278405f15f480d36aed969091702e169"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/e7c20ee9ffefbc38ee07c75652aa44bb8bcfdfe0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/e7c20ee9ffefbc38ee07c75652aa44bb8bcfdfe0","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKGU3YzIwZWU5ZmZlZmJjMzhlZTA3Yzc1NjUyYWE0NGJiOGJjZmRmZTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/7f0508e20f7c992894de4a5720c356200790e94c","sha":"7f0508e20f7c992894de4a5720c356200790e94c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/7f0508e20f7c992894de4a5720c356200790e94c"}],"sha":"e7c20ee9ffefbc38ee07c75652aa44bb8bcfdfe0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/e7c20ee9ffefbc38ee07c75652aa44bb8bcfdfe0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/7f0508e20f7c992894de4a5720c356200790e94c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T13:20:15Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T13:20:15Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"message":"feat(overlay,chrome): surface the findings a person has to answer\n\nA region declared `sources: { teams: … }`, seeded those keys, rendered\nperfectly and was completely inert: the islands emitted, the intent left, and\nnothing answered because no channel was installed. Every visible signal looked\nhealthy. The only trace was \"No channels installed.\" in grey italics under a\ntable, indistinguishable from any other empty section — and the panel''s own\nFindings list said \"1\", that one being \"4 keys could be props\".\n\nSo two things were wrong. The list did not contain the finding that mattered,\nand it ranked an optimisation above everything.\n\n- A new finding: a declared source no channel produced. It names its keys and\n  both ways out, and it is a decision — seeding is a legitimate answer, but\n  somebody has to make that call. Derived in the browser from the archipelago\n  config and the channel registry, so it needs no CLI and no report file; both\n  declared source forms expose `produces` at runtime.\n- Findings sort by `decision` first, then tone. Tone is loudness; `decision` is\n  whether it is yours to answer, and that is what a reader needs first.\n- The dock splits them: NEEDS A DECISION, then ALSO NOTED. An optimisation can\n  no longer sit at the top of a region that is not wired.\n- A count badge on the Seams tab, absent when nothing is waiting — the findings\n  were the last section of the second tab, so a region could be asking for a\n  decision while every visible surface said nothing.\n\nVerified against the CLI independently: on a region with two sources installed\nand four seeded, the lens names exactly the four `sources-live` names.\n\nThe dock sheet joins the stylesheet guard, one file late. Writing a comment in\nDOCK_CSS with backticks around a property name ended the template literal and\nkilled the lagoon with a SyntaxError pointing at an innocent line — the fifth\nround of the mistake that test''s header counts, in the one sheet it did not\ncover. It now also asserts the badge is not stranded in the phone media query,\nwhere it first landed and silently did nothing at desktop width.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"87741a0d50d0e3af227bd5dca2730bc99046ec6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/87741a0d50d0e3af227bd5dca2730bc99046ec6b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/7f0508e20f7c992894de4a5720c356200790e94c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/7f0508e20f7c992894de4a5720c356200790e94c","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKDdmMDUwOGUyMGY3Yzk5Mjg5NGRlNGE1NzIwYzM1NjIwMDc5MGU5NGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/7ec90c67566c19736bdda307cd1b12d196ce9cef","sha":"7ec90c67566c19736bdda307cd1b12d196ce9cef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/7ec90c67566c19736bdda307cd1b12d196ce9cef"}],"sha":"7f0508e20f7c992894de4a5720c356200790e94c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/7f0508e20f7c992894de4a5720c356200790e94c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/7ec90c67566c19736bdda307cd1b12d196ce9cef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T13:19:57Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T13:19:57Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"message":"fix(host,cli): a publish that reports success has to be checkable\n\n`publish --remote` printed the host''s URLs verbatim and never fetched one, so\n\"published\" meant \"the host answered 200\". Every field in that answer — ok,\nbytes, deduped, urls — is equally consistent with the host having stored the\nwrong blob, which left no way to tell \"the host mis-stored it\" from \"you are\nlooking at the wrong URL\". A session was spent diagnosing a host bug that did\nnot exist because of exactly that gap.\n\nThe host now returns the sha256 of what it stored and the CLI compares it with\nwhat it sent. Hashing costs nothing over the wire — both sides already hold the\nbytes — so a mismatch becomes an error instead of a URL. A host too old to\nanswer reports `verified: null` and the CLI says so rather than passing quietly.\n\nIt also returns `live`: a registered dev server proxies ahead of the store for\n`latest`, so publishing mid-session hands back a bookmark that serves vite. That\nis indistinguishable from a publish that never landed, so the CLI now names it\nand points at the immutable URL, which is never shadowed.\n\nTests drive real servers on both sides, including a host that answers 200 with a\nhash that does not match — the failure the old code was blind to.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7dc2ae3f7897679663caf9f3d7bdd2d04c8143a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/7dc2ae3f7897679663caf9f3d7bdd2d04c8143a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/7ec90c67566c19736bdda307cd1b12d196ce9cef","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/7ec90c67566c19736bdda307cd1b12d196ce9cef","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKDdlYzkwYzY3NTY2YzE5NzM2YmRkYTMwN2NkMWIxMmQxOTZjZTljZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/d97c962001451791c9b9d527d89f73b8328f9d7e","sha":"d97c962001451791c9b9d527d89f73b8328f9d7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/d97c962001451791c9b9d527d89f73b8328f9d7e"}],"sha":"7ec90c67566c19736bdda307cd1b12d196ce9cef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/7ec90c67566c19736bdda307cd1b12d196ce9cef"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/use