ps://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/32a70ad8e2d159ca9e412ceb313e4909c9859c37","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKDMyYTcwYWQ4ZTJkMTU5Y2E5ZTQxMmNlYjMxM2U0OTA5Yzk4NTljMzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/8664b946013a0b945e8f35ee7a00e6c9b218d508","sha":"8664b946013a0b945e8f35ee7a00e6c9b218d508","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/8664b946013a0b945e8f35ee7a00e6c9b218d508"}],"sha":"32a70ad8e2d159ca9e412ceb313e4909c9859c37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/32a70ad8e2d159ca9e412ceb313e4909c9859c37"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/8664b946013a0b945e8f35ee7a00e6c9b218d508/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T13:30:24Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T13:30:24Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"message":"feat: the boot splash wears the project''s colour, not motu''s\n\nThe shell around a framed lagoon already follows the project — peps'' rail is\ngold — so a teal loader inside a gold shell was the one moment the host\nattributed its own colour to somebody else''s application, and it was the first\nthing anyone saw of that project.\n\nThe ramp comes from `primaryVars`, the same function `applyMotuChrome` and the\nshell''s detector use, so there is no second set of percentages to drift. It is\nbuilt against `var(--mb)` rather than a colour: `primaryVars`'' mix helper only\nconcatenates strings, so it yields valid CSS, and the splash can then be\nrepainted by setting one property instead of the inline script carrying its own\ncopy of the percentages.\n\nTwo tiers, in the order the host already ranks them. DECLARED (`chrome.brand`)\nis known server-side, so it is in the first bytes and the splash is never\nbriefly teal. DETECTED can only come from a previous visit, because detection\nreads pixels the splash is covering — so it reads the sessionStorage entry the\nshell writes. Neither, and it stays motu teal, which is honest: the host is the\nonly thing on screen anybody has heard of yet.\n\nA DECLARED COLOUR IS NOT A HEX, and assuming it was made the first version of\nthis ship teal on the only project that had bothered to say otherwise. peps\ndeclares `color-mix(in srgb, hsl(55 90% 48%) 75%, #000)`; `normalisePrimary`\nparses hex only and answered null. Nothing needs to parse it — the browser does\nthe mixing. The clamp stays for detected colours, which arrive normalised.\n\nAlso keys the shell''s colour cache by repo/slug instead of frame src. One lagoon\nhad as many cache entries as it has URL spellings, and none of them was\npredictable from the server, where the splash is written.\n\nThis cannot poison detection: `rasteriseDocument` already excludes `#motu-boot`\nby name, for exactly this reason.\n\nVerified end to end against a throwaway host over a copied store (peps is\nprivate, so it cannot be fetched anonymously): a repo declaring peps'' exact\nbrand string serves `--mb:color-mix(...)` in the first bytes and the browser\nresolves the ramp to gold; an undeclared repo still serves #12988f.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"208d598da724d02b7e2067fc05e253bb98d0986e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/208d598da724d02b7e2067fc05e253bb98d0986e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/8664b946013a0b945e8f35ee7a00e6c9b218d508","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/8664b946013a0b945e8f35ee7a00e6c9b218d508","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKDg2NjRiOTQ2MDEzYTBiOTQ1ZThmMzVlZTdhMDBlNmM5YjIxOGQ1MDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/af61ed75b9709b4df8d334f80b46d930f551ac24","sha":"af61ed75b9709b4df8d334f80b46d930f551ac24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/af61ed75b9709b4df8d334f80b46d930f551ac24"}],"sha":"8664b946013a0b945e8f35ee7a00e6c9b218d508","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/8664b946013a0b945e8f35ee7a00e6c9b218d508"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/af61ed75b9709b4df8d334f80b46d930f551ac24/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T13:13:57Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T13:13:57Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"message":"feat: show the fit and transport chips only where they are a choice\n\nBoth chips offered a switch whose other position did nothing for most lagoons.\n\nFit: `legacyFit` lived only in the CLI (`util.mjs`), so the gallery had no way to\nknow whether a legacy skin existed. `motu island verify` has always been able to\nsay \"no legacy fit on host ''next'' — nothing to fit to\" while the dock went on\ndrawing the toggle. Injected as `__MOTU_LEGACY_FIT__` alongside\n`__MOTU_ISOLATION__`, for the same reason: it is a fact about the project''s host,\nand restating it in lagoon.config.json would only let the two drift.\n\nTransport: MOCK/HTTP needs somewhere for http to GO. The gallery already held the\ngate — `config.httpBase` and `overrides.transportFor` — so flipping it with\nneither set pointed the lagoon at a dispatcher the project does not have, and the\nregion stopped answering. A switch whose other position is \"broken\" is not a\nchoice.\n\n`legacyFit` defaults to true in GalleryOptions so an ejected entry that predates\nthe flag keeps the chip it has always had; demo-app''s ejected entry passes it by\nhand, which is exactly the drift `entry-current` reports.\n\nRecord stays: it captures backend responses into request-keyed fixtures, which is\na different question from the one motu/coverage answers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7474990d875f77e0d6dd210f213f79e28c5e3a47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/7474990d875f77e0d6dd210f213f79e28c5e3a47"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/af61ed75b9709b4df8d334f80b46d930f551ac24","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/af61ed75b9709b4df8d334f80b46d930f551ac24","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKGFmNjFlZDc1Yjk3MDliNGRmOGQzMzRmODBiNDZkOTMwZjU1MWFjMjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/5563348cf214aa54485518b6db30c379c86f4463","sha":"5563348cf214aa54485518b6db30c379c86f4463","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/5563348cf214aa54485518b6db30c379c86f4463"}],"sha":"af61ed75b9709b4df8d334f80b46d930f551ac24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/af61ed75b9709b4df8d334f80b46d930f551ac24"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/5563348cf214aa54485518b6db30c379c86f4463/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:57:23Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:57:23Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"message":"feat: drop the Seam lens pill from the rig\n\nThe layer is a MEANS, not a thing to manage. Everything that needs it opens\nit — the crosshair to aim with, Coupling to draw on — and the crosshair now\nputs it away once it has picked. A switch for something that turns itself on\nand off is one more pressed-looking control in a rig whose other chips all\nchange what you see.\n\nNote what this leaves: nothing opens the lens deliberately any more. That is\nthe intent, not an oversight — everything it used to SAY is in the tabs, and\nonly the outlines and wires over the running page are still its own, which\narrive with whatever asked for them. If a manual way back in is ever wanted\nit is `tab: true` on the lens mount (the overlay''s own edge tab), not a third\ntrigger somewhere else — the comment there says so, since the tab was\nswitched off BECAUSE this pill existed and that reasoning has now inverted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7b515021dd0d82bd1e165b964f69b7d30468745c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/7b515021dd0d82bd1e165b964f69b7d30468745c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/5563348cf214aa54485518b6db30c379c86f4463","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/5563348cf214aa54485518b6db30c379c86f4463","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKDU1NjMzNDhjZjIxNGFhNTQ0ODU1MThiNmRiMzBjMzc5Yzg2ZjQ0NjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/369ba62392ac74f5162e790cec8b965d78c9e8e6","sha":"369ba62392ac74f5162e790cec8b965d78c9e8e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/369ba62392ac74f5162e790cec8b965d78c9e8e6"}],"sha":"5563348cf214aa54485518b6db30c379c86f4463","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/5563348cf214aa54485518b6db30c379c86f4463"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/369ba62392ac74f5162e790cec8b965d78c9e8e6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:54:16Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:54:16Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"message":"feat: show an island''s scenario count on the lens badge\n\nThe count was on the dock''s island chips, and the chip a person is actually\nlooking at while deciding is the LENS badge — the label drawn over the\nisland on the page, under the crosshair. That is where the question comes\nup: is opening this one alone worth the click, when most islands have\nnothing but their default mount.\n\nRead from the artifact''s own catalogue (`__motuLagoonStates.scenarios`), the\nsame list the dock counts, so the two cannot disagree — and an artifact that\npublishes none (an older build, or a lagoon with no evidence) simply shows\nno count rather than a zero.\n\nIts own pill on the end of the label, not more prose: these are read at a\nglance while the crosshair moves, where \"4 scenarios\" would not be.\n\nModule scope, not a class method — the first attempt put a bare `function`\ninside `class Overlay`, which is a syntax error the build caught.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"55f3edd6936bdcec3f08827ac3843d0d25ab0f3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/55f3edd6936bdcec3f08827ac3843d0d25ab0f3b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/369ba62392ac74f5162e790cec8b965d78c9e8e6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/369ba62392ac74f5162e790cec8b965d78c9e8e6","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKDM2OWJhNjIzOTJhYzc0ZjUxNjJlNzkwY2VjOGI5NjVkNzhjOWU4ZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/b266de173c63e9d276efe8d18bbc0d22791724db","sha":"b266de173c63e9d276efe8d18bbc0d22791724db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/b266de173c63e9d276efe8d18bbc0d22791724db"}],"sha":"369ba62392ac74f5162e790cec8b965d78c9e8e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/369ba62392ac74f5162e790cec8b965d78c9e8e6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/b266de173c63e9d276efe8d18bbc0d22791724db/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:42:08Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:42:08Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"message":"feat: show an island''s scenario count, and spend the crosshair when it picks\n\nWORTH SCOPING OR NOT, ANSWERED BEFORE THE CLICK. Every island in the picker\nlooked equally worth opening, and most have nothing but their default mount\n— so finding the one with states meant opening them in turn. The count now\nrides on the island''s chip in the Islands tab and in the picker rows, with\n`—` where there are none. The seeded default is deliberately not counted: it\nis what an island shows with NO scenario, so the number is exactly what\nscoping buys. Read from the catalogue already in the page, so it cannot\ndisagree with the list it sits beside.\n\nTHE CROSSHAIR IS SPENT ONCE IT HAS PICKED. The overlay stops its own picking\non the pointerdown, but the gallery''s mirror of that state did not follow: ⌖\nstayed lit over a mode that was over, so the next press turned picking OFF\nand every second aim did nothing. The lens layer goes away with it — it was\nopened to aim with, and leaving it over the island you just scoped to is one\nmore thing to dismiss before you can look at what you asked for.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e81d2ef29763ba0f1cda5e1e18dae894ce7410d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/e81d2ef29763ba0f1cda5e1e18dae894ce7410d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/b266de173c63e9d276efe8d18bbc0d22791724db","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/b266de173c63e9d276efe8d18bbc0d22791724db","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKGIyNjZkZTE3M2M2M2U5ZDI3NmVmZThkMThiYmMwZDIyNzkxNzI0ZGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/beefd4fea7b6b3ce1db8ee4c37ea509f402ac94a","sha":"beefd4fea7b6b3ce1db8ee4c37ea509f402ac94a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/beefd4fea7b6b3ce1db8ee4c37ea509f402ac94a"}],"sha":"b266de173c63e9d276efe8d18bbc0d22791724db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/b266de173c63e9d276efe8d18bbc0d22791724db"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/beefd4fea7b6b3ce1db8ee4c37ea509f402ac94a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:39:00Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:39:00Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"message":"fix: switching lagoons left the URL and the dock behind; check ejected entries\n\nTHE DOCK WAS STALE BECAUSE UNMOUNTING THREW — my own regression. Making the\nattach poll run forever (so the dock re-subscribes when a lagoon is\nreplaced) dropped the handle it was assigned to, leaving the teardown''s\n`clearInterval(poll)` referring to nothing. A host that swaps lagoons\nunmounts before mounting the next, so it never got past that line: the dock\nstayed bound to the lagoon you arrived on and described it confidently while\nthe frame showed another. The interval leaked on top.\n\nTHE ADDRESS ONLY EVER GOT A HASH. `#<i>` indexes THIS page''s member list —\nright for a group, whose members have no page of their own; wrong for a\nlagoon rail, where every member has its own URL. Picking one left the bar\nnaming the lagoon you arrived at, so copying the link reopened the first.\nDerived from the frame''s own address now, so page and frame cannot disagree.\n\nTwo traps worth recording, both hit while writing five lines: that script is\na TEMPLATE LITERAL, so a backtick ends it and a backslash is an escape\nbefore it is code — the regex form emitted `//__motu_frame$/`, a line\ncomment that swallowed the rest of the function. `split()` needs neither.\n\nAND A CHECK FOR WHAT CAUSED THE LAST TWO BUGS. `entry-current` reports what\nan ejected entry never mentions of what the scaffold passes. Ejecting stops\nregeneration — the point of the hatch — so every option added afterwards\narrives only if somebody copies it down, and nothing said when they had not:\n`evidence` (every declared state unreachable in a browser) and\n`lens.onPicked` (the crosshair could not scope) both landed that way. It\nfinds a third on the same file: `target`, which is what `--archipelago` sets\nso a published artifact opens on a chosen region.\n\nName-presence, not shape: an ejected entry is a file somebody edits, and may\nwrap or conditionalise anything — parsing it precisely was tried first and\nread an `import.meta.glob` options object as lagoon options. A warning, not\nan error: dropping an option can be deliberate, but it must not be silent.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"02269b7fe1e23183bf3f95954dca1bfe4e5a3ea4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/02269b7fe1e23183bf3f95954dca1bfe4e5a3ea4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/beefd4fea7b6b3ce1db8ee4c37ea509f402ac94a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/beefd4fea7b6b3ce1db8ee4c37ea509f402ac94a","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKGJlZWZkNGZlYTdiNmIzY2UxZGI4ZWU0YzM3ZWE1MDlmNDAyYWM5NGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/063d494e48c916a0c9690ceb3ccaf170526b6320","sha":"063d494e48c916a0c9690ceb3ccaf170526b6320","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/063d494e48c916a0c9690ceb3ccaf170526b6320"}],"sha":"beefd4fea7b6b3ce1db8ee4c37ea509f402ac94a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/beefd4fea7b6b3ce1db8ee4c37ea509f402ac94a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/063d494e48c916a0c9690ceb3ccaf170526b6320/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:21:47Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:21:47Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"message":"feat: the crosshair scopes the island it picks\n\nPointing at an island with ⌖ selected it inside the LENS and left the view\nshowing the whole region — so the one gesture that literally means \"this\none\" was the only way of choosing an island that did not focus it, while a\nrow in the Islands list did.\n\nThe lens is a read-only observer of the page and should stay one, so it now\njust SAYS what was chosen: `onIslandPicked(fn)` fires on the crosshair''s own\npointerdown, and the gallery scopes on it. Deliberately not fired for the\nalt-click inspect beside it — a shortcut for looking at something must not\nsilently narrow the whole view.\n\nOptional on the lens interface: a lens that only observes is still a valid\nlens, and the dock simply does not scope on a pick when it is absent.\n\ndemo-app''s entry needed it by hand, because that entry is EJECTED — the same\nreason it was missing `evidence` earlier. The scaffold passes it for every\nproject generated from here on.\n\nVerified through the tunnel on the element mount path: crosshair on, a\npointerdown over the member-results island, and the view scopes to\n`x-member-results` with the chip and the address following.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4c5d9db0867741524e876d9423b20452d0201879","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/4c5d9db0867741524e876d9423b20452d0201879"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/063d494e48c916a0c9690ceb3ccaf170526b6320","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/063d494e48c916a0c9690ceb3ccaf170526b6320","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKDA2M2Q0OTRlNDhjOTE2YTBjOTY5MGNlYjNjY2FmMTcwNTI2YjYzMjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/1090ac3d7158639ff59d918773f6cf60791041af","sha":"1090ac3d7158639ff59d918773f6cf60791041af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/1090ac3d7158639ff59d918773f6cf60791041af"}],"sha":"063d494e48c916a0c9690ceb3ccaf170526b6320","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/063d494e48c916a0c9690ceb3ccaf170526b6320"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/1090ac3d7158639ff59d918773f6cf60791041af/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T11:49:11Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T11:49:11Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"message":"fix: the scope chip lived inside the panel, and its CSS inside a media query\n\nTwo faults, and the second is why the first was not obvious.\n\nIN THE PANEL. The chip was a child of the masthead, so collapsing the dock\ntook it with it — and a scope you cannot see is one you cannot tell you are\nin, which is the complaint it was added for. It is a sibling of the panel\nnow, fixed to the page beside the rail (bottom right, clear of the rail''s\nwidth), so it is on screen whether the panel is open, shut or sliding. On a\nphone the dock is a bottom BAR, so \"beside the rail\" is above it — anchored\nto the bar''s own top edge rather than a guessed height.\n\nAND ITS CSS NEVER APPLIED ON DESKTOP. The rules were inserted above\n`#tide .rail-chip`, which lives INSIDE `@media (max-width: 760px)` — so the\nchip rendered unstyled and statically positioned at any normal width, which\nis exactly how it looked wedged in a corner. Moved to the top level, with a\ndeliberate mobile override after it. Worth remembering when adding to this\nstylesheet: half of it is inside that media block, and an anchor picked by\nname says nothing about which half.\n\nVerified through the tunnel with the panel COLLAPSED: fixed, 56px from the\nright (the 46px rail plus its gap), 12px up, and its × still clears the\nscope without a reload.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f6479be87384ce22cb59bea755353202965d2267","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/f6479be87384ce22cb59bea755353202965d2267"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/1090ac3d7158639ff59d918773f6cf60791041af","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/1090ac3d7158639ff59d918773f6cf60791041af","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKDEwOTBhYzNkNzE1ODYzOWZmNTlkOTE4NzczZjZjZjYwNzkxMDQxYWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/33bc413f70503183da67906d75fad1fd095fc651","sha":"33bc413f70503183da67906d75fad1fd095fc651","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/33bc413f70503183da67906d75fad1fd095fc651"}],"sha":"1090ac3d7158639ff59d918773f6cf60791041af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/1090ac3d7158639ff59d918773f6cf60791041af"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/33bc413f70503183da67906d75fad1fd095fc651/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T08:12:37Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T08:12:37Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"message":"fix: seeding a scenario reached only the react mount path\n\nThe previous fix drove `window.__motuLagoon`, which is installed by the\nREACT mount. On the ELEMENT path the same seam lives on\n<motu-archipelago>, so every call was optional-chained into a no-op: the\nstate was reported, the URL moved, and the screen kept the boot scenario —\nthe same symptom as the bug before it, from a different cause, and only on\na host the fix had not been tried on. peps mounts react, demo-app mounts\nelements; verifying on one proved nothing about the other.\n\nNow resolved exactly as `provideScenario` resolves it — the archipelago\nelement when it carries `provide`, else the window seam — with the same\nfallbacks: `seed` where it exists (it ESTABLISHES where `provide` updates,\nwhich is the distinction the ownership guard draws) else `provide`, and\n`remount()` where it exists else re-inserting the <motu-island> markers,\nwhich is how the element path disposes and mounts afresh.\n\nVerified through the tunnel on the element host: \"no matches\" now renders\n\"0 total · Showing 0 of 0\" instead of the default 15.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7ae9b2887ad7428302e5cdf22ab5c831a7a1be8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/7ae9b2887ad7428302e5cdf22ab5c831a7a1be8b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/33bc413f70503183da67906d75fad1fd095fc651","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/33bc413f70503183da67906d75fad1fd095fc651","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKDMzYmM0MTNmNzA1MDMxODNkYTY3OTA2ZDc1ZmFkMWZkMDk1ZmM2NTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/7620ab663ab81ac6c74e76dcc5802d1a78c630a2","sha":"7620ab663ab81ac6c74e76dcc5802d1a78c630a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/7620ab663ab81ac6c74e76dcc5802d1a78c630a2"}],"sha":"33bc413f70503183da67906d75fad1fd095fc651","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/33bc413f70503183da67906d75fad1fd095fc651"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/7620ab663ab81ac6c74e76dcc5802d1a78c630a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T08:06:52Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T08:06:52Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"message":"fix: a scenario switch changed the address and not the screen; add a closable scope chip\n\nSWITCHING DID NOTHING AFTER THE FIRST ONE. Re-running `mountIsland` per\nscenario looked equivalent to a fresh boot and was not: the second call\ninstalled a new `window.__motuLagoon`, but `getArchipelagoStore` went on\nanswering from the FIRST store, so every switch re-rendered with the boot\nscenario''s seed still in place. The dock lit the row it was told to, the\nURL moved, and the screen did not — worse than the reload it replaced,\nbecause it looked like it had worked.\n\nNow driven through the seam the checks already use: reset the keys any of\nthis island''s scenarios sets (a scenario is a state — what it does not\nmention it must not inherit), seed the new one, then `remount()` so a\nfetch-on-mount island re-runs its effect. That is what `provideScenario`\ndoes, and `data-flow` has always moved between scenarios this way in one\npage; the bug was inventing a second mechanism beside a working one.\n\nReproduced and fixed against the case reported: `pas encore décidé` now\nrenders the entry card, and switching back to `engagé` returns to the\nsummary bar — both without a reload.\n\nA CLOSABLE SCOPE CHIP. The subtitle said \"press it again in Islands to\nleave\", which states the rule and still makes you go find the row —\nand on a phone that row is a scroll away inside the panel, so the way out\nwas effectively off screen. The chip names what the view is narrowed to and\ncarries its own ×, which is what a person reaches for. Closing it restores\nthe region and its flows.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"46be98b253ea0454c0fa440ec351ab3be0077d43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/46be98b253ea0454c0fa440ec351ab3be0077d43"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/7620ab663ab81ac6c74e76dcc5802d1a78c630a2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/7620ab663ab81ac6c74e76dcc5802d1a78c630a2","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKDc2MjBhYjY2M2FiODFhYzZjNzRlNzZkY2M1ODAyZDFhNzhjNjMwYTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/a597fcb3592d237da13ea5aab4b28d308c9db9ad","sha":"a597fcb3592d237da13ea5aab4b28d308c9db9ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/a597fcb3592d237da13ea5aab4b28d308c9db9ad"}],"sha":"7620ab663ab81ac6c74e76dcc5802d1a78c630a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/7620ab663ab81ac6c74e76dcc5802d1a78c630a2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/a597fcb3592d237da13ea5aab4b28d308c9db9ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T07:48:27Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T07:48:27Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"message":"feat: switch island scenarios in place, pick them beside the islands, and let go\n\nFour things, from using it.\n\nNO MORE FULL RELOAD PER SCENARIO. `openScenario` navigated, which was\ndefensible (the address runs the boot path, so the dock cannot reach a state\na URL could not) and miserable: four states of one island meant four reloads\nto compare two renders, which is what the list is FOR. It now re-seeds and\nre-mounts in place, and this is safe rather than lucky — `mountIsland`\nbuilds a synthesised archipelago and `defineArchipelago` does\n`new Store(seed)` per mount, so each switch gets a store seeded with exactly\nthat scenario and nothing left from the last. `provideScenario` has to reset\nowned keys to achieve the same thing; a fresh mount gives it for free. The\nURL still follows via `replaceState` — it must SAY what is showing, it just\nneed not be what causes it.\n\nISLANDS BESIDE THE STATES THEY BELONG TO. Reaching a scenario was: Islands\ntab, pick an island, back to States, pick a scenario. The picker now sits in\nthe same pane as the states it changes; the Islands TAB keeps the inspector\n(props, writes, what it called), which is a different question.\n\nPRESSING THE SCOPED ISLAND LETS GO. Everywhere else in the panel a lit\ncontrol toggles; here the only way back to the region was to pick a region,\nwhich is a different intent wearing the same gesture.\n\nAND THE VIEW SAYS WHEN IT IS SCOPED. The bay read the region name whatever\nwas mounted, so one island alone looked like a region with a suspiciously\nempty page. It now reads the island''s tag, `island only`, its scenario\ncount, and how to leave — in the panel and on the collapsed rail.\n\nThe picker lists the region''s DECLARED islands, not the mounted ones. Built\nfrom `islands()` first, it emptied the moment it was used — scoping unmounts\nthe rest — taking the way back out with it. Declared membership does not\nmove when the view narrows.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"563939c2256e7f2a1073164ae587f0e4fa2deaba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/563939c2256e7f2a1073164ae587f0e4fa2deaba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/a597fcb3592d237da13ea5aab4b28d308c9db9ad","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/a597fcb3592d237da13ea5aab4b28d308c9db9ad","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKGE1OTdmY2IzNTkyZDIzN2RhMTNlYTVhYWI0YjI4ZDMwOGM5ZGI5YWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/f2de1561e94387af025d69b459740a65ffc2efb7","sha":"f2de1561e94387af025d69b459740a65ffc2efb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/f2de1561e94387af025d69b459740a65ffc2efb7"}],"sha":"a597fcb3592d237da13ea5aab4b28d308c9db9ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/a597fcb3592d237da13ea5aab4b28d308c9db9ad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/f2de1561e94387af025d69b459740a65ffc2efb7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T07:30:31Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T07:30:31Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"message":"fix: the dock stopped following a lagoon that navigated\n\n`attach()` subscribed once and gave up — `if (!ctl || stop) return`, with\nthe poll clearing itself the moment it succeeded. When the host FRAMES the\nlagoon the dock is a separate document, so a navigation in the frame\nreplaces the control object and leaves the dock holding a subscription to a\npage that no longer exists: the lagoon was correctly on its new state and\nthe dock went on drawing the old one, with total confidence — the exact\nfailure the comment above it warns about, from the one direction it did not\ncover.\n\nLatent until something made the frame navigate. Opening an island from the\nislands pane is the first control that does, so it arrived with it: on the\npublished host the click DID move the lagoon (`?target=island:…`, island\nset in `current()`) and the panel kept listing the region''s flows.\n\nNow keyed on control IDENTITY rather than a boolean, re-subscribing whenever\nthe object changes, and the poll runs for the life of the page — the lagoon\nboots asynchronously (the original reason for it) and can also be replaced\nat any later moment, which a `tries` cap could not see.\n\nVerified through the tunnel: Islands → member-results → States lists\n\"Default mount, no criteria, email filter, no matches, the backend fails\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1fd0a9d55fb7c79e8fdf7f3d96ff50901690a7bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/1fd0a9d55fb7c79e8fdf7f3d96ff50901690a7bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/f2de1561e94387af025d69b459740a65ffc2efb7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/f2de1561e94387af025d69b459740a65ffc2efb7","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKGYyZGUxNTYxZTk0Mzg3YWYwMjVkNjliNDU5NzQwYTY1ZmZjMmVmYjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/b567356c876754f266deffe18c83206e75c179b5","sha":"b567356c876754f266deffe18c83206e75c179b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/b567356c876754f266deffe18c83206e75c179b5"}],"sha":"f2de1561e94387af025d69b459740a65ffc2efb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/f2de1561e94387af025d69b459740a65ffc2efb7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/b567356c876754f266deffe18c83206e75c179b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T07:20:03Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T07:20:03Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"message":"fix: an island''s scenarios were listed on a screen nothing could reach\n\nThe states list shows an island''s scenarios only on an ISLAND target, and\nnothing in the dock could open one — the islands pane INSPECTED what a\nregion had mounted (props, writes, emits, calls) with no click handler at\nall. So the only way in was typing `?target=island:<tag>` by hand, and\nopening the dock on a region showed that region''s flows with no sign that\nscenarios existed. Two halves of a feature, neither able to finish.\n\nThe island row is now a button: clicking it opens that island alone, and\nits scenarios appear under States. Clicking a region afterwards clears the\ntarget (`onStation` already rewrote the address for exactly this), so it is\nnot a one-way door.\n\nFound by a screenshot of the dock open on a region, asking where the\nscenarios were supposed to be. They were nowhere: the previous commit made\nthem appear once you were on an island, which is a state the UI had no path\nto.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3eee785ac578fde4f3c467d13710843e6d459c59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/3eee785ac578fde4f3c467d13710843e6d459c59"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/b567356c876754f266deffe18c83206e75c179b5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/b567356c876754f266deffe18c83206e75c179b5","node_id":"C_kwDOT8U1JNoAKGI1NjczNTZjODc2NzU0ZjI2NmRlZmZlMThjODMyMDZlNzVjMTc5YjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics/motu/commit/dc8d57be4ae439eb229a5ba3d6ea269acb822cf1","sha":"dc8d57be4ae439eb229a5ba3d6ea269acb822cf1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/dc8d57be4ae439eb229a5ba3d6ea269acb822cf1"}],"sha":"b567356c876754f266deffe18c83206e75c179b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/b567356c876754f266deffe18c83206e75c179b5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/commits/dc8d57be4ae439eb229a5ba3d6ea269acb822cf1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T07:03:20Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T07:03:20Z","email":"brice.bulgarelli@gmail.com","name":"Scorbutics"},"message":"fix: the demo-app lagoon could not open its own declared states\n\n`motu lagoon states` printed four addresses for `x-member-results`, and\nopening any of them on the published lagoon refused: \"no scenario … in\nx-member-results''s evidence — declares none\". The catalogue\n(`__motuLagoonStates`) was empty because nothing ever handed the scenarios\nto the entry, so every state this app has written down existed for the\nnode-side checks and nowhere a browser could reach.\n\nTwo causes, both from age rather than a bug in the feature:\n\n- `src/fixtures.ts` is HAND-WRITTEN here (the scaffolded barrel globs\n  `*.evidence.ts`, a layout this app predates) and exported only\n  `ALL_FIXTURES` / `ALL_ROLES`.\n- `roots/lagoon/src/main.tsx` is EJECTED — the project owns it and motu\n  will not regenerate it — so `evidence:` never appeared when the scaffold\n  gained it.\n\nWhich makes this the failure motu''s own rule exists to catch: the framework\nadvertised an address its in-tree consumer could not open, and only an\nadopting project in another repository was exercising it. Republished; the\nscenario now resolves and applies (the email filter narrows the table to\none row).\n\nRepublishing an already-published lagoon is what any project needs for\nscenario addresses to work on it — the artifact carries the catalogue.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bca6e92bb5fc1eb7c589eb7a3f966e55229dc61b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/trees/bca6e92bb5fc1eb7c589eb7a3f966e55229dc61b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scorbutics/motu/git/commits/dc8d57be4ae439eb229a5ba3d6ea269acb822cf1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5864483?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Scorbutics","id":5864483,"login":"Scorbutics","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjQ0ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scorbutics/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.g