ved_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tararir4/mxm-tools/commit/621657c1c755eaa9e0b4c7c56e0e963dc061c27c","node_id":"C_kwDOT8dE3toAKDYyMTY1N2MxYzc1NWVhYTllMGI0YzdjNTZlMGU5NjNkYzA2MWMyN2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tararir4/mxm-tools/commit/236484ef30d2f7e4f0e0d75a4d1a540d52a0a444","sha":"236484ef30d2f7e4f0e0d75a4d1a540d52a0a444","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tararir4/mxm-tools/commits/236484ef30d2f7e4f0e0d75a4d1a540d52a0a444"}],"sha":"621657c1c755eaa9e0b4c7c56e0e963dc061c27c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tararir4/mxm-tools/commits/621657c1c755eaa9e0b4c7c56e0e963dc061c27c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/316633917?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tararir4","id":316633917,"login":"Tararir4","node_id":"U_kgDOEt9zPQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tararir4/mxm-tools/commits/236484ef30d2f7e4f0e0d75a4d1a540d52a0a444/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T22:08:43Z","email":"316633917+Tararir4@users.noreply.github.com","name":"MxM Tools"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T22:08:43Z","email":"316633917+Tararir4@users.noreply.github.com","name":"MxM Tools"},"message":"The icon was the mark it disclaims\n\nA Chrome Web Store audit found one blocking problem and it was not in the\ncode: icons/icon128.png was Musixmatch''s brand mark recoloured — the same two\ninterlocking chevron ribbons, the same rounded square, the same notches. A\nsilhouette comparison against the published brand file put the mean deviation\nat 1.20% of height on the top edge and 0.87% on the bottom. The listing opens\nwith the word \"Unofficial\" and carries a non-affiliation paragraph 8.8% in, but\na disclaimer answers a claim made in words, and this claim was made in a logo.\n\nThe new mark is four audio bars — the transcription the extension is built\naround. It keeps the green and the black rounded square, which were never\nMusixmatch''s. The negative space is now one opaque colour: the old artwork had\na transparency checkerboard baked into it as opaque pixels, visible as a\nrendering bug on the 440x280 tile. tools/make-icons.mjs generates all four\nsizes, so the artwork no longer lives only inside a PNG.\n\nEverything downstream regenerates from that one file, so the five screenshots\nand both promo tiles are rebuilt. tools/store-assets.mjs had to be corrected\nfirst: the stale copy was rendered INTO screenshot 1, which makes it outdated\nmetadata in an uploaded image rather than a caption anyone could fix later.\n\nThe rest is documentation catching up with the product. Verified in code\nbefore writing: ORDER holds 23 buttons, not 21; GROUPS has three clusters, not\nfour, and btn-defs.js says in its own comment that the last contributor is not\none; three Typeforms ship, not two.\n\nTwo corrections matter more than the counts. The description claimed a closed\nlist of outbound destinations that was wrong in both directions — it omitted\nthe feedback form the same file declares as reaching the developer, and the\nGoogle/Spotify/Apple/Amazon quick links that carry the song title in a URL.\nAnd the single purpose asserted that every feature acts on the open task and\nthat the extension does nothing on any other page, both falsifiable from the\nmanifest in a minute: it runs on Diffchecker, on Typeform and on the mission\nlists. The replacement is scoped to the site and covers the launcher button\nthat no lyrics-curation sentence reached.\n\nThe privacy policy gains what it was missing rather than what it got wrong:\nthe per-task working record kept on the device (the Store requires disclosing\nlocal-only data), the search and streaming row, and the launcher. Two entries\nmove toward the truth in the extension''s favour — the YouTube search is sent\nwith credentials omitted, which the old text over-declared — and one against\nit: on the report and contributor-message paths nobody picks the Diffchecker\nexpiration, because the extension confirms the dialog with the default, which\nis Never.\n\nThe privacy-policy URL turns out not to have been a blocker at all. Three\nauditors fetched it independently; it resolves publicly, without a login, and\nserves this repository''s own docs/PRIVACY.md. The PENDIENTE note describing it\nas an unsubmittable placeholder was stale and is now a recorded decision.\n\nNo shipped JavaScript changed. 127/127 suites, lint and typecheck green.","tree":{"sha":"08402c19667bf8789f6b5eb64e8bdd145a69440b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tararir4/mxm-tools/git/trees/08402c19667bf8789f6b5eb64e8bdd145a69440b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tararir4/mxm-tools/git/commits/236484ef30d2f7e4f0e0d75a4d1a540d52a0a444","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/316633917?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tararir4","id":316633917,"login":"Tararir4","node_id":"U_kgDOEt9zPQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tararir4/mxm-tools/commit/236484ef30d2f7e4f0e0d75a4d1a540d52a0a444","node_id":"C_kwDOT8dE3toAKDIzNjQ4NGVmMzBkMmY3ZTRmMGUwZDc1YTRkMWE1NDBkNTJhMGE0NDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tararir4/mxm-tools/commit/04c1d0e3ef11aaad7a71851e40c1c4d8dc2377ff","sha":"04c1d0e3ef11aaad7a71851e40c1c4d8dc2377ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tararir4/mxm-tools/commits/04c1d0e3ef11aaad7a71851e40c1c4d8dc2377ff"}],"sha":"236484ef30d2f7e4f0e0d75a4d1a540d52a0a444","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tararir4/mxm-tools/commits/236484ef30d2f7e4f0e0d75a4d1a540d52a0a444"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/316633917?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tararir4","id":316633917,"login":"Tararir4","node_id":"U_kgDOEt9zPQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tararir4/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api